s adopted. Exit 2 -- deposit as a NEW run-id, e.g. 2026-09-04-re5-repaired -- is refused because it keeps append-only intact by adding to the fold a run that was never taken, which stops the run-era ledger being a record of runs. Exit 3 -- a :row/supersedes field -- is refused because it changes the seam file and the append API, and makes every historical verdict provisional in a way no reader of an old row can see.", :not-claimed "This entry governs REPAIRS of deposited runs. It says nothing about whether a check's semantics may change (that is :tensions-cashed-reading, and it changed one), and nothing about runs not yet deposited, which deposit normally under whatever the check now reads.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/RE-repair-receipts/README.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/RE-repair-receipts/flip-readiness-2026-09-04-010-accepted.md; C511-repair-or-elaborate.md:499-521; holes/labs/wm-contract/run_era_ledger.bb:241-243; holes/labs/wm-contract/flip_readiness_check.bb:743-765 (--as-of composes with neither --deposit nor --emit)", :reversal "re-record the choice: replace this entry's :adoption with the exit taken instead, and either deposit the repaired runs under new run-ids (C511's exit 2) or add :row/supersedes to run-era-ledger.edn's schema and its append API (exit 3). Nothing here forecloses either -- no row was written, no schema field was added, and the receipts under RE-repair-receipts/ are read by no check, so reversing costs deleting or relabelling a directory.", :adoption {:at "2026-09-05", :by :claude-wm-edge, :consequence "holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/RE-repair-receipts/ holds the convention (README.md) and the precedent instance. The :incomplete on runs taken before a check's capture existed is therefore permanent by design, and that is the honest reading of what those runs recorded.", :decision "A demonstrated retroactive derivation for an ALREADY-DEPOSITED run lands as a committed RECEIPT beside the run-era ledger and never as a row mutation, a new run-id, or a :row/supersedes field. The deposited row stands; the receipt is the accounting beside it, and a reader joins the two by hand.", :grounds :measurement, :under "Joe's autonomy ruling, 2026-09-05, as above. :adopted-by :machine, not a Joe ruling."}, :status :adopted-by-machine, :at "2026-09-05", :observed :repair-has-nowhere-to-land, :by [:claude-wm-edge], :row :AD1}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHAT DOES A `Receipt` HOLD, AND THEREFORE WHAT CAN F2 STATE? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:486 asks each selected pattern's receipt to carry three things -- the tension clause it acknowledges (IF/HOWEVER overlap), the retrieval route, and an as-of. `structure Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242) carries `citesTextOrEdges : Prop` and `scoreAlone : Prop` and none of the three, which is why `ConformantFind.f2Receipted` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:25-26) states receipt PRESENCE only. The RECORD is the other end and it is not empty: 96 receipts over 34 rounds in 6 scenarios (futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn at futon3 7c653bb), each with `:if`, `:however`, `:route`, `:state-fields` and a `:warrant` of `:file`, `:if-lines`, `:if-text`, `:however-lines`, `:however-text`. THE MEASUREMENT THAT ORDERS THE ARMS BELOW is that the blindness is in the CARRIER and not in F2's phrasing: a finder whose every receipt names a different pattern and one whose receipts name their own are EQUAL after erasure to today's `FindResult` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:186), so no predicate whatever on that carrier separates them. This entry is HALF of `:find-sorry`'s sixth arm; the other half, which of two readings F4 is, is still unregistered.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}],