ading, which is a separate and still unregistered question, and nothing about what should be done with the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264. It does not claim the five arms are exhaustive. It takes no position on the pin-vs-live divergence C559 recorded: the Lean transcription is at the pinned 18-pattern era while the live library carries 24, which belongs to C500 s3's fixture-pin defect.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A RECORD THAT COULD FILL THE FIELDS. Two of F2's three asks are unavailable as the record stands -- the as-of is per fixture and the route takes one value across all 96 receipts -- so today a data-carrying `Receipt` would be discriminating on the CLAUSE alone. A record with more than one retrieval route, or with a per-receipt as-of, would make the other two fields do work and would change what :carry-the-warrant-as-data buys. The other thing that would move it is a second consumer: the mechanical cost is one site outside the pricing modules TODAY, and it is that small only because `find` has no callers at all (the inertness census, :find-sorry :question).", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C562-F11-receipt-carrier.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/07-receipt-carrier.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/06-dispatch.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C561-F11-find-discharge-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C559-F11-f2-falsifier-reconciliation.md", :question "WHAT DOES A `Receipt` HOLD, AND THEREFORE WHAT CAN F2 STATE? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:486 asks each selected pattern's receipt to carry three things -- the tension clause it acknowledges (IF/HOWEVER overlap), the retrieval route, and an as-of. `structure Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242) carries `citesTextOrEdges : Prop` and `scoreAlone : Prop` and none of the three, which is why `ConformantFind.f2Receipted` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:25-26) states receipt PRESENCE only. The RECORD is the other end and it is not empty: 96 receipts over 34 rounds in 6 scenarios (futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn at futon3 7c653bb), each with `:if`, `:however`, `:route`, `:state-fields` and a `:warrant` of `:file`, `:if-lines`, `:if-text`, `:however-lines`, `:however-text`. THE MEASUREMENT THAT ORDERS THE ARMS BELOW is that the blindness is in the CARRIER and not in F2's phrasing: a finder whose every receipt names a different pattern and one whose receipts name their own are EQUAL after erasure to today's `FindResult` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:186), so no predicate whatever on that carrier separates them. This entry is HALF of `:find-sorry`'s sixth arm; the other half, which of two readings F4 is, is still unregistered.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-09.md Item 20a", :decision "Content-F2 against the applied (Item 18a/C590) data carrier: F2 states acknowledged clause, route and as-of CONTENT, not presence; the expectation remains an independently supplied parameter (DualContentF2), never the identity. Presence-only refuted by the choice-evidence experiment (futon3 704762a: presence preserved a planted clause-attribution fault; content checks rejected it).", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :row :F11, :arms [{:arm :leave-it-presence-only, :buys "NOTHING HAS TO MOVE, and unlike the sibling questions that is the whole of it: no edit to Holes.lean, so no C176 contract regeneration, no transcription, and no construction site touched.", :costs "F2 CANNOT SEE WHO A RECEIPT IS FOR, and this is measured twice over. `findSnatchMisattributingConformant` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:26) shows a finder that receipts every selected pattern satisfies F1-F3 as stated, F3 included, because `Receipt.nonSelfCertifying` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:244-245) reads two propositions and neither is about attribution. The stronger form is `findRErasuresAreEqual` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:186): the faithful and the misattributing finder are EQUAL after erasure, so the verdict cannot differ for ANY predicate on today's `FindResult`, not merely for this one. And the receipt that presence-F2 accepts names `consultTheRemedyBeforeExiting`, which is g1Snatcher's DECLARED ZERO-MASS pattern in the record (futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn, first scenario's `:f4`) -- the one pattern that scenario's F4 says the finder must not return.", :run-by "F11 slice 4 (C562); mathlib4 3c36c8e07e (codex-1) + 0a92815401 (review)", :what-it-is "Do nothing. `Receipt` keeps its two propositions and F2 keeps stating that a selected pattern HAS a receipt."} {:arm :add-the-three-as-propositions, :buys "NOTHING THAT WAS MEASURED. `assertionFieldsDoNotFixAttribution` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:87) proves all three can be true on a receipt whose owner is the wrong pattern. A `Prop` field says that something is the case without carrying WHICH, so the arm adds three fields and no discrimination. THE ARMS ARE NOT ORDERED BY HOW MUCH THEY ADD TO THE STRUCTURE but by whether what they add is DATA a law can compare against the tension -- written down before the result was seen, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/06-dispatch.edn.", :costs "THE FULL PRICE OF AN AMENDMENT FOR NONE OF THE BENEFIT: it edits Holes.lean, so it takes the C176 regeneration (the contract authority is `git log -1 -- Holes.lean`, mathlib4/DarkTower/Contract/Emit.lean:52-62), and it breaks every construction site, and F2 is exactly as blind afterwards.", :run-by "F11 slice 4 (C562); mathlib4 3c36c8e07e", :what-it-is "Add F2's three requirements to `Receipt` as `Prop` fields, matching the two that are already there: `acknowledgesClause`, `hasRoute`, `hasAsOf` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:73)."} {:arm :carry-the-warrant-as-data, :buys "IT DISCRIMINATES, AND IT IS INHABITED BY A FINDER AND NOT ONLY BY A HAND-BUILT RECEIPT. `findRFaithfulContentF2` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:222) holds and `findRMisattributingFailsContentF2` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:230) fails, the refutation witnessed at `askForSurplusNotSurrender`, which g1Snatcher's recorded row selects (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:628-630), over the full recorded 18-pattern repository (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:35-38) and not a degenerate one.", :costs "FOUR, AND THE FIRST IS BIGGER THAN THE ARM'S NAME. (i) IT IS A CHANGE TO `find`'s RETURN TYPE, not only to `Receipt`: `FindResult.receipts` is typed `P -> Option Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:247-250), so this arm moves the type of the declaration the row is trying to discharge. (ii) MECHANICALLY IT IS SMALL: 7 construction sites, exactly ONE of them outside the modules built to price this question -- `findStructuredReceipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:66-68), reused at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:107. Recomputed by holes/labs/wm-contract/f11_receipt_carrier_check.bb, which excludes mathlib4/DarkTower/APMCycleMachine.lean:87 (a `Receipt` of its own) and does not count mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1209, where `Receipt` is a bound type parameter of `Handoff` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1201). (iii) THE TRANSCRIPTION IS THE REAL COST: 96 warrants, none of them in Lean today. `FindSnatchRowLit` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:354-360) carries scenario, round, selected, receipted, nonSelfCertifying, absence -- warrant, route and as-of NOT FOUND. (iv) It edits Holes.lean, so C176 regeneration and the hole-registry literal apply as they do for the sibling arm.", :run-by "F11 slice 4 (C562); mathlib4 0a92815401", :what-it-is "Carry the clause, the route and the as-of as DATA rather than propositions -- `RelationalReceipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:96) -- and state F2 as agreement between what the finder returns and what the tension supplies (`ContentF2`, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:153).", :what-the-record-could-not-fill "TWO OF THE THREE THINGS F2 ASKS FOR ARE NOT AVAILABLE AS THE RECORD STANDS. The as-of is not per receipt: futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn carries ONE `:as-of` for the fixture and 0 of the 96 receipts carry one. The route would not discriminate: all 96 record `:route :structured-antecedent`, a single value, so a route field would be faithful and separate nothing on this record; all 96 also carry `:state-fields :not-instrumented`. And C559 bears on WHICH warrant fields to carry: the 96 receipts already fail to reproduce in `:if-lines`/`:however-lines` ALONE, with no `:if-text` or `:however-text` differing, because library edits shifted lines -- an arm that transcribed the LINE NUMBERS would import that fragility, and the clause TEXTS did not drift."} {:arm :state-content-f2-against-the-row-carrier, :buys :nothing-this-arm-is-not-available, :costs "IT IS NOT AVAILABLE, AND THAT IS THE MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN A COST: `FindReceiptRow` carries scenario, repository, selected, receipted, nonSelfCertifying, zeroMass and absence, and no warrant, route or as-of column -- so there is nothing on that carrier for a content-F2 to compare. The row carrier can say WHICH patterns were receipted, which is presence again at the row grain.", :run-by "F11 slice 4 (C562); refuted by reading the declaration", :what-it-is "Leave `Receipt` alone and state a content-F2 against `FindReceiptRow` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:252-259), the carrier the four recorded F1-F4 predicates already speak about."} {:arm :leave-it-to-the-checker, :buys "THE DISCRIMINATION EXISTS AND IS RUN TODAY, at no Lean cost and with no contract movement: C559 re-measured it at futon3 7c653bb over 24 snatch patterns with 0 drift mismatches, exit 0, and the report byte-identical over two runs. This is also the arm that already absorbed the C61 amendment, whose antecedent slice 1 discharged.", :costs "THE LEAN LAW THEN SAYS LESS THAN THE PAPER'S F2 AND IS KNOWN TO, which is a documentation obligation rather than a defect only while someone records it -- this entry is that record. A NEW implementation gets no content check in Lean: everything in the `:leave-it-presence-only` cost applies to any finder that is not the recorded replay. And the two representations have to be kept reconciled, which is the maintenance C61 named and C559 discharged once.", :run-by "F11 slice 4 (C562), reading the futon3 check that slice 1 reconciled", :what-it-is "Accept that Lean states presence and let the CONTENT of F2 be checked where the warrants actually live -- futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj, whose `find` evaluates the carried authored antecedent (futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:47-71) and whose `require-zero-drift!` (futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:148-155) refuses the run when any antecedent mismatches."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHAT CARRIES F3's CITATION -- AND IS IT A THIRD FIELD OR THE ONE ALREADY PRICED? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:487 asks a receipt to cite the SELECTED PATTERN'S OWN TEXT or authored edges. `structure Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242) carries `citesTextOrEdges : Prop` and `scoreAlone : Prop` and no field naming WHICH text, and slice 7 measured that this is a fact about the carrier and not about F3's phrasing: a finder citing each selected pattern's own text and one citing another recorded pattern's are EQUAL after erasure to today's `FindResult` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11NonSelfCertifying.lean:351), so no predicate on that carrier separates them. THE SLICE WAS DISPATCHED ON THE PREMISE THAT THE CITATION IS A THIRD FIELD, AND THAT PREMISE WAS REFUTED (premise written down before the work at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/15-dispatch.edn, futon2 da92b8d2): `ConformantAmendedFind.f2Content` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:40-41), the F2 conjunct of the sixth arm slice 6 priced, is CHARACTER-FOR-CHARACTER the citation predicate at slice 6's own instantiation, and `amendedFaithful_citesSelected` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:21-22) discharges the citation reading by that conjunct verbatim. THE CAUSE, WHICH IS THE REVIEW'S ADDITION AND IS WHY THIS IS STILL A QUESTION: slice 4's `ContentF2` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:153-156) carries the expectation `clauseOf : P -> Clause` as a PARAMETER -- review added it there so F2 is stated against an independently given assignment -- and slice 6 dropped the parameter and fixed it to the identity. At the identity the acknowledged clause carries nothing beyond the pattern's own name, which is why the two predicates coincide; with the parameter kept they come apart, and the finder that changes only the acknowledged clause SATISFIES F2 at its own expectation while refuting it at the identity and citing faithfully throughout (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:208-211).", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :find-f3-citation-field], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "WHAT CARRIES F3's CITATION -- AND IS IT A THIRD FIELD OR THE ONE ALREADY PRICED? futon2/holes/problems/P