e "WHAT CARRIES F3's CITATION -- AND IS IT A THIRD FIELD OR THE ONE ALREADY PRICED? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:487 asks a receipt to cite the SELECTED PATTERN'S OWN TEXT or authored edges. `structure Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242) carries `citesTextOrEdges : Prop` and `scoreAlone : Prop` and no field naming WHICH text, and slice 7 measured that this is a fact about the carrier and not about F3's phrasing: a finder citing each selected pattern's own text and one citing another recorded pattern's are EQUAL after erasure to today's `FindResult` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11NonSelfCertifying.lean:351), so no predicate on that carrier separates them. THE SLICE WAS DISPATCHED ON THE PREMISE THAT THE CITATION IS A THIRD FIELD, AND THAT PREMISE WAS REFUTED (premise written down before the work at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/15-dispatch.edn, futon2 da92b8d2): `ConformantAmendedFind.f2Content` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:40-41), the F2 conjunct of the sixth arm slice 6 priced, is CHARACTER-FOR-CHARACTER the citation predicate at slice 6's own instantiation, and `amendedFaithful_citesSelected` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:21-22) discharges the citation reading by that conjunct verbatim. THE CAUSE, WHICH IS THE REVIEW'S ADDITION AND IS WHY THIS IS STILL A QUESTION: slice 4's `ContentF2` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:153-156) carries the expectation `clauseOf : P -> Clause` as a PARAMETER -- review added it there so F2 is stated against an independently given assignment -- and slice 6 dropped the parameter and fixed it to the identity. At the identity the acknowledged clause carries nothing beyond the pattern's own name, which is why the two predicates coincide; with the parameter kept they come apart, and the finder that changes only the acknowledged clause SATISFIES F2 at its own expectation while refuting it at the identity and citing faithfully throughout (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:208-211).", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/find-f3-citation-field", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:arms-not-all-run "2026-09-07, F11 slice 9 (C567): all five arms carry measured :buys and :costs. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. mathlib4 git log -1 still reads 61c4825dc3e373fd1b761b800814bf85f5770b88 on Holes.lean; the sorry at :264 is untouched and the build still reports it. NOTE FOR :find-sorry's SIXTH ARM: this entry does NOT make :amend-the-carrier a three-half question. The refuter came out CONFIRMED, so the citation is not a third field to aggregate; what it is instead is a second reading of the field the sixth arm already prices, and re-pricing that arm in light of this entry is a later slice's.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED. This entry does not say what should carry the citation; it says what each carrier costs. It does not claim the five arms exhaustive. It does not claim the two-field independence is natural: the separating finders differ only in a field constructed for the comparison, which the arm's :costs states. It says nothing about what should be done with the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264, which is `:find-sorry`. It takes no position on the pin-vs-live divergence C559 recorded: every Lean witness here is over the pinned 18-pattern transcription while the live library carries 24, which belongs to C500 s3's fixture-pin defect and is the OTHER obligation slice 8 found unmet and ungated. It does not re-price `:find-sorry`'s sixth arm, and it does not claim the fixture measurements above were re-derived by anyone but the lane.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A RECORD THAT CARRIED THE TENSION'S OWN CLAUSE AS TEXT would make the F2 side non-degenerate and would let the fixture, rather than a constructed finder, say whether the two asks come apart -- it is the one thing that would move both :carry-a-separate-cited-text-field and :restore-the-expectation-parameter-to-f2 off `built, not witnessed`. A record with more than one warrant file per selected pattern would do the same for the citation side. MECHANICALLY what any arm here moves is small and counted site by site by the lane, not estimated: across 157 .lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower/ there are 24 Receipt-field assignment lines, all inside the F11 pricing family (F11Conformance.lean 2, F11ReceiptCarrier.lean 8, F11NonSelfCertifying.lean 8, F11AmendedCarrier.lean 6) and NONE in Holes.lean, F11DischargeArm.lean or F11F4Reading.lean. The four non-F11 files a bare grep for `Receipt` returns are NAME COLLISIONS and not sites: mathlib4/DarkTower/APMCycleMachine.lean:87 declares its own `structure Receipt` in namespace DarkTower.APMCycleMachine with campaignId/manifestHash/fromPhase/toPhase and no field in common; APMCampaignTraceChecker.lean matches only identifiers containing the substring; MemoryArmPreregistration.lean:101 is the word in a docstring; WarMachine/GainChain.lean:135 is a comment. This confirms slice 6's `none outside the F11 family` and records the reason it needed checking. The census is small only because `find` has no callers at all.", :what-the-record-cannot-decide "THE RECORD ANSWERS BOTH ASKS WITH ONE DATUM AND CANNOT SEPARATE THEM. Measured by the lane from futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn at sha256 839897ef8fe44952403700bd237389449ae4735d3da7df8239b1b94dc7ef4dfa (futon3 HEAD cdb5e8a), reading :scenarios -> :round-results -> :find -> :receipts: 96 receipts over 33 receipt-carrying rounds of 34, 11 distinct pattern ids receipted. The warrant's :file is the SELECTED pattern's own file in 96 of 96; :if-text and the receipted pattern id are in BIJECTION, checked both ways, and the pattern id likewise determines :if-lines; there is ONE distinct :route across all 96. On the F2 side there is no text at all: :if is `true` in all 96 (zero information) and :however takes two values (:none 42, true 54). So the record cannot separate `cites the selected pattern's TEXT` from `names the selected PATTERN`, and it cannot supply a non-identity expectation for F2 at all. A COROLLARY for C559's finding: `carry the texts, not the line numbers` is a claim about DRIFT and not about discriminating power, since the pattern id determines the line numbers too.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C567-F11-citation-field.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/15-dispatch.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C565-F11-non-self-certifying.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C566-F11-remainder.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/14-remainder.edn", :question "WHAT CARRIES F3's CITATION -- AND IS IT A THIRD FIELD OR THE ONE ALREADY PRICED? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:487 asks a receipt to cite the SELECTED PATTERN'S OWN TEXT or authored edges. `structure Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242) carries `citesTextOrEdges : Prop` and `scoreAlone : Prop` and no field naming WHICH text, and slice 7 measured that this is a fact about the carrier and not about F3's phrasing: a finder citing each selected pattern's own text and one citing another recorded pattern's are EQUAL after erasure to today's `FindResult` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11NonSelfCertifying.lean:351), so no predicate on that carrier separates them. THE SLICE WAS DISPATCHED ON THE PREMISE THAT THE CITATION IS A THIRD FIELD, AND THAT PREMISE WAS REFUTED (premise written down before the work at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/15-dispatch.edn, futon2 da92b8d2): `ConformantAmendedFind.f2Content` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:40-41), the F2 conjunct of the sixth arm slice 6 priced, is CHARACTER-FOR-CHARACTER the citation predicate at slice 6's own instantiation, and `amendedFaithful_citesSelected` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:21-22) discharges the citation reading by that conjunct verbatim. THE CAUSE, WHICH IS THE REVIEW'S ADDITION AND IS WHY THIS IS STILL A QUESTION: slice 4's `ContentF2` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:153-156) carries the expectation `clauseOf : P -> Clause` as a PARAMETER -- review added it there so F2 is stated against an independently given assignment -- and slice 6 dropped the parameter and fixed it to the identity. At the identity the acknowledged clause carries nothing beyond the pattern's own name, which is why the two predicates coincide; with the parameter kept they come apart, and the finder that changes only the acknowledged clause SATISFIES F2 at its own expectation while refuting it at the identity and citing faithfully throughout (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:208-211).", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-09.md Item 20c", :decision "The citation is the applied carrier's FindCitation data field (pattern text with file/lines/exact bytes, or authored descent), distinct from F2's acknowledged clause; the F3 two-fault matrix showed the checks separate (futon3 704762a).", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :row :F11, :arms [{:arm :leave-f3-as-the-two-propositions, :buys "IT IS WHAT THE FOUR CLOSED find DECLARATIONS WERE PROVED AGAINST, so nothing re-opens: `findF3NonSelfCertifying` and its table are at this carrier, the transcription pins futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn at sha256 839897ef8fe44952403700bd237389449ae4735d3da7df8239b1b94dc7ef4dfa, and the fixture is unchanged at that value (re-verified by the lane this slice; futon3 HEAD cdb5e8a). It also costs no edit site: the census below is 24 Receipt-field assignments and every one is inside the F11 pricing family.", :costs "F3 IS SELF-ASSERTED AT THIS CARRIER AND THAT IS MEASURED, NOT ARGUED. `findAssertingF3` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11NonSelfCertifying.lean:33-42) fills both propositions with True/False, carries no citation, selects a named recorded pattern and satisfies F1-F3, so F3 as carried costs a finder nothing; and `findCErasuresAreEqual` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11NonSelfCertifying.lean:351) proves no predicate on this carrier can separate the citing from the misciting finder. This arm is what leaves slice 8's `:f3-citation-stated-in-lean` unmet (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/14-remainder.edn).", :run-by "F11 slice 9 (C567); mathlib4 99fdfa7800 (codex-2) + ea58aa4249 (review)", :what-it-is "Change nothing: `Receipt` keeps `citesTextOrEdges : Prop` and `scoreAlone : Prop` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242) and `Receipt.nonSelfCertifying` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:244-245) is their conjunction."} {:arm :read-the-already-priced-clause-field-as-the-citation, :buys "IT IS ALREADY PROVED AND ALREADY PRICED, so the sixth arm needs no widening: `amendedFaithful_citesSelected` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:21-22) holds BY `ConformantAmendedFind.f2Content` with no proof of its own, `amendedMisattributing_not_citesSelected` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:26-37) refutes it on the named recorded pattern `askForSurplusNotSurrender` in `findSnatchRepository`, both finders select there (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:42-47), and the pair is separated before erasure and EQUAL after it (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:52-55), which is what makes it a buy over today's carrier rather than a difference. THE RECORD AGREES WITH THIS COLLAPSE: over all 96 receipts of futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn the warrant's `:if-text` and the receipted pattern id are IN BIJECTION, checked both ways by the lane, so on this record a citation typed as TEXT carries exactly what naming the pattern carries.", :costs "IT MAKES ONE FIELD ANSWER TWO ASKS, AND THE TWO COME APART AS SOON AS THE EXPECTATION IS NOT THE IDENTITY. `DualAcknowledgesSelected` IS F2 at `clauseOf = id`, definitionally (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:196-197), and `clauseFailureIsRelativeToTheExpectation` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:208-211) exhibits a finder that satisfies F2 at its own expectation, refutes it at the identity, and cites faithfully -- so under this arm a receipt that acknowledges the wrong tension clause and a receipt that cites the wrong pattern are indistinguishable complaints. It also silently narrows slice 4's F2, whose expectation parameter review had added on purpose.", :run-by "F11 slice 9 (C567); mathlib4 99fdfa7800 -- THIS IS THE CONFIRMED REFUTER", :what-it-is "Take the field the sixth arm already prices -- `AmendedReceipt.acknowledgedClause` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:18-21) at slice 6's instantiation `Clause := SnatchPattern`, `acknowledgedClause := p` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:106-114) -- to BE F3's citation, and add no third field."} {:arm :carry-a-separate-cited-text-field, :buys "THE TWO ASKS BECOME INDEPENDENT, PROVED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS ON THE RECORDED REPOSITORY: changing only the citation separates F3 while both finders satisfy the clause predicate (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:114-117), changing only the clause separates F2 while both cite faithfully (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:149-151), all three finders select the named recorded pattern (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:104-110), and both pairs are EQUAL after erasure to today's carrier (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:223-228).", :costs "THE INDEPENDENCE IS BUILT, NOT WITNESSED -- THE RECORD CANNOT SHOW IT. The separating finders differ only in a field constructed for the comparison (`dualReceipt`, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:88-92), and the record answers both asks with ONE datum: the warrant names the SELECTED pattern's own file in 96 of 96 receipts, its `:if-text` is in bijection with the pattern id, and the fields on the F2 side carry no text at all (`:if` is `true` in all 96, `:however` takes two values). So a two-field carrier is discriminating on this record exactly where a one-field carrier is. Mechanically it also moves `find`'s own return type, since `FindResult.receipts` is typed by `Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:247-250).", :run-by "F11 slice 9 (C567); mathlib4 99fdfa7800 + ea58aa4249", :what-it-is "Give the receipt BOTH data as separate fields -- `DualReceipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:60-62) extends `Receipt` with `acknowledgedClause` and `citedText` -- and state F2 of the first and F3 of the second."} {:arm :restore-the-expectation-parameter-to-f2, :buys "IT NAMES THE DIFFERENCE INSTEAD OF ADDING A FIELD, and the naming is proved to do work: at the identity the two predicates are the same proposition (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:196-197) and away from it they are not (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:208-211). It is the only arm here that explains WHY slice 6's F2 conjunct and F3's citation coincided, rather than adopting or undoing the coincidence.", :costs "IT PUTS THE DISCRIMINATION IN A PARAMETER THE RECORD DOES NOT SUPPLY, which is the shape slice 5 already priced and review already caught once: reading C of F4 takes its designation from outside the finder and is VACUOUS at the empty designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:114-118). Here the missing supply is measured: the record carries no text on the F2 side at all, so there is nothing in futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn from which a non-identity `clauseOf` could be read, and the arm is unwitnessed on the record for the same reason the previous arm's independence is.", :run-by "F11 slice 9 (C567); mathlib4 ea58aa4249 (review)", :what-it-is "Keep one clause field but restore slice 4's parameter: state F2 as `ContentF2 f clauseOf` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:153-156) with the expectation supplied from outside, and let F3 be the same predicate at the identity. `DualContentF2` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11CitationField.lean:189-191) is that shape."} {:arm :leave-it-to-the-checker, :buys "IT IS RUN TODAY AND ITS DATA IS COMPLETE: all 96 receipts carry `:structured-antecedent`, 0 are score-alone, and all 96 carry each of `:file`, `:if-lines`, `:if-text`, `:however-lines`, `:however-text` with the warrant being the selected pattern's own file (lane measurement this slice, and slice 7's independently).", :costs "THERE ARE TWO F3 PREDICATES IN THE CODE AND THEY ARE NOT EQUIVALENT, so `the checker` does not name one thing: find_snatch.clj:167-171 has two conjuncts, find_organise.clj:567-571 has four, and slice 7 proved them inequivalent (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11NonSelfCertifying.lean:134). The record cannot arbitrate, because both are true of all 96 receipts. And it leaves the Lean where slice 8 found it: `:f3-citation-stated-in-lean` unmet.", :run-by "F11 slice 9 (C567), reading slice 7's census of the two code predicates", :what-it-is "Accept that Lean states whichever F3 is convenient and let F3 be decided where it is executed -- futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:167-171, whose two conjuncts are what u46_find_transcribe.bb:113-121 transcribes into the Lean column."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHICH OF THREE READINGS IS F4? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:488 states it as: for a given tension there is at least one pattern in the repository the finder must NOT return (a zero-mass pattern -- T1512Z applied to retrieval); a finder that can return anything for anything is unfalsifiable. THREE formalisations of that one sentence are now in the tree and no two of them are equivalent. READING A, `FindFalsifiable` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:31-32), lets the FINDER nominate the excluded pattern, per input, after the fact. READING B, `FindExcludesRecordedZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:59-62), takes the excluded pattern from the RECORD and quantifies over the recorded repository ALONE. READING C, `FindRespectsZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:26-29), takes a zero-mass DESIGNATION as a parameter and quantifies over every repository, which is what the paper's deontic `must not` says: the designation comes from outside the finder. THE LATTICE, PROVED: C implies B (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:34-42); B does not imply C (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:68-89); A does not imply C at the recorded designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:136-146); C does not imply A even at the RECORDED designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:129-133). So C is strictly stronger than B, and A is INCOMPARABLE with C in both directions. This entry is the second and last half of `:find-sorry`'s sixth arm; the first half is `:find-f2-receipt-carrier`.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :find-f4-reading], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "WHICH OF THREE READINGS IS F4? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:488 states it as: for a given tension there is at least one pattern in the repository the finder must NOT return (a zero-mass pattern -- T1512Z applied to retrieval); a finder that can return anything for anything is unfalsifiable. THREE formalisations of that one sentence are now in the tree and no two of them are equivalent. READING A, `FindFalsifiable` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:31-32), lets the FINDER nominate the excluded pattern, per input, after the fact. READING B, `FindExcludesRecordedZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:59-62), takes the excluded pattern from the RECORD and quantifies over the recorded repository ALONE. READING C, `FindRespectsZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:26-29), takes a zero-mass DESIGNATION as a parameter and quantifies over every repository, which is what the paper's deontic `must not` says: the designation comes from outside the finder. THE LATTICE, PROVED: C implies B (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:34-42); B does not imply C (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:68-89); A does not imply C at the recorded designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:136-146); C does not imply A even at the RECORDED designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:129-133). So C is strictly stronger than B, and A is INCOMPARABLE with C in both directions. This entry is the second and last half of `:find-sorry`'s sixth arm; the first half is `:find-f2-receipt-carrier`.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "WHICH OF THREE READINGS IS F4? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:488 states it as: for a given tension there is at least one pattern in the repository the finder must NOT return (a zero-mass pattern -- T1512Z applied to retrieval); a finder that can return anything for anything is unfalsifiable. THREE formalisations of that one sentence are now in the tree and no two of them are equivalent. READING A, `FindFalsifiable` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:31-32), lets the FINDER nominate the excluded pattern, per input, after the fact. READING B, `FindExcludesRecordedZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:59-62), takes the excluded pattern from the RECORD and quantifies over the recorded repository ALONE. READING C, `FindRespectsZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:26-29), takes a zero-mass DESIGNATION as a parameter and quantifies over every repository, which is what the paper's deontic `must not` says: the designation comes from outside the finder. THE LATTICE, PROVED: C implies B (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:34-42); B does not imply C (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:68-89); A does not imply C at the recorded designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:136-146); C does not imply A even at the RECORDED designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:129-133). So C is strictly stronger than B, and A is INCOMPARABLE with C in both directions. This entry is the second and last half of `:find-sorry`'s sixth arm; the first half is `:find-f2-receipt-carrier`.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/find-f4-reading", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:arms-not-all-run "2026-09-07, F11 slice 5 (C563): all five arms carry measured :buys and :costs. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. Holes.lean is untouched: `find` at :264 is still a sorry and no reading of F4 is a conjunct of `ConformantFind` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:21-28), which the checker asserts. THE DISPATCH PREMISE WAS REFUTED rather than confirmed, and the arm that carries the refutation says so: this is what writing the premise down before the result (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/08-dispatch.edn) was for.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED. This entry does not say which reading F4 is; it says what each costs. It does not claim the three readings are the only ones, nor the five arms exhaustive. It does not claim the A-and-B witness is a natural finder: it branches on an equality test against the recorded pattern set, which the arm's :costs states. It says nothing about F2's receipt carrier, which is `:find-f2-receipt-carrier`, and nothing about what should be done with the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264. It takes no position on the pin-vs-live divergence C559 recorded: the Lean transcription is at the pinned 18-pattern era while the live library carries 24, which belongs to C500 s3's fixture-pin defect.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A RECORD THAT DECLARED MORE THAN ONE ZERO-MASS MEMBER, or that recorded an exclusion for a second reason, would let the fixture speak about the readings instead of about one member per scenario, and would move both the reading-B and reading-C arms. Independently: an A-and-B finder that is NOT defined by an equality test against the recorded pattern set would strengthen the conjunction arm from `jointly satisfiable` to `jointly satisfiable by a finder written without the record`, which is the form that would actually price the conjunction for a new implementation. MECHANICALLY, what a fixed reading would move is small and measured: across the 155 .lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower, `FindFalsifiable` occurs 21 times of which 10 are outside the module built to price this question, `FindExcludesRecordedZeroMass` 18 of which 8 are outside it, and `FindRespectsZeroMass` 10 of which 0 are outside it -- recomputed and COMPARED by holes/labs/wm-contract/f11_f4_reading_check.bb, which fails with :mechanical-cost-changed rather than merely reporting.", :what-the-record-cannot-decide "THE RECORD DISCRIMINATES THE READINGS THROUGH ONE MEMBER PER SCENARIO AND NOTHING ELSE. futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:25-31 declares exactly one zero-mass pattern for each of six scenarios, three distinct values across the six; the F4 leg tests only that member's presence in the repository and absence from the selection (futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:172-177), and an exclusion recorded for any OTHER reason is NOT FOUND in futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:100-114,172-177 or in the scenario F4 fields of futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn. So no recorded row distinguishes reading A from reading B: every recorded exclusion is the declared one.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C563-F11-f4-reading.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/09-f4-reading.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/08-dispatch.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C561-F11-find-discharge-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C562-F11-receipt-carrier.md", :question "WHICH OF THREE READINGS IS F4? futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:488 states it as: for a given tension there is at least one pattern in the repository the finder must NOT return (a zero-mass pattern -- T1512Z applied to retrieval); a finder that can return anything for anything is unfalsifiable. THREE formalisations of that one sentence are now in the tree and no two of them are equivalent. READING A, `FindFalsifiable` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:31-32), lets the FINDER nominate the excluded pattern, per input, after the fact. READING B, `FindExcludesRecordedZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:59-62), takes the excluded pattern from the RECORD and quantifies over the recorded repository ALONE. READING C, `FindRespectsZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:26-29), takes a zero-mass DESIGNATION as a parameter and quantifies over every repository, which is what the paper's deontic `must not` says: the designation comes from outside the finder. THE LATTICE, PROVED: C implies B (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:34-42); B does not imply C (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:68-89); A does not imply C at the recorded designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:136-146); C does not imply A even at the RECORDED designation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:129-133). So C is strictly stronger than B, and A is INCOMPARABLE with C in both directions. This entry is the second and last half of `:find-sorry`'s sixth arm; the first half is `:find-f2-receipt-carrier`.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-09.md Item 20b", :decision "READING C: the zero-mass designation is an externally supplied parameter (the paper's deontic must-not), with the vacuity clause -- an empty applicable designation is reported vacuous and earns no discrimination; B is what C reduces to when the only designation on record is the scenario's own. Joe's addendum: the designation supplier is an institutional role (Ostrom/IAD connection, SESSION-C-institutional-constraints-2026-09-09.md).", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :row :F11, :arms [{:arm :reading-a-forall-over-inputs, :buys "IT IS THE ONLY READING THAT BITES ON INPUTS THE RECORD NEVER SAW, which is what the paper's second sentence asks for -- a finder that can return anything for anything is refuted, and `findIdentity` is refuted by it on the recorded repository (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:174-186). It needs no fixture, so it survives any change to the record.", :costs "IT REFUTES THE RECORD'S OWN REPLAY. `findSnatchReplayNotFalsifiable` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:207-218) refutes reading A of the finder that replays the committed table, on a repository holding only `askForSurplusNotSurrender`, which every recorded scenario selects. And it does not see the record's declared zero-mass member at all: `findAllBut` at g1's declared member satisfies A and returns g4's (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:207-214), so a finder can meet A on every input and still return a pattern the record said in advance it must not.", :run-by "F11 slice 5 (C563); mathlib4 106e1c0c11 (codex-2) + 7060ad361e (review)", :what-it-is "Leave F4 as `FindFalsifiable` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:31-32): on every input with a nonempty repository the finder must exclude SOME repository member, whichever one it likes."} {:arm :reading-b-record-grain, :buys "IT IS THE ONE READING THE RECORD ACTUALLY CHECKS, and the correspondence is exact rather than approximate: the executable F4 leg tests precisely repository membership and omission of the declared member (futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:172-177), throwing at futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:106 when a declared zero-mass pattern is selected. The replay satisfies it (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:176-180).", :costs "IT SAYS NOTHING OFF THE RECORDED REPOSITORY, and that is a proved gap rather than a stylistic one: `findReplayRecordedElseIdentity` satisfies B and returns g1's declared zero-mass member on a repository whose only member IS that pattern (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:68-89), a witness that selects there (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:92-104). B is C with the repository quantifier removed, which is what the checker at holes/labs/wm-contract/f11_f4_reading_check.bb asserts and what its second plant moves.", :run-by "F11 slice 5 (C563); mathlib4 106e1c0c11", :what-it-is "Read F4 as `FindExcludesRecordedZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:59-62): the patterns futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj:25-31 declares zero-mass in advance are in the recorded repository and out of the selection."} {:arm :reading-c-external-designation, :buys "IT IS WHAT THE SENTENCE SAYS. The paper's `must not` is deontic, so the designation is not the finder's to choose; C is the only one of the three in which it is not. It is strictly stronger than B (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:34-42) and the recorded replay satisfies it on EVERY repository, not only the recorded one (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:44-49), which is a strengthening of the replay's recorded reading-B theorem.", :costs "IT NEEDS A DESIGNATION THE RECORD SUPPLIES ONLY AT SIX POINTS, and it is silent wherever the designation is. `findSnatchZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:342-348) gives exactly one pattern for each of six scenarios, three distinct values; for any tension outside those six the designation is undefined and C asks nothing. At the EMPTY designation C is vacuous and holds of `findIdentity` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:114-118), so C alone does not rule out the finder that returns everything -- C and A are incomparable, refuted in both directions (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:129-133 and :135-146).", :run-by "F11 slice 5 (C563); mathlib4 106e1c0c11", :what-it-is "Read F4 as `FindRespectsZeroMass` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:26-29), parameterised by a designation zm : State -> Set P supplied from outside the finder, and quantified over every repository. Reading B is C at the recorded designation with the quantifier dropped."} {:arm :require-both-a-and-b, :buys "IT IS SATISFIABLE WITHOUT GIVING UP THE RECORD, AND THAT REFUTES THE PREMISE THIS SLICE WAS DISPATCHED ON. The dispatch record (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/08-dispatch.edn, written before the result) expected A and B to pull in opposite directions, so that requiring both would cost the record's own selections. `findReplayRecordedElseRefuse` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:220-225) is F1-F3 conformant, satisfies A and B, and its selection on the recorded repository IS the recorded scenario-grain selection (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:307-312, review addition; the dispatched form stated equality with REPLAY, one step short of the record). Its selection there is nonempty (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:227-231).", :costs "THE CONJUNCTION IS PAID OFF THE RECORD, BY REFUSING. `findReplayRecordedElseRefuse` meets A on every repository whose pattern set is not the recorded one by returning nothing, so the conjunction does not cost recorded behaviour -- it costs behaviour everywhere else. AND THE WITNESS IS BUILT FROM A TEST AGAINST THE RECORD: the finder branches on `repo.patterns = findSnatchRepository.patterns`, so what is established is that A and B are jointly satisfiable while reproducing the record, NOT that a finder written without the record in hand can do it. The conjunction also inherits reading A's cost of refuting the plain replay (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:163-168).", :run-by "F11 slice 5 (C563); mathlib4 106e1c0c11 + 7060ad361e", :what-it-is "Take F4 as the conjunction: a conformant finder must satisfy the forall-over-inputs reading AND exclude the recorded declared member."} {:arm :leave-it-to-the-checker, :buys "IT IS RUN TODAY AND IT IS UNAMBIGUOUS: the executable leg is reading B and nothing else, so there is no reading to choose. C559 re-measured the check at futon3 7c653bb over 24 snatch patterns, exit 0, report byte-identical over two runs.", :costs "THE AMBIGUITY DOES NOT GO AWAY, IT MOVES TO WHOEVER READS THE LEAN. Three readings remain in the tree with no ruling between them, and the two the Lean states disagree in both directions (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:207-218 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:207-214). The checker's coverage is also the record's: it tests one declared member per scenario, so it discriminates the readings only through that member (see :what-the-record-cannot-decide).", :run-by "F11 slice 5 (C563), reading the futon3 F4 leg", :what-it-is "Accept that Lean states whichever reading is convenient and let F4 be decided where the zero-mass designation actually lives -- futon3:checks/find_snatch.clj, whose F4 leg reads the declared member from the table at :25-31, refuses the run at :106 when a declared member is selected, and validates membership plus omission at :172-177."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264? The declaration is a total function `Tension State -> Repository P -> FindResult P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:263 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded F1-F4 instances `do not select one canonical implementation`. The sorry is INERT, recomputed at slice 3 rather than asserted: over the 153 Lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower there is exactly ONE code occurrence of the token `find`, the declaration itself, plus 25 prose occurrences in doc-comments and module headers and one string literal in the hole registry (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:8020, `mkRefused \"find\"`) -- holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/05-discharge-arm.edn. So discharging it changes no proof obligation, and what the arms below differ over is what the declaration SAYS afterwards. EVERY EXISTENCE AND EVERY NON-UNIQUENESS RESULT BELOW IS STATED SEPARATELY UNDER EACH OF THE TWO READINGS OF F4, so that pricing the arms does not tacitly decide which reading F4 is.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :find-sorry], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264? The declaration is a total function `Tension State -> Repository P -> FindResult P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:263 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded F1-F4 instances `do not select one canonical implementation`. The sorry is INERT, recomputed at slice 3 rather than asserted: over the 153 Lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower there is exactly ONE code occurrence of the token `find`, the declaration itself, plus 25 prose occurrences in doc-comments and module headers and one string literal in the hole registry (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:8020, `mkRefused \"find\"`) -- holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/05-discharge-arm.edn. So discharging it changes no proof obligation, and what the arms below differ over is what the declaration SAYS afterwards. EVERY EXISTENCE AND EVERY NON-UNIQUENESS RESULT BELOW IS STATED SEPARATELY UNDER EACH OF THE TWO READINGS OF F4, so that pricing the arms does not tacitly decide which reading F4 is.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264? The declaration is a total function `Tension State -> Repository P -> FindResult P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:263 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded F1-F4 instances `do not select one canonical implementation`. The sorry is INERT, recomputed at slice 3 rather than asserted: over the 153 Lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower there is exactly ONE code occurrence of the token `find`, the declaration itself, plus 25 prose occurrences in doc-comments and module headers and one string literal in the hole registry (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:8020, `mkRefused \"find\"`) -- holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/05-discharge-arm.edn. So discharging it changes no proof obligation, and what the arms below differ over is what the declaration SAYS afterwards. EVERY EXISTENCE AND EVERY NON-UNIQUENESS RESULT BELOW IS STATED SEPARATELY UNDER EACH OF THE TWO READINGS OF F4, so that pricing the arms does not tacitly decide which reading F4 is.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/find-sorry", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:arms-not-all-run "2026-09-07, F11 slice 3 (C561): the FIVE arms that are this entry's carry measured :buys and :costs. The sixth, :amend-the-carrier, was NOT RUN and read :unmeasured. AMENDED 2026-09-07 by F11 slice 4: the receipt-carrier half became `:find-f2-receipt-carrier`. AMENDED AGAIN 2026-09-07 by F11 slice 5: the F4-reading half became `:find-f4-reading`. AMENDED AGAIN 2026-09-07 by F11 slice 6 (C564): ALL SIX ARMS NOW CARRY MEASURED :buys AND :costs -- the sixth was priced as ONE THING against the joint carrier at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean, checked by holes/labs/wm-contract/f11_amended_carrier_check.bb with ten Lean plants and six checker plants. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. mathlib4 git log -1 still reads 61c4825dc3 on Holes.lean; the sorry at :264 is untouched and the build still reports it.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED. This entry does not say the sorry should be discharged, amended, sealed or left; it says what each costs. The sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264 is untouched by the slice that registered it. It says nothing about which reading of F4 is correct -- both existence and both non-uniqueness results are stated separately under each reading precisely so that this entry does not decide it -- and nothing about F2's receipt carrier. It does not claim the six arms are exhaustive: the sixth is unpriced. It takes no position on the pin-vs-live divergence C559 recorded (the Lean transcription is at the pinned 18-pattern era and the live library carries 24), which belongs to C500 s3's fixture-pin defect.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A SECOND READING-B DISCHARGE THAT ACTUALLY SELECTS. Reading A has a located pair of finders that both find things and disagree on exactly two patterns (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:225); reading B does not, and the only two reading-B discharges on this record are the replay of the record and the total refusal. A finder that satisfies reading B on all six recorded scenarios without replaying the record would make the reading-B non-uniqueness as strong as the reading-A one, and would change what :discharge-with-a-conformant-implementation costs. Failing that, what would move the measurement is the F2 carrier: the fixture carries the acknowledged clause, the route and the as-of (futon3:checks/find-snatch.edn), and a `Receipt` that held them would let F2 discriminate implementations that receipt-presence cannot.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C561-F11-find-discharge-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/05-discharge-arm.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C560-F11-find-function-conformance.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C559-F11-f2-falsifier-reconciliation.md", :question "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264? The declaration is a total function `Tension State -> Repository P -> FindResult P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:263 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded F1-F4 instances `do not select one canonical implementation`. The sorry is INERT, recomputed at slice 3 rather than asserted: over the 153 Lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower there is exactly ONE code occurrence of the token `find`, the declaration itself, plus 25 prose occurrences in doc-comments and module headers and one string literal in the hole registry (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:8020, `mkRefused \"find\"`) -- holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/05-discharge-arm.edn. So discharging it changes no proof obligation, and what the arms below differ over is what the declaration SAYS afterwards. EVERY EXISTENCE AND EVERY NON-UNIQUENESS RESULT BELOW IS STATED SEPARATELY UNDER EACH OF THE TWO READINGS OF F4, so that pricing the arms does not tacitly decide which reading F4 is.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-08", :by "joe", :channel "session, claude-1 decision-sheet item 3; RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-08.md item 3", :decision "REFUSAL-BECOMES-PATTERN: 'this sounds like a case where refusal-becomes-pattern would be ideal, and the pattern would act as a warrant to proceed with this implementation and gather evidence as NEXT STEPS that will support or modify it. That experience will be more useful than a ruling from me.' The refusal at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264 is converted into a written pattern; the written pattern is the warrant to proceed with an implementation of find; the evidence the implementation produces arrives as NEXT STEPS that support or modify the pattern, and :find-f2-receipt-carrier and :find-f4-reading are to be DECIDED BY THAT EVIDENCE, not guessed first (they stay :observed-not-decided until it arrives). Meta-pattern recorded with the ruling: 'many needs joe situations are really needs evidence situations, and we can't get that as efficiently if we wait gated on me to say so.' Verbatim, typos preserved.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :row :F11, :arms [{:arm :discharge-with-any-inhabitant, :buys "THE SORRY GOES AND, UNLIKE THE SIBLING ROW, THE RESULT IS NOT REFUTED. The type is inhabited with no assumptions (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:16), and `find`'s cheapest inhabitant SATISFIES F1-F3 and F4 reading A (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:20). This is where find and organise come apart: organise's cheapest inhabitant is refuted by O1 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:32), so for organise this arm converts a declaration that proves nothing into one that is false, and for find it does not.", :costs "THE LAWS STILL BITE, AND THE ARM IS THEREFORE A CHOICE RATHER THAN A FREE MOVE: `findSilent` -- the same empty output with F1's typed absence omitted -- is refuted, on the recorded 18-pattern repository and not on a degenerate empty one (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:35, non-vacuous by mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:45). What the arm actually costs is that the discharged `find` FINDS NOTHING: it selects the empty set on every input, so every F2 and F3 obligation is discharged vacuously and no recorded selection is reproduced.", :run-by "F11 slice 3 (C561); mathlib4 75a84289e8 + 34858bce32 review f99ab6bd44", :what-it-is "Replace the sorry with any total term. `findRefusing` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:120) returns the empty selection with F1's typed absence whatever it is handed."} {:arm :discharge-with-a-conformant-implementation, :buys "A CONFORMANT DISCHARGE EXISTS AND THE EXISTENCE IS PROVED SEPARATELY UNDER EACH F4 READING, so taking this arm does not tacitly decide which reading F4 is: F1-F3 alone at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:49, with reading A at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:54, with record-grain reading B at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:65.", :costs "IT SELECTS ONE IMPLEMENTATION, WHICH IS THE THING THE DOCSTRING REFUSES -- and the refusal is now a PROVED FACT rather than a stated one, under both readings: reading A at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:120, reading B at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:149. The disagreement is LOCATED rather than merely exhibited, and locating it is what needed review to add. Under reading A the located pair is two `findAllBut` instances at the two patterns the record declares zero-mass: both select the recorded member `askForSurplusNotSurrender` and each selects exactly the pattern the other drops (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:225). Under reading B there is no such pair, and that is itself the measurement: a finder can exclude one pattern from every repository, as reading A asks, and still return `forcedPlayNeedsALossFloor`, which the record declared zero-mass at `g4Snatcher` in advance (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:207). So on this record the two reading-B discharges are the finder that replays the record and the finder that refuses (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:169), and the second one's half of that agreement is vacuous because it excludes everything.", :run-by "F11 slice 2 (C560) built the witnesses; F11 slice 3 (C561) states the existence and the non-uniqueness under each F4 reading; mathlib4 75a84289e8 + f99ab6bd44", :what-it-is "Replace the sorry with a term the F-laws accept -- `findSnatchReplay` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:72), which replays the recorded find, or `findAllBut` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:72), each a total function at find's own type."} {:arm :amend-to-an-existence-statement, :buys "ITS WHOLE CONTENT IS ALREADY PROVED and needs no new mathematics: existence under each reading (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:54, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:65) and non-uniqueness under each (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:120, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:149). It removes the sorry while saying exactly what the docstring says, instead of contradicting it.", :costs "TWO, AND ONE OF THEM IS OUTSIDE THIS ROW. It turns `find` from a term into a proposition, so anything applying `find` would have to eliminate an existential -- which costs nothing today, since the census above finds zero term references anywhere in DarkTower, and would cost whatever the first consumer costs. And editing Holes.lean moves the contract twice over: the authority is derived as `git log -1 -- Holes.lean` (mathlib4/DarkTower/Contract/Emit.lean:52-62), so the amendment requires the C176 regeneration, AND the hole registry in the same file carries `find` as a refusal (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:8020), which an amendment has to restate rather than leave saying `implementation, not a law` of a declaration that is no longer an implementation. That is why this slice proved the content in a separate module and left Holes.lean untouched.", :run-by "F11 slice 3 (C561) proves the content; the edit to Holes.lean is NOT applied", :what-it-is "Replace the refused `def find ... := sorry` with the conformance predicate plus `exists f, ConformantFind f` -- the shape the acceptance's own swappability clause asks for at futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:530-534, `implementation conformance, not identity`."} {:arm :seal-it-opaque, :buys "THE SORRY GOES WITH NO IMPLEMENTATION CHOSEN. `opaque` does not require a body -- established for organise at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:271 and reproduced here: `findOpaqueNoBody` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:249) elaborates with no body at all from the local inhabitance instance at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:245, and removing that instance is what makes it fail. What separates the two routes is their AXIOM FOOTPRINT and it is machine-readable: `#print axioms` reports NO axioms for the body-carrying `findOpaqueRefusing` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:242) and `Classical.choice` for the bodiless one. A negative control also re-establishes that an instance declared LATER in the file does not rescue an earlier bodiless `opaque`.", :costs "NOTHING ABOUT THE VALUE SURVIVES THE SEAL, so no F-law can be witnessed of the declaration at all -- this arm keeps the refusal's content and gives up its evidence, where the conformant-discharge arm gives up the refusal and keeps the evidence. The body-carrying route additionally seals a specific term, and the term sealed here is `findRefusing`, which finds nothing.", :run-by "F11 slice 3 (C561); mathlib4 75a84289e8", :what-it-is "Replace the sorry with an `opaque` declaration, keeping the refusal and removing the sorry token."} {:arm :leave-it-refused, :buys "NOTHING MOVES, and the cost of that is smaller than it looks: the sorry is INERT, by the census in :question above -- over the 153 Lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower there is ONE code occurrence of `find` and it is the declaration itself. No proof obligation anywhere depends on it, and `holes/labs/wm-contract/f11_discharge_check.bb` FAILS with :find-is-no-longer-inert if a term reference ever appears.", :costs "THE MODULE KEEPS REPORTING IT. `lake build DarkTower.WarMachine.F11DischargeArm` emits `declaration uses sorry` for mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:264 alongside nine others in the same file, so any sorry census over Holes.lean counts it, and the acceptance's clause stays open indefinitely.", :run-by "F11 slice 3 (C561) measured its cost; recomputed, not copied from the sibling row", :what-it-is "Do nothing to the declaration."} {:arm :amend-the-carrier, :buys "MEASURED 2026-09-07 (F11 slice 6, C564; mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean, 43 declarations). TWO SEPARATIONS TODAY'S CARRIER CANNOT MAKE, AND THEY ARE INDEPENDENT. (i) Carried-clause receipts separate the faithful from the misattributing finder (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:259) where today's carrier CANNOT -- the two are EQUAL after erasure to today's `FindResult` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:340), which is slice 4's benchmark (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:186) restated of the joint pair; and content-F2 REFUTES the misattributor (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:246) at `ask-for-surplus-not-surrender`, a pattern the record selects, which today's presence-only `f2Receipted` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:25-26) accepts. (ii) A returned zero-mass field separates a second pair (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:286) that is likewise equal after erasure (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:351). THE TWO ARE NOT ONE AMENDMENT: the receipt-separated pair agrees on zero mass (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:298) and the zero-mass-separated pair agrees on receipts (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:302), so each buys a distinction the other does not. F4 also becomes a CONJUNCT of conformance (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:35) rather than a predicate over inputs -- but see :costs, because that conjunct is weaker than its name.", :costs "MEASURED 2026-09-07 (F11 slice 6, C564). THE F4 CONJUNCT CONSTRAINS NOTHING ON ITS OWN, which is the arm's real price and was not visible from either half. `amendedIdentity` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:358) satisfies all four joint laws (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:369) while selecting the WHOLE recorded 18-pattern repository (nonempty at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:398) and returning the EMPTY designation, and it refutes ALL THREE readings of F4 at once -- A at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:406, B at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:416, C at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:425, collected at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:440. So the two implication results (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:60 for reading B, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:71 for reading C) are carried ENTIRELY by their pinning hypotheses: the amendment buys a PLACE to put a designation, not an obligation that the designation be the recorded one. The finder still nominates, and may nominate nothing -- F4-as-a-conjunct is self-certifying in the way F3 forbids receipts to be. SECOND COST: it does NOT buy a `find` that finds something. `amendedRefusing` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:314) is conformant (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:320) with an empty selection, so this arm shares the limit every other arm above has. MECHANICAL COST, recomputed site by site rather than counted (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F11-find/11-amended-carrier.edn): NINE construction sites over all Lean files under mathlib4/DarkTower -- ONE plain `Receipt` at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:67 and EIGHT plain `FindResult` at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:76, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:121, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean:143, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:27, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11DischargeArm.lean:76, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:22, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:144 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:51. NONE anywhere under DarkTower outside the F11 family, which is small only because `find` has no callers at all. TWO CORRECTIONS TO WHAT WAS EXPECTED: the joint census is NOT slice 4's 7 -- that number counted F11ReceiptCarrier's own constructions of its variant carriers (`ReceiptWithAssertions`, `RelationalReceipt`) alongside the one real `Receipt`, and type-accurately there is exactly ONE plain `Receipt` site in the tree; and `none outside the pricing modules` holds only under the boundary that treats the whole F11 family as pricing modules -- under slice 4's boundary, SEVEN of the nine are outside this slice's module and are ordinary Lean code a real amendment breaks.", :run-by "F11 slice 6 (C564); mathlib4 d4103fce45 (codex-1) + 5c4aefab36 (review). The two halves it aggregates are `:find-f2-receipt-carrier` (slice 4) and `:find-f4-reading` (slice 5).", :what-it-is "Change what `find` returns or what a `Receipt` holds, so the laws can be stated of it in full. TWO SEPARATE QUESTIONS LIVE HERE. BOTH ARE NOW REGISTERED: `:find-f2-receipt-carrier` (F11 slice 4, 2026-09-07, five arms priced) and `:find-f4-reading` (F11 slice 5, 2026-09-07, five arms priced). (i) F2's carrier: `Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:240-242) has `citesTextOrEdges` and `scoreAlone` and no field for the acknowledged tension clause, the retrieval route or the as-of, all of which futon2/holes/problems/P-validated-R5.md:486 asks for and the record carries, so `ConformantFind.f2Receipted` states receipt PRESENCE only. (ii) F4's reading: `FindResult` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:247-250) has no `zeroMass` field -- that field is on the row carrier `FindReceiptRow` at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:258 -- which is why F4 is a predicate over a finder's inputs rather than a conjunct of `ConformantFind`, and why it has the two readings this entry prices against.", :why-not-run-here "The SORRY is not this entry's to remove. What this entry adds is that the carrier questions and the sorry are SEPARABLE -- every other arm above removes the sorry without touching either carrier. UPDATED 2026-09-07 (F11 slice 4): half of this arm now HAS an entry to point at -- `:find-f2-receipt-carrier` prices five arms for the receipt carrier, and its finding is that the blindness is in the carrier and not in F2's phrasing (the misattributing and the faithful finder are EQUAL after erasure to today's `FindResult`, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11ReceiptCarrier.lean:186). UPDATED AGAIN 2026-09-07 (F11 slice 5): the other half is now `:find-f4-reading`, which prices five arms and finds that C implies B, that A is incomparable with C in both directions, and that A-and-B is jointly satisfiable while reproducing the record (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F11F4Reading.lean:207-211). PRICED 2026-09-07 (F11 slice 6, C564): the arm's :buys and :costs are now MEASURED, and the aggregation was not a paraphrase of the two halves -- the joint module found the price neither half could see, that the F4 conjunct constrains nothing without a pinning hypothesis. What this key still records is why the SORRY does not follow from the pricing: amending the carrier and removing the sorry remain separable, and every other arm above removes the sorry without touching either carrier. This arm is also bigger than its name: `FindResult.receipts` is typed by `Receipt` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:247-250), so amending the carrier amends `find`'s own return type."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHICH mission's C parameterizes the tick's G when the machine's own selection and its witnessed clock edge name different missions -- and what the tick records when they do. G imports C (dacosta2020 eq. 44), and the formalism does not say which mission supplies it; that is the free hand. U11 wired C_mis to the CLOCKED mission, U21 wired it to the SELECTED one behind FUTON_WM_SELECTION_FOCUS, and neither says what happens when the two disagree -- which they do on 3 of 3 recorded 2026-09-02 ticks.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :focus-clock-reconciliation], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "WHICH mission's C parameterizes the tick's G when the machine's own selection and its witnessed clock edge name different missions -- and what the tick records when they do. G imports C (dacosta2020 eq. 44), and the formalism does not say which mission supplies it; that is the free hand. U11 wired C_mis to the CLOCKED mission, U21 wired it to the SELECTED one behind FUTON_WM_SELECTION_FOCUS, and neither says what happens when the two disagree -- which they do on 3 of 3 recorded 2026-09-02 ticks.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "WHICH mission's C parameterizes the tick's G when the machine's own selection and its witnessed clock edge name different missions -- and what the tick records when they do. G imports C (dacosta2020 eq. 44), and the formalism does not say which mission supplies it; that is the free hand. U11 wired C_mis to the CLOCKED mission, U21 wired it to the SELECTED one behind FUTON_WM_SELECTION_FOCUS, and neither says what happens when the two disagree -- which they do on 3 of 3 recorded 2026-09-02 ticks.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/focus-clock-reconciliation", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:measured "All eight cases produced what they declared (the script exits 1 if any does not). On the LIVE corpus no record reaches :lagged-write-landed or :lagged-write-missing, and that is the finding rather than a gap in the replay: the S4 read dropped witness.source until this row, so no persisted :active-mission carries the discriminating field and the honest reading of all three records is :lag-unattributable -- the divergence is real and its cause is not yet measurable. Record 0a18c4f7 reads :no-durable-edge; 4abad68c and 801976e7 read :lag-unattributable. U21's boolean returns false on all three AND on :clock-not-read, :durable-unreadable and :no-durable-edge, which is why the case vocabulary is added BESIDE it and does not replace it.", :grounds "The two rejected options both write or promise a write; only the third turns a silent failure into a recorded one without changing what a clock edge means. The discriminator is not new evidence -- witness.source has been stamped on every edge since S4 and was simply dropped by the read (active-clock-edge->mission, war_machine.clj:1525-1548, now keeps it under this flag).", :statement "The seam: load-active-mission reads the durable clock at the TOP of the tick (war_machine.clj:1549) and record-selection-clock! writes the new edge AFTER the trace is persisted (war_machine.clj:1986), inside a `future` whose failure is printed to stderr and dropped. So the focus a tick reads is the PREVIOUS tick's selection, and -- this is the part U21 left open -- a durable edge that is one tick stale because the write LANDED and one that is stale because the write NEVER LANDED read identically from inside a tick. U21 recorded the relation as one boolean, :agrees-with-durable?, which returns false for at least four different states including one where the durable side was never read at all (FUTON_WM_CLOCK_FOCUS off makes active-mission nil, so the projection is compared against {}).", :not-claimed "NOT ADJUDICATED, and one thing explicitly NOT repaired. :observed records that the divergence is now typed and the dropped write is now visible; no number here says the chosen option is better than the two rejected ones, and none of them has been run live. record-selection-clock! remains a fire-and-forget future whose failure is printed to stderr and dropped -- a tick that records :lagged-write-missing does not re-attempt the write. Repairing the write (a retry, or a same-tick witnessed edge) would change what a clock edge means and needs its own witness rule named; it is out of this row's scope and is not minted as a row here.", :evidence "IMPLEMENTED, DEFAULT OFF. Flag: war_machine.clj:125 *focus-reconcile?* / FUTON_WM_FOCUS_RECONCILE. Shared identity rule used by both sides of the seam, so writer and reader cannot drift: trace-record-identity war_machine.clj:1610-1618, delegated to by clock-source at war_machine.clj:1977-1984. Closed eight-case vocabulary: focus-reconciliation-cases war_machine.clj:1631-1667. Reconciler: focus-reconciliation war_machine.clj:1669-1738, attached by tick-mission-focus war_machine.clj:1740-1783 and called once at war_machine.clj:6195-6196 with the previous trace record. Render (half b): render-mission-focus-line war_machine.clj:4068-4109, appended at war_machine.clj:4126-4128 AFTER the untouched render-active-mission-line war_machine.clj:4058-4066, so the durable clock and the tick's focus are two lines and never one. Tests: war_machine_test.clj:2022-2247. Replay over the three 2026-09-02 records: holes/labs/wm-contract/u43_focus_reconcile.clj, artifacts under holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U43-focus-reconcile/.", :question "WHICH mission's C parameterizes the tick's G when the machine's own selection and its witnessed clock edge name different missions -- and what the tick records when they do. G imports C (dacosta2020 eq. 44), and the formalism does not say which mission supplies it; that is the free hand. U11 wired C_mis to the CLOCKED mission, U21 wired it to the SELECTED one behind FUTON_WM_SELECTION_FOCUS, and neither says what happens when the two disagree -- which they do on 3 of 3 recorded 2026-09-02 ticks.", :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-09.md Item 19d", :decision "DEFERRED WITH REASON: C_mis stays flag-gated per the :c-grain Item 19a ruling, so the which-mission-C-at-the-tick question cannot bite in RUN4; reopens when a run enables C_mis.", :grounds :ruling}, :provenance "U43, minted by U21. Choice-set registration under TN-edge-review-aif-wiring section 1 point 3, NOT a ruling (Joe 2026-09-01 rule): it records what the War Machine is observed to do behind a default-off flag. Related: :c-grain, which registers WHICH C runs live; this entry registers which MISSION supplies it when the two candidate sources disagree.", :observed :recorded-divergence-flag-gated-default-off, :options {:recorded-divergence-cleared-by-a-later-tick "CHOSEN. The tick records a typed divergence and the next tick says whether the previous tick's write landed, read off a witness rather than assumed: the clock edge already carries witness.source, the identity of the trace record whose selection caused it (clock-source, war_machine.clj:1977), and the tick already holds the previous trace record. Comparing them answers `did the previous write land?` with evidence. It requires no new write, mints no edge, and makes the currently-dropped failure visible in the record.", :same-tick-witnessed-edge "Write the clock edge synchronously before the trace, so the two sides agree by construction. REJECTED: it changes what a clock edge MEANS (a witness of a persisted decision becomes a witness of an intention), puts a substrate write on the tick's critical path ahead of the trace, and does not solve the case the row was minted for -- it moves the write's failure earlier, into the tick, rather than removing it. The row's own statement puts edge-minting out of scope: `a clock edge is witnessed evidence, and any minting this row proposes needs its witness rule named`.", :typed-pending-state "Record :pending on every mission selection until the write is witnessed. REJECTED: the tick cannot observe its own future's completion, and nothing in the tick ever resolves the pending state, so every mission tick would carry a :pending that only a LATER tick could clear -- which is option three with an extra field. It relocates the silence rather than removing it."}, :flip-is-j-gated "NO FLIP IS MADE AND NO RULING IS WRITTEN. FUTON_WM_FOCUS_RECONCILE defaults off (war_machine.clj:125); with it off, tick-mission-focus returns U21's map unchanged and the S4 clock read keeps its exact four-key shape (pinned by war_machine_test.clj:2022-2049). The reconciliation is computed from wm-decision and the previous trace record, both already final where they are bound, and attached after ranking and selection, so no rank, weight, temperature, admissibility verdict or selector can read it."}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "free-energy-form", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :free-energy-form], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "free-energy-form", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/free-energy-form", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "free_energy.clj:184-205; war_machine.clj:4450-4452; efe.clj:601-619, 782-794 (C448 5c.1)", :observed :laplace-channel-grain-diagnostic, :ruling {:at "2026-09-01", :by "joe", :consequence "The F row (R8) is marked :status :shortcut-to-retire; it stays in the registry and the figure until its replacement is realised and consumed, so the drawing keeps matching the code. Opened H4 (hole: F_pi not computed, F not consumed) and I2 (implement F_pi into Q(pi)) in worklist.edn.", :decision "The current Laplace channel F is a shortcut (J2). Do not accept it as a diagnostic to keep: retire it, and replace it with theory-aligned free-energy quantities that are actually needed and consumed -- the per-policy F_pi that the policy posterior imports (parr2022 eq. B.9: pi = sigma(ln E - F - G)), and a belief update that is the gradient of the F the machine reports, at one grain.", :grounds :ruling}, :statement "F is the continuous Laplace form over error channels and has no live consumer; the policy side is the discrete formulation (dacosta2020). No retrieved source cites this mixed-grain composition as one formalism; it is a stack composition unless a source is found.", :status :decided}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "gamma-fixed-point", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :gamma-fixed-point], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "gamma-fixed-point", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/gamma-fixed-point", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/C14" "wm-ticket/C15" "wm-ticket/C19" "wm-ticket/C20" "wm-ticket/C21" "wm-ticket/C22" "wm-ticket/C25"], :subjects [], :choice {:statement "TWO questions, and the source settles the first. WITHIN A TICK: pi = sigma(-F - gamma.G) and the beta update are mutually dependent -- gamma needs pi, and the policy posterior that defines pi imports tau = 1/gamma. friston2017 states the scheme outright: 'usually one would iterate the equalities in equation 2.7 until convergence' (friston2017.txt:683-685), with the gradient form in appendix B (:1690-1720) as the robust alternative. That is the formalism's answer, not an option. ACROSS TICKS: eq. 2.7 reads beta_posterior = beta_prior + (pi - pi0).G -- two distinct symbols the text extraction collapses. P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta_prior) at :339 and Q(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta_posterior) at :357 are the prior/posterior pair, and the precision prediction error at :1711 is eps_gamma = (beta_prior - beta_posterior) + (pi - pi0).G, which would be identically zero in its first term if the two were one symbol. What the paper does NOT say is what beta_prior is at the start of each tick. That silence is the choice point.", :u2-retrodiction {:report "C486-u2-tau-retrodiction.md", :bearing-on-the-ruling "Joe's :carried-prior ruling STANDS, unchallenged and unsupported by these numbers. It rests where it rested: on the tick-grain argument in :grounds-audit, not on a measurement. This entry records that the measurement Joe's own rule of 2026-09-01 asked for (:also-to-be-run) has now been attempted by retrodiction as well as by the rank-movement route of V6, and returned a typed no-discrimination result both times.", :script "u2_retrodiction.clj:1-632", :question-not-reached "WHETHER CARRYING IS BETTER. The measurement cannot reach it, and not because the effect is small: the counterfactual control recorded in :choices :temperature-update :u2-retrodiction shows the whole arm ordering is fixed before the outcome arrives (swapping the realised observation for one already known changes every arm-against-arm gap by 1.066e-14 on S2). A no-discrimination verdict from a score that does not depend on the outcome is not evidence about the arms. It is the absence of evidence, typed.", :at "2026-09-02", :question-reached "THE ACROSS-TICK ARMS, :carried-prior against :fixed-prior, scored by retrodiction on 19 S2 transitions and 3 S4 transitions. beta_0 was SWEPT over {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0} rather than fixed at the runs' 1.0, because C468 found the J4 rank movement concentrated at beta_0 = 0.5 and a result at one initial condition would be a result about that condition. NO DISCRIMINATION AT ANY beta_0: 0 ticks with a different argmax out of 19 (S2) and 0 out of 3 (S4), in every ln E arm, at every beta_0. The largest score difference anywhere is max |dL_mix| = 1.240e-03 at beta_0 = 0.5 in the :pi-only arm -- 0.16 percent of the 0.754047 range between an all-mass-on-the-best-retrodictor arm and an all-mass-on-the-worst one -- and it never reaches an argmax. Consistent with the :run-result above (C464 / V6: the argmax never moves).", :by "claude-cli", :question-also-reached "THE WITHIN-TICK QUESTION, which friston2017.txt:683-685 settles by fiat, was run anyway so that the source's answer has a number beside it: an arm applying the eq. 2.7 update ONCE from beta_prior, without iterating to the fixed point, differs from the iterated arm by max |dL_mix| 1.530e-07 (S2) and 1.165e-07 (S4), with 0 argmax differences on 22 of 22. On these fields the iteration the source requires costs nothing and buys nothing measurable. The source still settles it; nothing here contradicts it.", :artifact "U2-RETRODICTION.txt", :row :U2}, :evidence "worklist J4; build_order.bb (gamma sits in no layer); C461-beta-gamma-discovery.md section 6; friston2017.txt:334-339 (prior), :353-357 (posterior), :660-666 (eq. 2.7), :683-685 (iterate to convergence), :1705-1720 (appendix B gradient form and eps_gamma)", :experiment "Not yet run, and it does not need a live run: both arms are computable against a recorded field. Take a trace tick's ranked actions and G; iterate 2.7 to convergence from (a) a fixed beta_0 and (b) the previous tick's converged beta; report for each the converged gamma, the iteration count, whether it converged inside a bound at all, and the RANK CHANGES produced -- all three against the control, today's default live path, not against each other. BETA_0 IS A PARAMETER OF BOTH ARMS, not just the fixed one (claude-1, 2026-09-01): the carry arm has no previous tick at the first tick of any recorded sequence, so it starts from a declared beta_0 too. If beta_0 is not reported the two arms differ by an initial condition nobody chose, and the comparison measures that instead of the thing. A gamma difference that changes no ranking is not a difference worth ruling on. The iteration count and the non-convergence rate are the other half of the result: the WM has no iteration budget today, so 'it converges in k steps on real fields' is itself a finding.", :leaning {:at "2026-09-01", :by "joe", :note "A LEANING, not a ruling: worklist J4 stays :needs-joe. Joe, 2026-09-01: 'this is a good example of where we have a choice provided to us by the absence of any declaration from the theory... perhaps we are going to want to record the choice point, and develop some experiments looking at the two different ones... My leaning would be towards the second option.' His leaning was given against an earlier framing that offered within-tick iteration and across-tick carry as EXCLUSIVE alternatives (worklist J4 as first written, claude-20). They are not exclusive -- claude-1 caught this on 2026-09-01 and the source confirms it. The leaning survives the reframing: it was toward carrying, and carrying is now the :carried-prior arm of the second question, with the first question answered by the paper rather than by anyone here.", :toward :carried-prior}, :status :decided, :ruling {:grounds :ruling, :statement "beta_prior at the start of each tick is the previous tick converged beta_posterior. beta_0 remains required as the first-tick prior and must be declared and reported, never defaulted silently.", :also-to-be-run "Joe's rule of 2026-09-01 applies to his own ruling: :carried-prior against :fixed-prior over a recorded field, with the control being today's default path, reported as numbers beside the ruling rather than instead of it. If the numbers contradict the ruling that is a RESULT he wants, not a J row. Dispatched as worklist V6; beta_0 is a parameter of both arms and is reported.", :implied-by-the-source "An argument from the paper structure, not a sentence in it. friston2017 splits the approximate posterior into states and parameters -- x = (s_tilde, pi, eta) with eta = (a, b, d, beta) (:343) -- so beta is a PARAMETER, in the same tuple as the Dirichlet concentrations. Of that side the paper says the updates 'accumulate coincidences over time, because parameters are time invariant (in contrast to states that change over time)' (:815). States are re-derived per tick; parameters accumulate. :fixed-prior would move a member of eta onto the state side of the paper own division. Joe reached this before the check: 'the theory should say beta is carried, as i think that is implied'.", :run-result "RUN, 2026-09-01 (V6, C464-beta-carry-experiment.md, futon2 a08b90b + 9b6eac0). Three arms over both recorded fields, beta_0 swept {0.5, 1, 2, 5}, control = today default path. THE ARMS DIFFER: carried and fixed orderings diverge on 14 to 36 transitions in every field/start combination, so the choice is real. THE ARGMAX NEVER MOVES: not once across 54 transitions and four starts, so on these fields the choice changes no selection. THE CARRY DOES NOT DIVERGE: beta stays in 0.28..5.58, nowhere near the floor or the ceiling. AND THE HORIZON IS LONGER THAN OUR EVIDENCE. On 07-04 the four trajectories contract to within 0.001 of each other by t=37 -- the carry forgets its initial condition -- but at t=17 they are still 0.50, 0.87, 1.58 and 2.48 apart. 07-05 has only 17 transitions, so its apparent path dependence is a LENGTH artifact, not a property of that field. A carried beta over a 20-tick run is therefore still dominated by its beta_0, and any run of that length must report beta_0 beside every beta and must not describe the carry as converged. The ruling is not contradicted: carrying and resetting are genuinely different, they just do not reach the top of the ranking on the fields we have.", :consequence "I1 unblocked and built on :carried-prior. The :fixed-prior arm is retained below as the experiment control arm, not as a live option.", :at "2026-09-01", :by "joe", :grounds-audit "2026-09-01, after the V5 cross-check against SPM (C463). Joe gave TWO grounds; only one survives, and the entry says which. SURVIVES -- the tick grain: a WM tick is an SPM TIME STEP, not a trial. An SPM trial is an episode whose start re-initialises beliefs from D/d, re-enumerates the policy set, and returns qb to the prior; the WM has no such boundary, carries belief tick to tick, and never re-initialises from a prior, so it is one unending trial, and within a trial SPM carries beta across time steps exactly as ruled (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:433-434, :951-974). CONTRADICTED -- the parameter tuple: the argument that beta sits in eta = (a, b, d, beta) with the parameters that accumulate is not how the reference implementation treats it, since spm_MDP_update carries a, b, c, d and e between trials and NOT beta (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:1444-1448). The ruling stands on the first ground. Tick-grain decided by claude-20 as steward under Joe bar for J rows (worklist J5), not referred back to him.", :decision :carried-prior}, :control "TODAY'S DEFAULT LIVE PATH IS NEITHER ARM, and that is what dissolves the argument about which one it resembles (claude-1, 2026-09-01). On the default :selection-gain-only mode, tau comes from a CARRIED state that never updates live -- fold-realized-outcome's own docstring says the :realized-outcome field is absent today, sim-only (C2, C454) -- so today is a carried prior that does not move. Each arm therefore resembles today in exactly one aspect and departs in the other: :carried-prior keeps the persistence and adds the movement; :fixed-prior keeps the staticness and drops the persistence. The experiment's control must be the default live path itself, not either arm. A control chosen from the two things being compared is the failure this campaign keeps finding one level down.", :observed :neither-implemented, :options {:carried-prior "The previous tick's converged beta_posterior becomes this tick's beta_prior -- precision learned across ticks, the shape futon2.aif.selection-gain already uses (read/coerce at war_machine.clj:4332-4361, written back at :4773-4776). The machine gets more or less decisive as its policy evidence accumulates. Keeps the PERSISTENCE SHAPE of today's default path, and nothing else.", :fixed-prior "beta_prior resets to a declared beta_0 every tick. Each tick's decisiveness is set only by this tick's G and pi; nothing about precision is remembered. Keeps the WITHIN-TICK FRESHNESS of FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE=spread, which is not the default. Simpler, and the arm against which carrying is measurable."}}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 7, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "habit-prior", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :habit-prior], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "habit-prior", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/habit-prior", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/C23"], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "habit_prior.clj:70-89, 100-163 (learned, persisted); war_machine.clj:262-271, 4276-4283; policy.clj:234-271 (:habit-prior-applied? false on the live path) (C448 5c.3)", :observed :implemented-not-applied-live, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-09.md Item 19c", :decision "E is ON for RUN4: the learned, persisted habit prior is applied on the live strategic path; implementation task routed to codex-17 (discovery first; the :pi-zero-form arm question surfaces there and returns to Joe unless a recorded principle settles it).", :grounds :ruling}, :ruling-addendum-2026-09-09 "SUPERSEDED IN PART by Items 21a and 22 (same file): the promotion of the persisted E into the final strategic selector was REFUSED at implementation -- the persisted prior is tactical-grain by deliberate design (war_machine.clj comment; evidence in runs/E-live-strategic-discovery-2026-09-09.md + its addendum, futon2 b60d2f4b) -- and Joe then ruled FORWARD ACCUMULATION ONLY (Item 22, verbatim: models changed too much for historical reconstruction; redesign if needed after RUN4 is banked). Implemented at futon2 8dd17915 (store-level version-2 :strategic-habit-state alongside byte-unchanged tactical v1; opt-in :accumulate-strategic-habit? with explicit-false-wins; fixture E_S and beta wiring unchanged; promotion refused pending nonempty grain-labelled data), reviewed by claude-1 (63 tests/342 assertions/0 failures re-run). The E-ON intent of this ruling is realised for RUN4 as: accumulation ON, selector prior unchanged.", :statement "E is learned and persisted but the live strategic path does not apply it; the two run records carry no habit state.", :status :decided}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 1, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "hierarchy", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :hierarchy], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "hierarchy", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/hierarchy", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "rollout.clj:166-176 ('flat temporal rollout, not nested fast/slow hierarchy'); hierarchical_budget.clj exists but is not wired as a generative hierarchy (C448 5c.5)", :observed :single-level, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "model-choices sitting with codex-17; verbatim in SESSION-model-choices-2026-09-09.md (4f81e3d1)", :decision "RUN4-SCOPED: the single-level prediction model is accepted for RUN4's inner-loop exercise. If outer-loop work is involved in this run it USES the inner loop; that does not establish a coupled generative hierarchy. NOT a permanent single-level design and not a claim the stack is one AIF system. FOLLOW-ONS PRESERVED (Joe verbatim: the hierarchical model comes in due course with the Zaif agents): the outer loop with its own AIF, the inner loop with its own AIF, and AIF-backed Zaif agents / hierarchical model (M-zaif-harness reference); no coupling claimed now.", :grounds :ruling}, :statement "One level is realised; R15 runs no equation and is listed under :plumbing.", :status :decided, :theory-alternative "dacosta2020 A.4 deep temporal models"}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "learning", :presentation-title "Finish the learning design for review", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-10", :basis-count 2, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :observed-not-decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :learning], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"} {:as-of "2026-09-10", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "p4ng/empirics-futon/issue-board-next-actions.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/Item25-model-choice-chain-2026-09-09/README.md:1", :selector "wm-choice/learning", :sha256 "ee324659f7f7ad75fdc863ccb84b96377a98e4b7d47094dd779f58e7c777a849"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "The other model choices are ruled. Learning remains formally unruled: complete the proposed evidence/update/next-consumer design for review; do not reopen the offline-only question or infer adoption.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "Finish the learning design for review", :column :ready-for-lane, :id "wm-choice/learning", :kind :choice, :workflow-disposition-only? true, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Learning and next-use", :loops ["Inner loop" "Outer loop"], :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/Item25-model-choice-chain-2026-09-09/README.md:1", :related-r-nodes [], :status :editorial}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "r17_offline.clj:1-6, 64-96; a4a.clj:126-159; Holes.lean:6380-6385 DirichletConcentrations (carrier only) (C448 5c.6)", :observed :offline-bmr-only, :scope-correction-2026-09-09 "Joe, later the same sitting (SESSION-model-choices-2026-09-09.md, 'Record learning scope correction'): NO full PLoP-variant restoration required — the earlier work INSPIRES a concrete AIF-compatible implementation and claim; learning is not prescribed as a single final phase. LR1-LR7 (LEARNING-historical-recovery-spec) are REFERENCE MATERIAL, not mandatory restoration and not RUN4 gates. Not inferred: offline-only adoption, automatic post-RUN4 deferral, mandatory GFN/BMR combination. The next design specifies each actual learned variable, its evidence, update equation/objective, schedule, persistent state and NEXT CONSUMER, distinguishing state inference / parameter learning / slower structure-proposal revision. No arm ruled yet.", :statement "Structure learning by BMR runs offline on Dirichlet models; live F is not its input (R8->R17 not realised).", :status :observed-not-decided, :theory-alternative "dacosta2020 eq. 21 Dirichlet accumulation -- Lean carrier exists, no live counterpart", :withheld-2026-09-09 "Joe EXPLICITLY WITHHOLDS the ruling pending theory/PLoP/implementation clarification (model-choices sitting; verbatim in SESSION-model-choices-2026-09-09.md, investigation runs/LEARNING-theory-history-runtime-2026-09-09.md, 685c107c). Do NOT close as offline-only: the Da Costa synthesis (sections 8-9) licenses trial-boundary parameter learning (posterior becomes next prior) and BMR; the missing evidence is SUBSEQUENT CONSUMPTION, not an online/offline distinction. Recorded conflict, no side asserted: PLoP Campaign S 26-observation inter-tick claim vs VERIFY-r-nodes later failing to locate retained receipts. Preserved: the July GFN diversity-supplier ruling and slush apparatus; edge credit today counts attachments and has no cascade-construction consumer. Proposed next contract (not adopted): named learned object, admissible evidence, versioned posterior, observed next-use with a disconnected-consumer control."}, :source-derived-column :ruling-needed, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "mission-phase-value", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :mission-phase-value], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "mission-phase-value", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/mission-phase-value", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/U22" "wm-ticket/U44"], :subjects [], :choice {:measured "Per resolvable id in :mission/cross-refs, whether that neighbour's :mission/phase is readable, which is what the judge needs to answer 'is this neighbour workable, at or past DERIVE?'; and once per mission, whether :mission/mtime is inside a declared 14-day window. Both come off the code/v05/mission-doc hyperedge that mission-doc-index (war_machine.clj:1450-1474) already fetches -- no new read boundary. On the 2026-09-03 field: 374 hyperedges, all 374 named, 313 with a readable phase; 123 of the 133 candidates :measured, 8 :phase-unreadable, 2 absent from the index.", :statement "Mission value is pragmatic-only in the shipped default: central and strategic say where a payoff lands, doable says how close the mission is to delivering one, and no factor pays for finding out. The epistemic term is implemented as of 2026-09-03 and reachable through the :mission-value-weights opt or FUTON_WM_VALUE_WEIGHTS, at weight 0.0 by default. Da Costa eq. 42's G is ambiguity + risk - novelty; the mission-grain term here is the novelty side at a grain the theory does not write, so it is a stack specialisation and not a form any retrieved source states.", :not-claimed "NO RULING AND NO DEFAULT CHANGE. Nothing here says 0.15 is the right weight or that this question set is the right one; :observed records that the term is now in the code behind a declared input. Three limits, measured rather than hedged. (a) 266 cross-references over 116 missions resolve to no mission the index knows, 39 of them numeric (M-1..M-7 on M-pattern-mining, M-foo/M-bar/M-baz on M-portfolio-inference, M-INC, M-WS): the first run of this term paid ln 2 nats for each and put M-pattern-mining at rank 4 on nine open questions, eight of them scrape artefacts, so unresolvable references are now EXCLUDED and counted, and the ingest that writes :mission/cross-refs is where that belongs. (b) Over the 123 measurable candidates the open-question count is {0 6, 1 108, 2 8, 3 1} -- 108 have exactly one open question and it is their own reading staleness, and only 9 have an unread neighbour -- so on this field the term is close to a staleness ordering with a phase mask and its moves are correspondingly small. The obvious next question kind is already written in the docs (the numbered 'MAP must answer:' lists) and is a follow-on row. (c) NOTHING DOWNSTREAM CHANGES BY DEFAULT: with :epistemic 0.0 the term is not computed at all.", :chosen-form "epistemic(M) = survey-availability(phase(M)) * min(1, EIG(M) / (10 * ln 2)), added as a FOURTH additive factor beside central/strategic/doable. EIG(M) is the sum over M's field questions of the policy-conditioned expected information gain of resolving that question, computed by the canonical kernel epistemic_value.clj:64-90 with its Bayes-coherence gate -- NOT a posterior spread and NOT a gap lookup, which epistemic_value.clj:9-13 refuses by name. Each question is ONE BINARY LATENT READ PERFECTLY, so an unsettled question has prior 0.5 and is worth ln 2 nats and a settled one is worth 0; the degenerate settled case goes through the same kernel via a one-observation model whose posterior IS the prior (mission_epistemic_value.clj:186-205), so the coherence gate applies to every question rather than to the open ones only.", :evidence "Implementation mission_epistemic_value.clj (316 lines) wired at war_machine.clj:2301-2302 and :2326-2329; tests mission_epistemic_value_test.clj and the U22 block of war_machine_test.clj. Step-through runs/U22-mission-epistemic/ (README.md plus seven EDN files), produced by u22_mission_epistemic.clj: both rankings from the SHIPPED enrich-candidates-with-mission-value on the same 133 candidates, differing only in the weights map. The after-weights keep Joe's option-B ratio among the three exploit factors and shrink them by (1 - 0.15), so value_after = 0.85 * value_before + 0.15 * epistemic * gates * decay -- checked and holding on 133 of 133 rows -- and a common positive factor cannot reorder the exploit part, so every rank move IS the epistemic term. Rank 1 unchanged in both arms (M-zaif-harness-v1). Headline: M-web-arxana-missions, MAP, rank 124 -> 74 on two open questions worth 1.3863 nats; against a LIVE doability factor (arm C, one declared substitution) 102 -> 87, passing fifteen missions closer to delivering.", :fiat-table "phase-doability, war_machine.clj:2133-2143: head 0.1, identify 0.2, map 0.3, derive 0.5, argue 0.6, verify 0.8, instantiate 1.0, document 0.4, complete 0.0, unknown 0.3. It prices only the exploit side -- monotone toward INSTANTIATE -- which is what the ruling is about. UNCHANGED by U22 and deliberately so; changing it would have been the silent default change the row forbids.", :default-off "default-mission-value-weights is {:central 0.25 :strategic 0.45 :doable 0.30 :epistemic 0.0} (war_machine.clj:2128-2131). At weight 0.0 field-readings returns nil, NO substrate read happens, no field is attached to any candidate, and the recorded numbers are byte-identical -- pinned by war_machine_test/the-epistemic-weight-defaults-to-zero-and-reads-nothing. A three-key weights map is still accepted with :epistemic defaulted to 0.0, so the FUTON_WM_VALUE_WEIGHTS declarations already in use are unaffected; the four must still sum to 1 (mission-value-weights, war_machine.clj:2212-2231).", :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-02", :by "joe", :consequence "Opened zaif-harness S5, ported here as worklist :U22 (implemented 2026-09-03). The DEFAULT FLIP -- giving :epistemic a non-zero weight in default-mission-value-weights -- is NOT ruled and is worklist :J7.", :decision "The selector must be able to prefer a PERCEIVE-stage phase: 'yes, we do need to prefer perceive in some cases... with the MAP phase in a mission, we need to be able to do that, and that's similar to the explore-exploit dichotomy that active inference is supposed to be quite good at'. The AIF-native fix is NOT a bigger fiat number for MAP -- it is an EPISTEMIC TERM in the mission value, so a MAP-phase mission scores by expected information gain about the field and wins exactly when uncertainty about the field is what blocks everything else. The hand-authored table then becomes what it should have been: a prior, not the whole value.", :grounds :ruling, :where "futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle-wm-alignment.md section 5, question 1, dictated in session"}, :declared "Four fiats, named as such. (1) The latent is 'workable' = phase at or past DERIVE, read off phase-doability at threshold 0.5 rather than declared a second time (mission_epistemic_value.clj:100-128, pinned equal to war-machine's table by war_machine_test/the-doability-prior-is-pinned-across-the-two-namespaces). (2) The observation model is a perfect reading of that bit. (3) phase-survey-availability, one number per phase: head 0.3, identify 0.6, map 1.0, derive 0.2, argue 0.1, verify 0.0, instantiate 0.0, document 0.1, complete 0.0, with 'unknown' DELIBERATELY ABSENT so an unreadable phase earns no survey credit and says so as a typed absence. (4) reference-open-questions 10, the denominator, which is a CONSTANT and not the mission's own question count -- dividing by n(M) measures the DENSITY of ignorance and on this field it ranked M-metric-harness (one question, open, 0.69 nats) above M-pattern-mining (nine open, 6.24 nats), the thinnest neighbourhood winning the survey. This table is hand-authored exactly like phase-doability; under the ruling that is what it is allowed to be, because it MULTIPLIES measured nats instead of standing in for them.", :observed :three-factor-exploit-only-epistemic-term-implemented-default-off, :adjacent-finding "The doability factor itself has been INERT on the futon2 path since 2026-07-19, and the phase is sitting on the hyperedge it already fetched. compute-delta-t-mission (war_machine.clj:2046-2054) resolves phase through futon3c.aif.mission-delta-t, which is not on futon2's classpath, so requiring-resolve returns nil, the {:delta-T 0.0} fallback carries no :mission-phase, and phase-doable takes the 'unknown' 0.3 for every candidate. In the records: :phase is nil on every ranked mission row in every trace file from wm-trace-2026-07-19.edn onward (rows carrying a :doable key, per trace file: 07-17 103 rows / 98 non-nil phases / nine distinct :doable values; 07-18 107 / 99 / nine; then 07-19 106 / 0 / {0.3 106}, 07-21 109 / 0 / {0.3 109}, 08-30 and 08-31 134 / 0 / {0.0 4, 0.3 130}, 09-01 267 / 0 / {0.0 8, 0.3 259}, 09-02 269 / 0 / {0.0 8, 0.3 261}), so on 09-02 :doable is 0.3 on 261 of the 269 rows with the other 8 operator-gated at 0.0. Meanwhile :mission/phase is a prop on the same code/v05/mission-doc hyperedge (mission_delta_t.clj:237-240 reads it off the endpoint vertex) and 313 of 374 carry a readable one. Where both carriers have a reading they AGREE: 123 agree, 0 disagree (runs/U22-mission-epistemic/07-doability-live.edn). So this is a plumbing gap, not a disagreement about phase. NOT REPAIRED HERE -- repairing it would change the default doable of most candidates, which is the silent default change U22 forbids. Written up in C492-mission-epistemic-value.md section 4b; it wants its own row.", :default-ruling {:at "2026-09-03", :by "joe", :channel "J7 walkthrough in session, claude-1 presenting the recommendation with the inert-doability sequencing argument; Joe verbatim: 'j7 stay off (but come back to this later)'", :decision "The :epistemic weight stays 0.0 by default. EXPLICITLY A STAY, NOT A RETIREMENT: 'come back to this later' is part of the ruling. The accepted grounds: the doability factor is inert on the futon2 path (:adjacent-finding below -- every candidate reads the constant 0.3), so a non-zero epistemic default today would trade explore against a constant rather than against real doability. The named prerequisite for revisiting is the doability-liveness repair, minted as worklist :U44; when it lands, J7's question returns to Joe with a live-doability step-through.", :grounds :ruling}}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 3, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHICH CARRIER are O1-O4 stated of? organise returns a Cascade (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861), and Cascade carries nodes, addedByOrganise, edges, acyclic and precedence (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-34) -- none of `selected`, none of `admittedBy`, and none of the six before/after fields O4 reads. The four laws as proved today are proved of a CascadeDiff VALUE instead (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:846-858, fixture at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:974), so what organise is declared to return and what the laws are stated of are two different types. This is D1, raised at C539 section 4. It blocks slice 4 -- implementing organise and discharging or amending the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 -- because an implementation has to return one of these carriers.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :organise-carrier], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "WHICH CARRIER are O1-O4 stated of? organise returns a Cascade (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861), and Cascade carries nodes, addedByOrganise, edges, acyclic and precedence (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-34) -- none of `selected`, none of `admittedBy`, and none of the six before/after fields O4 reads. The four laws as proved today are proved of a CascadeDiff VALUE instead (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:846-858, fixture at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:974), so what organise is declared to return and what the laws are stated of are two different types. This is D1, raised at C539 section 4. It blocks slice 4 -- implementing organise and discharging or amending the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 -- because an implementation has to return one of these carriers.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "WHICH CARRIER are O1-O4 stated of? organise returns a Cascade (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861), and Cascade carries nodes, addedByOrganise, edges, acyclic and precedence (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-34) -- none of `selected`, none of `admittedBy`, and none of the six before/after fields O4 reads. The four laws as proved today are proved of a CascadeDiff VALUE instead (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:846-858, fixture at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:974), so what organise is declared to return and what the laws are stated of are two different types. This is D1, raised at C539 section 4. It blocks slice 4 -- implementing organise and discharging or amending the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 -- because an implementation has to return one of these carriers.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/organise-carrier", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:all-arms-run "2026-09-07, F12 slice 13 (C551): the sixth arm, registered by C550 as :not-run with both fields :unmeasured, is run and carries measured :buys and :costs. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is still :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. Every arm of this choice now carries a measured cost and the payments still differ in kind, so what a slice can add to D1 is exhausted; the choice is Joe's.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED: :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. This entry chooses no carrier, discharges and amends nothing -- the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is untouched, and mathlib4 git log -1 still reads 61c4825dc3 on Holes.lean and 50fa53469a on holes-contract.json. It says nothing about D2 (which denominator O4's acting order is read over), about D3, about the third-origin choice registered as :organise-third-origin, or about the O3 field question registered as :organise-o3-field: arms four and five each carry BOTH O3 readings, so registering them here does not decide the field. The `O4 unstatable` rows are claims about which fields a structure has, not claims about whether O4 is true. UPDATED 2026-09-07 BY SLICE 13: the sixth arm is no longer unrun, so this entry now carries an :all-arms-run key as its two sibling F12 entries do; what that key records is that no slice has anything left to run on this choice, NOT that the choice is settled.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "TWO THINGS, and neither is producible from the code as it stands. (1) A library-scale recorded run whose precedence moves, which is what would let arm two's and arm six's extra law be exercised where the other arms are instantiated: futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:402 writes :precedence-before [] and :precedence-after [] as literals (futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:420-421) and carries no score, so the constructor cannot produce one -- and holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_cascadediff_check.bb FAILS if that literal ever becomes computed, because the vacuity finding would then be stale. The corpus is not empty of such a run: futon3:checks/ants-cascade.edn carries one, at five patterns rather than library scale, so the missing thing is a library-scale one and not the shape. (2) An implementation that COMPUTES admittedBy rather than looking it up on the recorded input, which is what would move arm five's second cost; that is the same absence :organise-third-origin measures. UPDATED 2026-09-07 BY SLICE 13: the row this text called blank is now filled, and filling it did not change what separates the other five arms.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C551-F12-cascadediff-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/08-cascadediff-arm.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C550-F12-carrier-choice.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C543-F12-d1-arms-run.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C544-F12-organise-function-conformance.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C545-F12-admitting-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C539-F12-organise-census.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/03-d1-arms.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/04-conformance.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/05-admitting-arm.edn", :question "WHICH CARRIER are O1-O4 stated of? organise returns a Cascade (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861), and Cascade carries nodes, addedByOrganise, edges, acyclic and precedence (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-34) -- none of `selected`, none of `admittedBy`, and none of the six before/after fields O4 reads. The four laws as proved today are proved of a CascadeDiff VALUE instead (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:846-858, fixture at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:974), so what organise is declared to return and what the laws are stated of are two different types. This is D1, raised at C539 section 4. It blocks slice 4 -- implementing organise and discharging or amending the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 -- because an implementation has to return one of these carriers.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-07", :by "joe", :channel "session, claude-1 walking C558 item-by-item (RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-07.md item 4); Joe verbatim: 'I agree we can go with arm 6, and I also think, given the complexity entailed, we need to find an example... let's see if it even works at all in principle once, on something. So, we'll try to build to this specification and then see how it looks after that.'", :consequence "F12 slice 4 is unblocked and is the designated place for the build-to-spec exemplar. The declared signature at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is expected to change (the Score parameter appears) ONLY as part of the staged edit the :organise-sorry ruling describes -- one Holes.lean edit, after the exemplar, paying the C176 contract regeneration once.", :decision "ARM 6, :function-at-the-cascadediff-codomain: the four O-laws are stated of a FUNCTION at the CascadeDiff codomain (signature mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:119, predicate mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:16), WITH AN EXEMPLAR PROVISO: the choice is exercised once on something real before being treated as validated. The designated exemplar is what C558 section 1 names as what would change the measurement -- a recorded run whose precedence moves and carries a score, driven through a conformant implementation at the arm-6 signature, so O4 is non-vacuous on a run rather than only on the C59 fixture and futon3:checks/ants-cascade.edn.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :measurement-that-separates-them "NO ARM STATES ALL FOUR LAWS OF ONE CARRIER WITHOUT PAYING, AND THE PAYMENTS DIFFER IN KIND RATHER THAN IN SIZE -- an extra hypothesis (arm one), a type parameter the interface does not declare (arm two), a law that cannot be written (arms one, three, four, five for O4; arm three for O1), or an origin that is statable and undetermined (arm five). RECOMPUTED, NOT CITED: on 2026-09-07 the three checkers that measure these arms were re-run and each PASSes and regenerates its artifact byte-identically -- holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d1_arms_check.bb (03-d1-arms.edn), holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_conformance_check.bb (04-conformance.edn), holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_admitting_check.bb (05-admitting-arm.edn). What they establish, and why the table above is a measurement rather than a reading: the three carriers' field lists are read out of Holes.lean and F12D1Arms.lean rather than transcribed (Cascade five fields, ArmOneCascade seven, CascadeDiff twelve), so every `O4 is unstatable here` row is checked; each arm's signature is read out of its own file and compared with organise's own type (:organise-type in 04-conformance.edn and 05-admitting-arm.edn), so no arm's verdict can quietly be a verdict about a different interface; both O3 readings are read out and differ in exactly the fastForward argument and agree in o1 and o2, so arms four and five are not tacitly deciding the field question; and the recorded numbers every arm is instantiated at -- twenty nodes, eleven selected, nine admitted, thirteen authored edges, a 27-vertex closure -- agree with slice 2's derivation at futon3 1b8b1d1 in every arm file.", :row :F12, :arms [{:arm :widen-the-cascade-carrier, :buys "O1 becomes writable of what organise returns, and is proved on the recorded run with nine of the twenty nodes coming from admittedBy rather than the C59 fixture's selected u empty u empty (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:98).", :costs "THE WIDENED CARRIER STILL HAS ONE EDGE FIELD AND NO AUTHORED RELATION, so O2 and O3 cannot be stated of it alone: both take the repository as an extra hypothesis (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:106 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:113 each carry `hrepo`). The arm needs arm three's pairing for two of the three laws it was meant to fix. O4 stays unstatable: all six O4 fields are absent from ArmOneCascade, recomputed into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/05-admitting-arm.edn (:carriers :o4-fields-absent-from-arm-one).", :run-by "F12 slice 5 (C543 sections 3 and 4a); mathlib4 cde38a4b2e + e77f73b679", :what-it-is "ArmOneCascade (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:74-81): Cascade's five fields plus `selected` and `admittedBy`. The arm's signature widens the FIRST argument as well as the result (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:84), which is what separates it from arm five."} {:arm :codomain-cascadediff, :buys "THE ONLY SELF-SUFFICIENT VALUE CARRIER: authoredEdges and organisedEdges are separate fields, so O1, O2 and O3 need nothing supplied alongside and are already proved of the recorded run (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:993, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1004, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1014). It is also the only carrier at which O4 is statable at all.", :costs "A `Score` TYPE PARAMETER THE DECLARED SIGNATURE DOES NOT HAVE (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:119 against mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861), and the extra law it makes room for is UNEXERCISED ON THE RUN EVERY ARM IS INSTANTIATED AT: all three before/after pairs are flat on the zaif run (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:123, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:129, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:134), because futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:402 writes both precedence vectors as [] (futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:420-421) and carries no score. UNEXERCISED IS NOT UNEXERCISABLE and the difference is worth keeping: O4 is discharged on the C59 fixture, whose precedence does move (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:916-921), and one of the nine recorded cascades carries a satisfied O4 row -- futon3:checks/ants-cascade.edn:79-105, read out of the record today: :precedence-changed? true, the acting order moves (pheromone-trail-tuner and white-space-scout swap), :score-changed? false, so the disjunction holds on its left. Whether that record's acting order is the denominator O4 means is D2's question and not this one.", :run-by "F12 slices 2 and 5 (C543 sections 3 and 4b); mathlib4 61c4825dc3, cde38a4b2e + e77f73b679", :what-it-is "retype the result to CascadeDiff P Score (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:846-858); the signature is mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:119."} {:arm :cascade-repository-pair, :buys "O2 and O3 proved directly, with no extra hypothesis and no carrier edit (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:152, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:158), and neither is a statement about an empty edge relation: the recorded edge 18-19 is inhabited (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:165) and the unauthored pair 0-1 is refuted (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:174).", :costs "O1 IS NOT WRITABLE AT ALL -- neither carrier has `selected` and neither has anywhere for `admittedBy` (Repository is patterns, standsOn, acyclic: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:121-124) -- and the one substitution the pair makes available is REFUTED ON THE RECORD rather than left as a doubt: Repository.patterns is the 27-vertex closure and not the cascade's twenty nodes, with vertex 26 the witness (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:180). O4 unstatable. So under this arm O1's third origin has nowhere to live, which is the gap the :LA2 amendment added the field to close (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:833-845).", :run-by "F12 slice 5 (C543 sections 3 and 4c); mathlib4 cde38a4b2e + e77f73b679", :what-it-is "leave both carriers alone and state the laws of a Cascade-plus-Repository pair (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-34 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:121-124)."} {:arm :state-the-laws-of-the-function, :buys "THE CARRIER QUESTION DISAPPEARS FOR TWO OF THE FOUR LAWS. O2 and O3 need neither the extra hypothesis arm one pays nor the pairing arm three pays, because the repository is already an argument. Swappability is witnessed rather than asserted: two implementations at the exact signature are both conformant (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:59 proved at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:68, and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:77 proved at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:86) and differ on the recorded inputs at vertex 26 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:107).", :costs "O1 LOSES ITS THIRD ORIGIN -- the two-way union is all that is writable -- and the loss is measured, not described: any conformant f returning the recorded twenty files all nine policy-admitted nodes under addedByOrganise (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:123), which is the misattribution the :LA2 amendment added admittedBy to prevent (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:833-845). The unconditional half: the up-closure temperament cannot reach admitted vertex 11 at all (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:216), and the up-closure of the recorded selected set is exactly {20, 21, 25, 26} with no edge from a selected node into an admitted one -- recomputed 2026-09-07 into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/04-conformance.edn (:up-closure-of-selected). O4 stays unstatable, and that claim is a measurement rather than a comment: the checker reads Cascade's field list out of the source as {acyclic, addedByOrganise, edges, nodes, precedence} with all six O4 fields absent (same artifact).", :run-by "F12 slice 6 (C544); mathlib4 0c5745c39e + 0691f74e48", :what-it-is "NO CARRIER EDIT: state conformance of a FUNCTION at the declared type (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:19, predicate at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:23-28), where `sel` and `repo` are arguments rather than fields. It is a fourth framing next to C539 section 4's three arms rather than a fourth arm of the same kind: the arms ask which carrier holds the laws and this asks whether they need one."} {:arm :function-with-the-result-widened, :buys "THE THIRD ORIGIN BECOMES STATABLE: O1 is the three-way law (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:893-897 at the value grain), and O2 and O3 discharge at the recorded repository with no extra hypothesis (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:33, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:40). A witness returns exactly the nine recorded admissions in admittedBy and exactly the recorded twenty nodes, and is conformant on all four clauses (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:73, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:79, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:63).", :costs "STATABLE IS NOT DETERMINED: a mirror files the same nine nodes under addedByOrganise, leaves admittedBy empty, is conformant (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:87, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:98), agrees on nodes and on the whole edge relation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:108, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:114) and differs at recorded vertex 11 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:120). That undetermination is the choice registered separately as :organise-third-origin, and this arm is where it comes from. Two further costs. The clause list grows by one over the function framing -- `osel`, which pins the widened selected field to the argument (recomputed into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/05-admitting-arm.edn, :clauses :added-over-slice-6). And the only witness anyone has built for the third origin is a lookup on the recorded input, `if sel = d1Selected then d1Admitted else empty` (same artifact, :witness :shape :recorded-lookup-table), so what it establishes is that the field CAN be filled consistently, not that anything computes it. O4 still unstatable: the six fields are absent from ArmOneCascade too.", :run-by "F12 slice 7 (C545); mathlib4 7d4f6ffca3 + acb4e95bcf", :what-it-is "the function framing with the RESULT carrier alone widened to ArmOneCascade (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:17), the argument list of mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 unchanged -- which is what separates it from arm one, whose signature also widened the first argument."} {:arm :function-at-the-cascadediff-codomain, :buys "ALL FOUR LAWS JOINTLY STATABLE AND JOINTLY DISCHARGED OF ONE WITNESS at the recorded inputs, with no hrepo hypothesis of the kind arm one pays (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:266 against mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:106 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:113). The O4 half is unique to the carrier and that is a measurement, not a reading: four field lists are read out of their own sources -- Cascade five, Repository three, ArmOneCascade seven, CascadeDiff twelve -- and the six O4 fields are present in CascadeDiff and in nothing else (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/08-cascadediff-arm.edn :carriers :o4-statable-at). O1 is three-way and identical to slice 7's clause; O3 takes the node-set reading, so this arm does not tacitly decide :organise-o3-field.", :costs "TWO, AND NEITHER IS THE ONE THE DISPATCH EXPECTED. (1) THE SCORE PARAMETER IS NOT NOTATION: at Score := Empty this arm's type has NO INHABITANTS (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:292), because a total function at the signature must produce two Score values on inputs that carry none, while organise's declared type is inhabited at the same argument types (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:300). The witness therefore takes [Inhabited Score] and writes default twice. (2) THE EXTRA LAW IS SATISFIED VACUOUSLY ON THE RUN EVERY D1 ARM IS INSTANTIATED AT, measured three ways rather than assumed: generally over every function (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:100), by a second conformant witness whose acting order and score both move with the precedence flat (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:129, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:161), and over the corpus -- nine cascade records under futon3:checks, EXACTLY ONE (futon3:checks/ants-cascade.edn) carrying an O4 row whose antecedent is true, six declining with a reason and two carrying no :o4 key, with the zaif run among the six that decline. THE CLAUSE IS NOT VACUOUS IN GENERAL and that is proved rather than said: a counterexample moving its precedence with acting order and score flat satisfies every other clause and is not conformant (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:184 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:196), which locates the failure at O4 alone. Nor is the vacuity an artefact of the Lean transcription: the Clojure law it mirrors is a disjunction whose first disjunct is the negated antecedent (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531), read out of the source by the checker. A THIRD THING IS NOT A COST AND SAYING SO IS PART OF THE RESULT: CascadeDiff is the only carrier with its own authoredEdges field, and dropping the clause that pins it does NOT let O2/O3 be satisfied against an invented relation, because both read the repository ARGUMENT (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:218). What the clause does is pin a result field no other clause reads -- any function conformant without it is conformant under an overwrite that changes none of the other eleven fields (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:306, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:312, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:340) -- where the value-grain O2 at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1004 DOES read the field, having no repository in scope. Both facts are checked textually and not asserted.", :run-by "F12 slice 13 (C551); mathlib4 dc3ab3bf98 + bea1e26583", :what-it-is "the two halves nobody had put together: conformance of a FUNCTION (arm four) whose result is a CascadeDiff (arm two), at the already-written signature mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:119. WHEN C550 REGISTERED THIS ARM THAT ABBREV WAS MENTIONED BY NO THEOREM IN ANY F12 MODULE, so what the build checked of it was well-formedness; the predicate is mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12CascadeDiffArm.lean:16 and the abbrev is now used 15 times in that file, recomputed by holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_cascadediff_check.bb rather than counted (:organise-type :arm-two-uses-in-the-arm-file).", :why-it-was-named-not-run "C550 section 3 registered it :buys :unmeasured :costs :unmeasured rather than counting it among the five run arms, on the ground that registering D1 with five arms and calling them all would be the overstatement the entry exists to avoid. Slice 13 ran it. What it found is that the arm does deliver the joint statability the entry credited it with, and that its price is not the one C550 guessed: C550 named the vacuous O4 as the suspected cost and that is confirmed, but the Score parameter turns out to buy emptiness at some instantiations rather than mere notation, and the authoredEdges field the dispatch expected to be a self-certification hazard is not one."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHAT DISCHARGES THE EXEMPLAR PROVISO ON THE ARM-6 CARRIER RULING? Joe's ARM 6 ruling of 2026-09-07 attached a proviso -- verbatim, `the choice is exercised once on something real before being treated as validated` (holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:615) -- and the :organise-sorry ruling stages the Holes.lean edit behind it (holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:668; destination mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861, still at 61c4825dc3e373fd1b761b800814bf85f5770b88 and untouched). Three exemplars now stand at the ruled signature `RuledOrganiseType` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12RuledCarrier.lean:17-18) and ALL THREE PASS its seven clauses: holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/18-ants-exemplar.edn:66, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/19-mining-exemplar.edn:140, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:186, jointly holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:65. So the proviso is not open because a clause fails. IT IS OPEN BECAUSE THE THREE DIVIDE ON THE CLAUSE THE o3 RULING INTRODUCED. `addedByOrganise` is empty on ants (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AntsExemplar.lean:38) and on mining (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12MiningExemplar.lean:60), so on those two the ruled set-minus of `addedByOrganise` removes nothing and the no-bootstrap reading is INDISTINGUISHABLE THERE from the node-set reading it was ruled over; snatch is the only exemplar where the subtraction bites (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:141), and it is the one whose organised edge set does not reproduce its own run's (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:63-64). The question this entry registers is which of those facts the proviso asks about, and its arms are the five dispositions C582 prices.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :organise-exemplar-proviso], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "WHAT DISCHARGES THE EXEMPLAR PROVISO ON THE ARM-6 CARRIER RULING? Joe's ARM 6 ruling of 2026-09-07 attached a proviso -- verbatim, `the choice is exercised once on something real before being treated as validated` (holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:615) -- and the :organise-sorry ruling stages the Holes.lean edit behind it (holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:668; destination mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861, still at 61c4825dc3e373fd1b761b800814bf85f5770b88 and untouched). Three exemplars now stand at the ruled signature `RuledOrganiseType` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12RuledCarrier.lean:17-18) and ALL THREE PASS its seven clauses: holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/18-ants-exemplar.edn:66, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/19-mining-exemplar.edn:140, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:186, jointly holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:65. So the proviso is not open because a clause fails. IT IS OPEN BECAUSE THE THREE DIVIDE O