r/WarMachine/F12MiningExemplar.lean:60), so on those two the ruled set-minus of `addedByOrganise` removes nothing and the no-bootstrap reading is INDISTINGUISHABLE THERE from the node-set reading it was ruled over; snatch is the only exemplar where the subtraction bites (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:141), and it is the one whose organised edge set does not reproduce its own run's (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:63-64). The question this entry registers is which of those facts the proviso asks about, and its arms are the five dispositions C582 prices.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/organise-exemplar-proviso", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/U69"], :subjects [], :choice {:arms-not-all-run "2026-09-08, F12 slice 11. THESE FIVE ARMS ARE DISPOSITIONS OF A PROVISO, NOT CONSTRUCTIONS, so `run` does not mean the same thing here as in the sibling organise- entries: no arm has a module of its own and none is expected to. What WAS run is the measurement common to all five -- holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_proviso_sheet.bb into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn, twice and byte-identically, at sha256 d79f341e44dfe4de04208610c4f3fdb95a9dcd446ef6eae52d92c5f15289cead -- plus the three exemplar modules it reads. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED: :status is :observed-not-decided, there is no :ruling key, aif-equations.edn's other organise- entries are unchanged by this slice, and mathlib4 git log -1 on Holes.lean still reads 61c4825dc3e373fd1b761b800814bf85f5770b88 with the item-5 amendment staged.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED, and no arm is preferred. This entry does not say whether the proviso is met; it says what each disposition costs. It does not claim the five arms exhaustive -- they are the five C582 prices. It says nothing about the five other registered organise- choices, all of which are decided and none of which is reopened here; in particular it does NOT reopen :organise-o3-field, which is what arm four would do and arm four is not taken. It does not claim the three exemplars are a representative sample of anything: they are what F12 slices 4, 5 and 9 built. It does not claim the snatch divergence is a defect in the exemplar's transcription -- `organiseSnatch` uses `nodes` minus `addedByOrganise` for every input rather than an equality special to the recorded arguments (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SnatchExemplar.lean:100-108) -- nor that it is a defect in the ruling. It takes no position on the sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861, which is :organise-sorry, beyond recording that its staged edit waits on this proviso.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A RECORDED ROW WHOSE ORGANISED EDGES ARE FAST-FORWARDED OVER `nodes` MINUS `addedByOrganise` -- that is, a producer at futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:339 that computes the ruled reading rather than the node-set one. Under the current producer the two readings coincide precisely when `added` supplies no fast-forward endpoint, so no run of it can both change an edge under the ruled clause and reproduce its own edge set. Short of that, A SECOND JOINT OVER A DIFFERENT RECORDED SCENARIO is the cheapest thing that would move this entry: it would say whether snatch's one-of-ten is characteristic or particular to [:g4 :snatcher], and it is also where a row with non-empty `added` supplying no endpoint would be found if one exists, which is the only way arm three is reachable without touching the producer: five further rows carry edges and a moved precedence (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/23-snatch-joint.edn:162-168) and none of them has been driven through the ruled signature.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C582-F12-exemplar-proviso-sheet.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_proviso_sheet.bb; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/23-snatch-joint.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/18-ants-exemplar.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/19-mining-exemplar.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/17-ruled-carrier.edn", :question "WHAT DISCHARGES THE EXEMPLAR PROVISO ON THE ARM-6 CARRIER RULING? Joe's ARM 6 ruling of 2026-09-07 attached a proviso -- verbatim, `the choice is exercised once on something real before being treated as validated` (holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:615) -- and the :organise-sorry ruling stages the Holes.lean edit behind it (holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:668; destination mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861, still at 61c4825dc3e373fd1b761b800814bf85f5770b88 and untouched). Three exemplars now stand at the ruled signature `RuledOrganiseType` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12RuledCarrier.lean:17-18) and ALL THREE PASS its seven clauses: holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/18-ants-exemplar.edn:66, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/19-mining-exemplar.edn:140, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:186, jointly holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:65. So the proviso is not open because a clause fails. IT IS OPEN BECAUSE THE THREE DIVIDE ON THE CLAUSE THE o3 RULING INTRODUCED. `addedByOrganise` is empty on ants (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AntsExemplar.lean:38) and on mining (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12MiningExemplar.lean:60), so on those two the ruled set-minus of `addedByOrganise` removes nothing and the no-bootstrap reading is INDISTINGUISHABLE THERE from the node-set reading it was ruled over; snatch is the only exemplar where the subtraction bites (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:141), and it is the one whose organised edge set does not reproduce its own run's (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:63-64). The question this entry registers is which of those facts the proviso asks about, and its arms are the five dispositions C582 prices.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-08", :by "joe", :channel "session, claude-1 decision-sheet item 4; RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-08.md item 4", :decision "NEW DISPOSITION (f), not among the five priced arms: '(e) is the best of the given options, but I would propose instead (f) to use these 3 existing examples as as a source of inspiration to find a real working example not on the list. Otherwise tge inly way to pass is saticficing, rather that building a real reusable tool.' The proviso discharges when the arm-6 choice is exercised on a NATURALISTIC exemplar found using ants, mining and snatch as inspiration -- not on any of the three. Sequence ruled with it: 'Making snatch reproducible is a good warm up and bridge to the new naturalistic example.' The staged Holes.lean:861 amendment stays staged until (f) is exercised. The episode is owed to the paper (p4ng/futon-2026.tex, worklist :U69): 'This is a great example fir tge What problems are we solving paper and it should be written up there.' Verbatim, typos preserved.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-08", :measurement-that-separates-them "THE ARMS ARE SEPARATED BY ONE NUMBER AND ONE FACT ABOUT WHY. The number: at the ruled signature snatch's organised edge set is [[0 2]] against the ten the running code computes (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:40 and :38), and the two computations agree by three independent routes on the ten (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:12, :41 and :42) so the ten are not a transcription artefact. The fact: the nine dropped edges are exactly those with an endpoint in `addedByOrganise` (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:25-26). A QUALIFICATION THIS ENTRY OWES :organise-o3-field, whose :measurement-that-separates-them reads that no recorded cascade separates the node-set from the no-bootstrap reading and that the separating witness has to be constructed. That measurement was over the 52 O1-shaped cascades of the slice-1 census, and it stands as taken; the snatch row is not one of them. It is the JOINT of a recorded patterns row and a recorded exchange-first row, formed by slice 8 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/23-snatch-joint.edn:39, six rows all carrying edges and a moved precedence at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/23-snatch-joint.edn:162-168), against a census that had recorded the snatch record as carrying neither (the gap is written down at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/23-snatch-joint.edn:2-11, repointing holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/20-o4-edges-census.edn:238-249). So what is new is not that a recorded cascade separates the readings; it is that a joint of recorded rows does, and the o3-field entry's `the separating witness has to be CONSTRUCTED` is now true only of the census it was measured over.", :row :F12, :arms [{:arm :discharged-as-it-stands, :buys "IT IS THE ONLY ARM UNDER WHICH BOTH IMPLICATION CLAUSES ARE NON-VACUOUSLY WITNESSED. Of the seven ruled clauses only o2 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12RuledCarrier.lean:28-29) and o4 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12RuledCarrier.lean:33-37) are implications; the other five are unconditional equations or an equivalence (osel :23, oauth :24, oattr :25, o1 :26-27, o3 :30-32) about which nothing can be vacuous (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:133-140). o2's antecedent is satisfied by mining and snatch and vacuous on ants, o4's by ants and snatch and vacuous on mining (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:167-202) -- so it takes MORE THAN ONE exemplar to witness both, and this arm is the one that keeps them all.", :costs "OF THE THREE, ONE REPRODUCES ITS RUN'S EDGES, ONE DOES NOT, AND ON ONE THE QUESTION IS NOT MEASURABLE (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:63) -- and the one that does not is the only one that stresses the ruled subtraction. Ants is the not-measurable row and not by omission: `antsRepo.standsOn` is the empty relation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AntsExemplar.lean:22) and no organised edge is possible at all there, proved rather than assumed (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AntsExemplar.lean:72-74). So this arm discharges a proviso about exercising the ruled clause on two rows where that clause is inert and one where it diverges.", :run-by "F12 slice 10 (C582); futon2 560c99d5 (codex-2) + 7d0a8686 (review). No mathlib4 commit: no Lean was edited by the slice.", :what-it-is "Read the proviso as met by the three exemplars standing. All three are conformant at the ruled signature and the ruling is thereby exercised on something real; the staged amendment at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is released."} {:arm :discharged-by-the-subtraction-stressing-row-alone, :buys "THE EXERCISE IS ON A ROW WHOSE EVERY INPUT IS RECORDED, not on a constructed input. The repository is the 24 patterns and 26 authored edges the run used (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SnatchExemplar.lean:51-56 off futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:619-622), the precedence, acting order and score are the recorded before/after pairs (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SnatchExemplar.lean:64-98 off futon3:checks/snatch-cascade.edn:71-74, :84-92, :204, :210-219), all four O-laws hold on the row and organise reproduces the record (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:54-55). It is also the only exemplar that witnesses o2 and o4 together.", :costs "THE DESIGNATED ROW KEEPS 1 OF THE 10 EDGES THE RUNNING CODE COMPUTES FOR IT: `fastForward` over `nodes` minus `addedByOrganise` is the single pair 0 to 2 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:40) against the ten at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:38. The nine it drops are dropped for one reason, measured and not inferred: each has an endpoint in `addedByOrganise` (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/24-snatch-exemplar.edn:25-26), and the instance is exhibited in Lean for edge 18 to 22, which the full-node reading carries (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SnatchExemplar.lean:183-190) and the ruled subtraction refuses (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SnatchExemplar.lean:191-199). So this arm discharges the proviso on a ruled organise that does not compute what the running organise computes on the same inputs.", :run-by "F12 slice 10 (C582); futon2 560c99d5 (codex-2) + 7d0a8686 (review).", :what-it-is "Read the proviso as asking after the clause the ruling introduced, so only snatch counts: it is the one exemplar with non-empty `addedByOrganise`, {7, 11, 18, 22} at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SnatchExemplar.lean:41 from the recorded row at futon3:checks/snatch-cascade.edn:66-70."} {:arm :not-discharged-until-one-row-does-both, :buys "It is the reading under which the proviso does what it was written to do: the clause is exercised on something real AND the ruled function agrees with the recorded one on that something.", :costs "NO RUN OF THE EXISTING PRODUCER CAN SUPPLY SUCH A ROW, and this is a fact about the producer rather than about the corpus. The producer that populates the field computes its edges over the union it just added to: `:added-by-organise added` at futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:333 with `:edges (fast-forward nodes ...)` over `nodes = selected u added` at futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:330 and :339, and the O1-shaped constructor writes the field as a literal empty set and fast-forwards over `nodes` likewise (futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:412 and :415). So every recorded run is a node-set run BY CONSTRUCTION, and it agrees with the ruled subtraction exactly when `added` supplies no fast-forward endpoint. THAT LEAVES THE ARM REACHABLE ONLY IN ONE DIRECTION, and the distinction is worth stating because the sheet's criterion for `stresses the subtraction` is non-empty `addedByOrganise` (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:141) rather than a changed edge set. A row whose `added` is non-empty but supplies no endpoint would satisfy this arm on that criterion while the ruled clause changes nothing on it; a row whose `added` DOES supply an endpoint can never satisfy it, because the producer fast-forwards over the full node set and so drops exactly the edges the ruled subtraction drops. Whether any recorded row is of the first kind is NOT MEASURED HERE -- and if one is, it discharges the arm without exercising the clause, which is arm one's cost returning under another name. Getting a row of the second kind to reproduce means changing futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:339 to the ruled reading, which is a code change and not an exemplar. Three passing exemplars are set aside meanwhile (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:65).", :run-by "F12 slice 10 (C582); futon2 560c99d5 (codex-2) + 7d0a8686 (review).", :what-it-is "Hold the proviso unmet until one exemplar BOTH stresses the ruled subtraction AND reproduces its run's edge set. No exemplar in this set does both (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:63-64, :141)."} {:arm :discharged-with-o3-field-reopened, :buys "THE MEASUREMENT PUTS THE DIVERGENCE ENTIRELY IN o3 AND NOWHERE ELSE, and that is proved rather than argued: the full-node reading of the same row satisfies every ruled clause except no-bootstrap o3 (`organiseSnatchRecordedEdgesSansO3`, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SnatchExemplar.lean:172-181), so the carrier is not what the divergence indicts. It is also the arm that keeps the running Clojure and the Lean law one proposition.", :costs "A RULING OF 2026-09-07 IS REOPENED AFTER ITS EXEMPLAR WAS BUILT TO IT (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:227-234): the ruled carrier module states o3 in no-bootstrap form (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12RuledCarrier.lean:30-32) and all three exemplars are conformant at it. And the self-justification the ruling was taken to refuse is not hypothetical on this row -- it is what nine of the ten edges do -- so reopening reopens a cost that has now been paid once.", :run-by "F12 slice 10 (C582); futon2 560c99d5 (codex-2) + 7d0a8686 (review).", :what-it-is "Accept the arm-6 carrier as exercised and reopen :organise-o3-field instead, on the ground that the divergence is a fact about the o3 ruling and not about the carrier."} {:arm :discharged-conditionally-with-the-divergence-carried-open, :buys "It unblocks the one Holes.lean edit the :organise-sorry ruling stages, which pays the C176 contract regeneration once (holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:616), without asserting that the divergence is settled.", :costs "THE EDIT LANDS WHILE THE CLAUSE IT ENCODES IS STILL UNSETTLED ON SNATCH (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/25-proviso.edn:235-240). The amendment is an existence statement at the arm-6 signature, so what it existentially quantifies over is a conformance predicate whose o3 clause is the one under question; a later ruling on this entry would land inside a declaration that is no longer a sorry.", :run-by "F12 slice 10 (C582); futon2 560c99d5 (codex-2) + 7d0a8686 (review).", :what-it-is "Release the staged amendment at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 and carry the snatch divergence as a separate open row rather than as a condition on this one."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 1, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "O3 says organise's edges are exactly the authored fast-forwards. WHICH SET the fast-forward quantifies over is not determined by the theory and the sources disagree: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:909 quantifies over `.selected`, while the Clojure law futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:529 and the constructor that builds the edges futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:415 both quantify over `nodes`. On the C59 fixture (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:872) nodes = selected, so the two are one proposition and the file never had to choose; on the recorded zaif run they are not (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1034). Slice 2 recorded the disagreement and left it. This entry registers it with its arms named, each run.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :organise-o3-field], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "O3 says organise's edges are exactly the authored fast-forwards. WHICH SET the fast-forward quantifies over is not determined by the theory and the sources disagree: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:909 quantifies over `.selected`, while the Clojure law futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:529 and the constructor that builds the edges futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:415 both quantify over `nodes`. On the C59 fixture (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:872) nodes = selected, so the two are one proposition and the file never had to choose; on the recorded zaif run they are not (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1034). Slice 2 recorded the disagreement and left it. This entry registers it with its arms named, each run.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "O3 says organise's edges are exactly the authored fast-forwards. WHICH SET the fast-forward quantifies over is not determined by the theory and the sources disagree: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:909 quantifies over `.selected`, while the Clojure law futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:529 and the constructor that builds the edges futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:415 both quantify over `nodes`. On the C59 fixture (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:872) nodes = selected, so the two are one proposition and the file never had to choose; on the recorded zaif run they are not (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1034). Slice 2 recorded the disagreement and left it. This entry registers it with its arms named, each run.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/organise-o3-field", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:all-arms-run "2026-09-07, F12 slice 11. The two readings the sources carry were run by slices 2, 6 and 7; the third reading is run by slice 11 in mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED. What remains for a slice to run on this choice is nothing; what would change the measurement is a producer, named above.", :not-claimed "This entry says nothing about D1 (which CARRIER the four O-laws are stated of), about D2, about D3, or about the third-origin choice registered separately as :organise-third-origin. It takes no ruling: :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. The sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is neither discharged nor amended by it.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "a recorded cascade in which organise's own closure contributes a fast-forward endpoint. That needs a producer that populates :added-by-organise; futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:412 writes #{} as a literal and futon3:checks/construct_open_cascade.clj:145 reads that same value, so today there is none. The up-closure temperament named at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is the one that would (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:116 adds recorded vertex 26 through authored edge 6-26), and it is not what any recorded run ran.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C549-F12-o3-field-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/07-o3-field.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_o3_field_check.bb; holes/labs/wm-contract/C540-F12-zaif-cascadediff-witness.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C544-F12-organise-function-conformance.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C545-F12-admitting-arm.md", :question "O3 says organise's edges are exactly the authored fast-forwards. WHICH SET the fast-forward quantifies over is not determined by the theory and the sources disagree: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:909 quantifies over `.selected`, while the Clojure law futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:529 and the constructor that builds the edges futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:415 both quantify over `nodes`. On the C59 fixture (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:872) nodes = selected, so the two are one proposition and the file never had to choose; on the recorded zaif run they are not (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1034). Slice 2 recorded the disagreement and left it. This entry registers it with its arms named, each run.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-07", :by "joe", :channel "session, same walkthrough, item 6; Joe verbatim: 'it seems that you've got a clear ruling yourself for this latest question. And I'm happy to accept your arm three selection for this one.'", :consequence "The slice-4 exemplar states arm 6's O3 clause in no-bootstrap form -- a restatement using the slice-11 predicate (F12O3FieldArm.lean:16), not new mathematics. The arm-6 module as built took the node-set reading precisely to avoid pre-deciding this choice; that neutrality is now spent by ruling.", :decision "ARM 3, :over-the-nodes-organise-did-not-add (the no-bootstrap reading). At the ruled CascadeDiff carrier (:organise-carrier arm 6) the set is selected union admittedBy, which contains both endpoints of the recorded edge 18-19, so the recorded run stays a witness; and the node-set reading's self-justification (edge 26-25 through organise's own additions, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:101) is refused by construction. The selected reading's virtue survives: no edge is justified by anything organise did itself, because admitted nodes are the policy's contribution.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :measurement-that-separates-them "NO RECORDED CASCADE SEPARATES THE NODE-SET READING FROM THE NO-BOOTSTRAP READING, and the reason is the constructor rather than the runs. Recomputed 2026-09-07 by holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_o3_field_check.bb into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/07-o3-field.edn: over the 52 O1-shaped cascades in the nine records slice 1's census names, 0 carry an edge running through a node organise added, which is exactly the condition under which the two readings differ. Eight cascades DO carry a non-empty :added-by-organise, all eight in futon3:checks/snatch-cascade.edn, and in all eight that set is DISJOINT from the cascade's own :nodes and the cascade carries no :edges -- so the field there does not denote O1's second origin and cannot exercise the question. The sole producer of an O1-shaped cascade fixes the field to a literal empty set (futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:412), so no run of it can separate them: the separating witness has to be CONSTRUCTED, and slice 11 constructs it in Lean. THE SELECTED READING, by contrast, is separated by the recorded data alone (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1034).", :row :F12, :arms [{:arm :over-the-selected-set, :buys "organise cannot justify an edge by anything it did itself: the endpoints are the caller's, so the law is not self-referential in any reading. It is also the only one of the three that needs no field the declared carrier lacks.", :costs "REFUTED ON THE RECORDED RUN, which is the strongest fact any arm of this choice carries. The one edge the zaif run records runs 18-19 and both endpoints were ADMITTED rather than selected, so fast-forward over the 11 selected is empty and the reading contradicts the record (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1034). At the function carrier the same cost is a theorem about every conformant implementation, not about one: no conformant f returns the recorded edge on the recorded selected input (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:141), and the same implementation does return it once all twenty nodes are supplied (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:149) -- so it is the missing origin and not the edge law that puts the run out of reach. At the admitting carrier the reading leaves the recorded organised edge set EMPTY (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:262).", :run-by "F12 slices 2, 6 and 7; mathlib4 61c4825dc3, 0c5745c39e, 0691f74e48, 7d4f6ffca3, acb4e95bcf", :what-it-is "fast-forward over the set organise was HANDED -- `.selected` at the value carrier (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:909), `sel` at the function carrier (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:23). This is what the Lean file has said since before the row opened."} {:arm :over-the-node-set, :buys "it is the only reading the recorded run satisfies. O3 is proved of the zaif fixture in this form (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1014), and it agrees with the code that produced the record, so the Lean law and its Clojure mirror are one proposition rather than two.", :costs "ORGANISE MAY USE ITS OWN ADDITIONS AS FAST-FORWARD ENDPOINTS, so the law is partly self-justifying: organise adds a node, authors an edge through it, and O3 confirms the edge because the node organise added is in `nodes`. Constructed and machine-checked at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:101 -- on the recorded inputs a node-set-conformant implementation (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:72) returns the edge 26-25, and BOTH its endpoints are nodes organise itself added (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:90). The cost is not visible on any recorded run: see :measurement-that-separates-them.", :run-by "F12 slices 2, 6 and 11; mathlib4 61c4825dc3, 0c5745c39e, 1e6625bbf6", :what-it-is "fast-forward over everything the cascade ended up containing -- `nodes`. This is what the running Clojure does: futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:529 states the law over `nodes` and futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:415 builds the edges the same way."} {:arm :over-the-nodes-organise-did-not-add, :buys "the self-justification is closed by construction: the implementation that exhibits it is node-set conformant and NOT no-bootstrap conformant, refuted on the recorded inputs at the edge 26-25 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:119), because outside its organise-added field precisely the caller's selection remains (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:81). And it costs the recorded run NOTHING at the value carrier: `addedByOrganise` is empty in both recorded fixtures (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:25, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:38), so the O3 already proved of the zaif fixture IS its no-bootstrap O3 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:52), on an edge relation shown inhabited rather than assumed (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:186).", :costs "THE READING IS ONE PROPOSITION WITH TWO CONTENTS, and which it has is decided by D1 rather than by this choice. At CascadeDiff the field is `selected ∪ admittedBy`, which is the whole recorded node set (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:46), and the recorded edge 18-19 is inside it (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:200). At the function carrier `Cascade` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-35) has no `admittedBy` field, so the same reading is just the caller's selection and NO conformant function returns the recorded edge on the recorded selected input (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:172) -- the selected arm's cost, inherited. Stated against overstating it: on the recorded selected input the no-bootstrap relation is EMPTY (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:128), so the separation above is checked against a relation shown inhabited on a constructed input (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:162) and not on a recorded one.", :run-by "F12 slice 11 (C549); mathlib4 1e6625bbf6 + 28c518612a", :what-it-is "the no-bootstrap reading: fast-forward over the nodes that came in from OUTSIDE organise -- `nodes \\ addedByOrganise` at the function carrier (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12O3FieldArm.lean:16) and `selected ∪ admittedBy` at CascadeDiff. It refuses the node-set arm's self-justification without giving up the admitted origin the selected arm gives up."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "O4 says that where the precedence changed, the acting order or the score changed with it (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538). Exercising it needs a cascade two of whose members carry rules, and no recorded run has one: the maximum rule-carrying member count over the nine records is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:265). Reaching two therefore means changing the apparatus after the law is already written -- either a construction over a tension chosen so the find selects two rule-bearing patterns, or a new play-grain encoding of a THEN a member already carries -- or refusing both and leaving O4 unexercised. The zaif rule table's whole standing is that it was committed before the run and not fitted to it, and its STATED un-fitting guard covers fitting to a WIN: `a table written to make the cascade win would not carry rules for patterns the cascade does not contain` (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:53-57), computed by membership (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:479-480) and failing only when that collection is empty (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:585). It says nothing about fitting to a LAW, which is the intervention this question is about. This is D3, raised at C541 section 4 with two routes and the refusal. This entry registers all three with what each is measured to cost.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "O4 says that where the precedence changed, the acting order or the score changed with it (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538). Exercising it needs a cascade two of whose members carry rules, and no recorded run has one: the maximum rule-carrying member count over the nine records is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:265). Reaching two therefore means changing the apparatus after the law is already written -- either a construction over a tension chosen so the find selects two rule-bearing patterns, or a new play-grain encoding of a THEN a member already carries -- or refusing both and leaving O4 unexercised. The zaif rule table's whole standing is that it was committed before the run and not fitted to it, and its STATED un-fitting guard covers fitting to a WIN: `a table written to make the cascade win would not carry rules for patterns the cascade does not contain` (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:53-57), computed by membership (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:479-480) and failing only when that collection is empty (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:585). It says nothing about fitting to a LAW, which is the intervention this question is about. This is D3, raised at C541 section 4 with two routes and the refusal. This entry registers all three with what each is measured to cost.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "O4 says that where the precedence changed, the acting order or the score changed with it (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538). Exercising it needs a cascade two of whose members carry rules, and no recorded run has one: the maximum rule-carrying member count over the nine records is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:265). Reaching two therefore means changing the apparatus after the law is already written -- either a construction over a tension chosen so the find selects two rule-bearing patterns, or a new play-grain encoding of a THEN a member already carries -- or refusing both and leaving O4 unexercised. The zaif rule table's whole standing is that it was committed before the run and not fitted to it, and its STATED un-fitting guard covers fitting to a WIN: `a table written to make the cascade win would not carry rules for patterns the cascade does not contain` (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:53-57), computed by membership (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:479-480) and failing only when that collection is empty (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:585). It says nothing about fitting to a LAW, which is the intervention this question is about. This is D3, raised at C541 section 4 with two routes and the refusal. This entry registers all three with what each is measured to cost.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:all-arms-run "2026-09-07, F12 slice 18. All three arms C541 section 4's D3 names -- the two after-the-law routes and the refusal -- carry measured :buys and :costs, each run by slice 15 (futon2 652f4805) with its plant read back before the worker that measured it. Arm B additionally carries slice 16's measurements at the three non-primary denominators (futon2 23f22dc5). One gap is named rather than hidden and is recorded under :what-would-change-the-measurement: arm A was measured at the primary denominator only. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is still :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED: :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. This entry does not say that an after-the-law encoding is admissible or that it is not; it says what each of the three answers is measured to cost. It does NOT restate the un-fitting guard: C541 section 4 says that restatement is owed IF the answer is yes, and no answer is taken here, so the guard stands as written at futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:53-57. It takes no position on the gate's :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then failure, which belongs to whoever owns that table. It says nothing about D1 (which carrier the four O-laws are stated of, registered as :organise-carrier), about D2 (which denominator O4 is read over, registered as :organise-o4-denominator), about the third origin (:organise-third-origin), about the O3 field question (:organise-o3-field), or about the sorry (:organise-sorry), which at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is still neither discharged nor amended. Registering this choice ran no machine and wrote no source file: the arms were run by slice 15, which made every plant in a temporary copy and left futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj and every file under futon3:checks/ unmodified.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A RECORDED RUN IN WHICH TWO RULE-BEARING PATTERNS BOTH ACT, PRODUCED BY THE GATE RATHER THAN BY A PLANT -- which would settle D3 by making it moot rather than by answering it, since every number above other than arm C's comes from a temporary copy. That needs the THEN-correspondence failure repaired by whoever owns the rule table, 3 of 4 at HEAD (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:264-272). Short of that, two measurements would move this entry: arm A run at the paired, transcript and full-play denominators, which no artifact carries (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:109 reads the primary arm alone), and a construction on which the two member-carried rules contend INSIDE the primary cohort, which neither arm supplies -- arm A gives zero primary contentions (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:12) and arm B gives three, all outside it (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:30).", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C553-F12-d3-encoding.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj; holes/labs/wm-contract/C541-F12-o4-reachability.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C554-F12-d2-denominator.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn", :question "O4 says that where the precedence changed, the acting order or the score changed with it (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538). Exercising it needs a cascade two of whose members carry rules, and no recorded run has one: the maximum rule-carrying member count over the nine records is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:265). Reaching two therefore means changing the apparatus after the law is already written -- either a construction over a tension chosen so the find selects two rule-bearing patterns, or a new play-grain encoding of a THEN a member already carries -- or refusing both and leaving O4 unexercised. The zaif rule table's whole standing is that it was committed before the run and not fitted to it, and its STATED un-fitting guard covers fitting to a WIN: `a table written to make the cascade win would not carry rules for patterns the cascade does not contain` (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:53-57), computed by membership (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:479-480) and failing only when that collection is empty (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:585). It says nothing about fitting to a LAW, which is the intervention this question is about. This is D3, raised at C541 section 4 with two routes and the refusal. This entry registers all three with what each is measured to cost.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-07", :by "joe", :channel "session, same walkthrough, item 8; Joe verbatim: 'the cascades are meant to correspond to production rule systems... patterns should have THEN statements available, which are authored and which can be adapted into production rules through an attested interpretation, or, if it's not attested, a documented interpretation... We're not tuning to a win; we're tuning to a law, or a structural requirement of how the system works. At the same time, we do need to exercise that and come up with some examples.'", :consequence "O4 becomes exercisable under the ruled split denominator (:organise-o4-denominator arm 5). An examples excursion is commissioned alongside the slice-4 exemplar: construct at least one cascade with two rule-bearing members from the committed library, with each rule's interpretation attested or documented. Same evidentiary shape as D1 and the carrier proviso: accepted as direction, validated by computed examples.", :decision "ARM B, :encode-a-then-a-member-already-carries, ADMISSIBLE AS MARKED INSTRUMENTATION, with three riders. (1) Provenance marking is the rule: any planted encoding is labeled constructed-instrumentation in every artifact that reads it and is never reported as a corpus fact. (2) The owed guard restatement (C541 section 4) is to be written: the un-fitting guard's stated scope extends to say when fitting-to-a-law is admissible -- encoding an AUTHORED THEN a member ALREADY CARRIES adds no content the library did not commit before the run. (3) The real fix is generative, per Joe: authored THENs adapt into production rules through attested (or documented) interpretation, and two-rule cascades should be constructible from the library as it now stands -- the fresh why/how edges and the problems sub-library included -- so examples tuned to this project's own work are the path that eventually moots the plant. The :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then table failure still belongs to its owner, but waiting on it is not the plan.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :measurement-that-separates-them "THE ARMS SEPARATE ON WHETHER O4 BECOMES EXERCISABLE, NOT ON WHETHER IT BECOMES TRUE -- no arm produces a true O4 at the denominator the gate grades. Arm A moves the carrying count 1 -> 2 and leaves the primary verdict false with zero contending primary rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:2, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:5, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:12); arm B moves the status :not-exercised -> :exercised-false (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:136, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:15); arm C leaves zero (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:246). THE ONE PLANT THAT DOES MOVE THE PRIMARY VERDICT TO TRUE IS A NEGATIVE CONTROL, NOT AN ARM: broadening an existing member-carried rule so it is live on primary rounds gives :primary-o4-true (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:256-259, planted at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:160-165), and it is in the control set precisely because it is the edit that would make the law pass. So on everything measured, D3 and D2 are not independent: an affirmative D3 buys a TRUE O4 only if D2 also reads the law off a denominator wider than primary, where arm B gives true three times over (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1396, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1562, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:802). Three further controls fix what each measurement is sensitive to, each plant read back before its worker ran (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:35-40, hard-failing at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:210-216): renaming the fifth rule to a nonmember returns O4 to :not-exercised (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:248-251), killing its antecedent takes it from 102 live rounds to none (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:252-255), and fitting every rule id to a member fires the un-fitting guard (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:260-263).", :row :F12, :arms [{:arm :construct-a-cascade-that-selects-two-rule-bearing-patterns, :buys "THE PRECONDITION, AND ONLY THAT. The maximum rule-carrying member count moves 1 -> 2 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:2 against the premise at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:265), so slice 3's :not-a-witness blocker -- no constructor selected both patterns, so there is no cascade for an O4 row to be OF -- is the one thing this arm removes.", :costs "IT BUYS NO WITNESS. Over the same 29 primary rounds the primary O4 is still FALSE: the acting order does not change and the score stands at 14 -> 14, with zero contending primary rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:4-8, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:12). Nothing else moves either -- the cohort still carries 103 rounds and the primary denominator still 29 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:10-11). So answering D3 in the affirmative on this route leaves O4 exactly where it was unless D2 moves off the primary denominator too, which is a second choice (:organise-o4-denominator) and not this one. UNMEASURED AND NOT GUESSED: this arm was run at the primary denominator alone (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:109), so what it would give at paired, transcript or full play is not recorded anywhere -- unlike the arm below, which slice 16 did carry to the other three.", :run-by "F12 slice 15 (C553); futon2 652f4805", :what-it-is "C541 section 4's first route -- change WHAT THE FIND SELECTS. Measured by planting the second rule-bearing pattern, war-machine/ambient-pattern-retrieval, into the marginal-gain-floor arm of a TEMPORARY COPY of the cascade record and bumping that run's member count, then re-running slice 3's reachability report against the copy (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:89-104, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:106-121). The plant is read back and cross-checked against the member count before the arm is measured (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:102-104)."} {:arm :encode-a-then-a-member-already-carries, :buys "IT IS THE ONLY ARM THAT MAKES O4 EXERCISABLE AT ALL. The primary O4 status moves :not-exercised -> :exercised-false (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:136, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:15, exercised? true at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:238); the fifth rule is live on 102 rounds including all 29 primary ones (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:32-134, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:137-166); and the two member-carried rules contend on rounds 3, 4 and 7 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:16-28), the first contention between two rules the cascade actually carries -- slice 3's contention at the same rounds dropped the membership filter deliberately, because only one member carried a rule and the gate's own contention over members is empty (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn:335-337, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn:186). AT EVERY DENOMINATOR OTHER THAN PRIMARY THE SAME ENCODING GIVES O4 TRUE: paired, contention at round 7, score 15 -> 15, true by the acting-order disjunct alone (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1389, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1394-1398); transcript, contention at 3, 4 and 7 with the score moving 20 -> 19 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1555, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1560-1564, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1878-1879); full play, the same contention with the score at 21 -> 20 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:794-804, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1119-1120). Every non-primary TRUE that :organise-o4-denominator records as its Arm B rests on THIS arm being admitted.", :costs "THE VERDICT IT MAKES POSSIBLE IS FALSE WHERE THE GATE GRADES. At the primary denominator the precedence exchange [8 3] -> [3 8] changes neither the acting order -- the before and after vectors are identical, each 29 entries of the fifth rule alone, the other member-carried rule firing on no primary round (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:178-207, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:208-237, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:239-240) -- nor the score, 15 -> 15 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:241-242), so O4 does not hold (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:31) and all three contentions fall outside the cohort (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:30). AND THE STATED UN-FITTING GUARD DOES NOT FIRE ON IT, which is a cost and not a clearance: three rules remain outside the cascade after the plant (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:167-170, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:176) and the guard fails only on an empty collection (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:585), so the one intervention D3 is about passes a guard written about a different one. That the guard CAN fire is checked rather than assumed -- fitting every rule id to a cascade member empties the collection and fires it (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:260-263). This is why an affirmative answer on this route owes the restatement C541 section 4 names, and the restatement is not written here.", :run-by "F12 slice 15 (C553); futon2 652f4805. Slice 16 (C554; futon2 23f22dc5) then measured THE SAME ENCODING at the other three denominators, using this arm's rule value rather than copying it (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:190-192, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:24-31).", :what-it-is "C541 section 4's second route -- change WHAT A SELECTED MEMBER CAN DO. A fifth rule is added to the play-grain rule table encoding the authored THEN of aif/status-gated-belief-update, a pattern the cascade ALREADY carries, citing the span futon3:library/aif/status-gated-belief-update.flexiarg:26-30; the plant goes into a temporary copy of the gate placed first on the worker's classpath and is read back before the worker runs (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:24-33, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:35-40, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:42-53, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:146-148)."} {:arm :refuse-both-after-the-law-interventions, :buys "the rule table keeps the property its whole standing rests on -- committed before the run, not touched to make a law testable -- and it is the only arm under which no number in this entry comes from a plant.", :costs "ZERO EXERCISE, MEASURED AND NOT ASSUMED: across the same nine cascade records the runs exercising O4 number 0 and the row list is empty (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:245-246), recomputed by walking every :o4 map in every record rather than read off a summary field (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:123-132). AND THE ROUTE THAT WOULD PRODUCE AN EXERCISE WITHOUT A PLANT IS CLOSED AT HEAD, independently of this choice: require-pass! (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:565) aborts with :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then for 3 of 4 rules, the finding built at futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:579-582 and thrown at futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:589-591, recomputed into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn:264-272. So refusing both arms is not a wait with a known end: it is a wait on a rule table that is not :F12's to repair.", :run-by "F12 slice 15 (C553); futon2 652f4805 (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d3_encoding_check.clj:123-132)", :what-it-is "take neither route: witness O4 only from what the corpus already records, and leave it unexercised until a run the gate itself produces exercises it."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "O4 is a three-way disjunction -- the precedence did not change, OR the acting order changed, OR the score changed (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538) -- and it does not say WHICH ROUNDS the acting order and the score are read over. The gate's agreement number is computed over the primary cohort because a comparison needs a determined oracle label, but O4 makes no reference to an oracle: an acting order is something the cascade does whether or not the record can grade it. The denominator is therefore free, and it is not a free hand that leaves the verdict alone -- on the recorded run one and the same precedence exchange over one and the same rule pair gives O4 FALSE over the 29 primary rounds and TRUE over the 49 paired and the 102 transcript rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4903-4907, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4976-4980, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5089-5093). This is D2, raised at C541 section 4 with three options. This entry registers those options with what each is measured to cost, and adds the fourth the checker ran.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :organise-o4-denominator], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "O4 is a three-way disjunction -- the precedence did not change, OR the acting order changed, OR the score changed (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538) -- and it does not say WHICH ROUNDS the acting order and the score are read over. The gate's agreement number is computed over the primary cohort because a comparison needs a determined oracle label, but O4 makes no reference to an oracle: an acting order is something the cascade does whether or not the record can grade it. The denominator is therefore free, and it is not a free hand that leaves the verdict alone -- on the recorded run one and the same precedence exchange over one and the same rule pair gives O4 FALSE over the 29 primary rounds and TRUE over the 49 paired and the 102 transcript rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4903-4907, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4976-4980, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5089-5093). This is D2, raised at C541 section 4 with three options. This entry registers those options with what each is measured to cost, and adds the fourth the checker ran.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "O4 is a three-way disjunction -- the precedence did not change, OR the acting order changed, OR the score changed (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538) -- and it does not say WHICH ROUNDS the acting order and the score are read over. The gate's agreement number is computed over the primary cohort because a comparison needs a determined oracle label, but O4 makes no reference to an oracle: an acting order is something the cascade does whether or not the record can grade it. The denominator is therefore free, and it is not a free hand that leaves the verdict alone -- on the recorded run one and the same precedence exchange over one and the same rule pair gives O4 FALSE over the 29 primary rounds and TRUE over the 49 paired and the 102 transcript rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4903-4907, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4976-4980, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5089-5093). This is D2, raised at C541 section 4 with three options. This entry registers those options with what each is measured to cost, and adds the fourth the checker ran.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/organise-o4-denominator", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:all-arms-run "2026-09-07, F12 slice 20, registering the run slice 19 made (futon2 3c0ad833). ALL FIVE ARMS NOW CARRY MEASURED :buys AND :costs. Slice 17 registered four and named the fifth as unrun together with what running it would take -- one more denominator spec reading the two fields from two round sets (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:20-23, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:44-71) -- and slice 19 built exactly that (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:88-138) and ran it on both constructions, the acceptance run printing :problems [] (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6157). THIS KEY REPLACES :arms-not-all-run, WHICH SLICE 19'S OWN RUN MADE FALSE and which C555 named as the stale claim rather than leaving it to be found. The fifth arm's verdicts are pinned like the other arms' so a later run reports a move instead of silently restating today's numbers (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:376-379), and three plants each move the acceptance run off PASS: reading the score over the acting-order round set (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:380-387), giving the identity collapse a paired order side (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:388-392), and making the forced-empty side non-empty (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:98-101, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:393-395). STILL NO ARM IS PREFERRED and no verdict is taken on O4 itself; :status remains :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED: :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. This entry does not say O4 holds or that it fails -- every verdict above is a verdict AT a denominator, and the entry's content is that they differ. It says nothing about D1 (which carrier the four O-laws are stated of, registered as :organise-carrier), about D3 (whether an O4 witness may be reached by an encoding written after the law, registered as :organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding), about the third origin (:organise-third-origin), about the O3 field question (:organise-o3-field), or about the sorry (:organise-sorry), which at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is still neither discharged nor amended. It takes no position on the gate's :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then failure, which belongs to whoever owns that table. Registering this choice ran no machine and wrote no source file: the first four arms were run by slice 16 and the fifth by slice 19, and this entry only records them. NOR IS THE FIFTH ARM PREFERRED BY BEING LAST: five measured arms are five verdicts AT a reading.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A RECORDED RUN IN WHICH TWO RULE-BEARING PATTERNS BOTH ACT -- which would move every arm's numbers off a plant and onto the corpus. The maximum rule-carrying member count on any recorded run is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn), and the gate that would produce such a run does not pass at HEAD: require-pass! aborts with :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then for three of four rules, with :file-exists? and :pattern-id-matches-path? true for all four and :span-inside-the-then-block? false for three (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:579-582, thrown at futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:589-591, recomputed into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6105-6156), and that rule table is not :F12's to repair. Until then, whether a plant may supply the second rule at all is D3's question, measured by slice 15 into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/10-d3-encoding.edn and registered by slice 18 as :organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding, whose Arm B is where every non-primary TRUE recorded above comes from.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C554-F12-d2-denominator.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C555-F12-d2-fifth-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj; holes/labs/wm-contract/C541-F12-o4-reachability.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C553-F12-d3-encoding.md", :question "O4 is a three-way disjunction -- the precedence did not change, OR the acting order changed, OR the score changed (futon3:checks/find_organise.clj:531-538) -- and it does not say WHICH ROUNDS the acting order and the score are read over. The gate's agreement number is computed over the primary cohort because a comparison needs a determined oracle label, but O4 makes no reference to an oracle: an acting order is something the cascade does whether or not the record can grade it. The denominator is therefore free, and it is not a free hand that leaves the verdict alone -- on the recorded run one and the same precedence exchange over one and the same rule pair gives O4 FALSE over the 29 primary rounds and TRUE over the 49 paired and the 102 transcript rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4903-4907, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4976-4980, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5089-5093). This is D2, raised at C541 section 4 with three options. This entry registers those options with what each is measured to cost, and adds the fourth the checker ran.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-07", :by "joe", :channel "session, same walkthrough, item 7; Joe verbatim: 'Arm 5 looks like the right one here... Arm 5 seems to allow not only a complex orchestration across those layers, but also some opportunity for tuning and learning at the meta level what works. It seems as though Arm 5 gets us unstuck now and creates the possibility for further development later. So let's go with that.'", :consequence "The slice-4 exemplar should include the separating construction if reachable -- a run whose transcript acting order does NOT move while its score does -- since arm 5 is currently observationally equivalent to the transcript arm on every construction built (:construction-can-separate-them? false, runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn). This ruling does not decide :organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding: whether the plant that makes O4 exercisable is admissible remains open, and every non-primary TRUE measured so far rests on it.", :decision "ARM 5, :split-acting-order-over-transcript-score-over-primary (C541 section 4 option (i) AS WRITTEN): the score is read over the rounds the gate grades (a score is evidence against a determined oracle label), the acting order over every transcript round (an acting order is something the cascade does whether or not the record can grade it). Joe's framing: the nesting denominators are an opportunity to learn -- escalating scales of nothing-has-changed become an escalating chain of signals, up to 'nothing has changed over this very long epoch, shut down and wait for someone to get us unstuck'; the split preserves that layered structure for tuning rather than collapsing it into one cohort.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :measurement-that-separates-them "THE DENOMINATOR ALONE DECIDES THE VERDICT, AND NO RECORDED RUN EXERCISES O4 AT ALL. Over the nine cascade records slice 1's census names, ZERO carry a run in which both rule-bearing patterns are members (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5379), so every number above other than the HEAD baseline comes from a planted fifth rule. What separates the arms is that the round sets NEST -- primary inside paired inside transcript (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5323-5324) -- and the contention lies exactly in the differences: round 7 in paired-minus-primary, rounds 3 and 4 in transcript-minus-paired, on the baseline measure (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5319-5320) and on Arm B's (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1217-1218) alike. On Arm B, with one precedence exchange over one rule pair, the four single-denominator arms return FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE in denominator order (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1290, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1396, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1562, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:802), each recomputed by fo/o4-precedence-governance rather than read from a stored field (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:71). ONE READING CAUTION THE ARTIFACT CARRIES: the baseline arms and the Arm-B worker report contention under DIFFERENT KEYS -- :rounds-on-which-the-fired-rule-differs and :contending-rounds -- and the floor records which one it read rather than assuming they are one measure (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5318, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1216, key taken as an argument at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:78-94). WHAT THE ARMS CANNOT SAY, AND WHAT ONE CONTROL SLICE 19 RAN DOES: the transcript arm's TRUE fires BOTH disjuncts -- :acting-order-changed? true with the score moving 83 -> 81 at HEAD (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5087-5090, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5303-5305) and the same pair on Arm B with 20 -> 19 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1555, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1562-1564, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1878-1879) -- so it cannot say whether the score alone would carry it. The MIRROR of the fifth arm -- acting order over the 29 primary rounds, score over the 102 transcript ones -- gives O4 TRUE on both constructions where the primary arm gives FALSE, on :disjuncts-that-hold [:score-changed] with the acting order unmoved (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:7447-7450 with scores 83 -> 81 at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:7514-7515; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6686-6688, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6720 with scores 20 -> 19 at holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6890-6891), and :construction-can-separate-them? true on both (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6905-6912, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6170-6179). So the primary arm's FALSE depends on BOTH fields being read over the primary rounds, not on the acting order alone. THE MIRROR IS NOT A SIXTH ARM AND IS NOT OFFERED AS ONE: C541 section 4 names three options, nobody proposed this reading, and it was run to test whether a split can separate a verdict at all (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:180). Whether a reading no one proposed belongs among D2's options is not a slice's to say.", :row :F12, :arms [{:arm :over-the-primary-rounds, :buys "the O4 verdict and the gate's agreement number are read over the same rounds, and it is the only arm all of whose rounds carry a determined oracle label. It is also the smallest denominator, so a TRUE here would be the strongest of the four.", :costs "O4 IS FALSE HERE ON BOTH CONSTRUCTIONS ANYONE HAS BUILT, and false for the same reason each time -- the contention is real and lies outside the cohort. At HEAD the exchange leaves the acting order unchanged and the score at 14 -> 14 over the 29 rounds, with no round on which the fired rule differs (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4901, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4904-4907, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4971-4972). On Arm B -- slice 15's fifth rule, encoding the authored THEN of aif/status-gated-belief-update, the one construction on which two member-carried rules DO contend -- the primary cohort still carries zero contending rounds and the score still stands at 15 -> 15, so O4 is false again (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1283, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1288-1290, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1387-1388), on a row whose precedence really did move from [1 2] to [2 1] (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1385-1386). The contention it excludes is one round away: round 7 lies in paired and not in primary and carries contention on both measures (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5319, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1217).", :run-by "F12 slices 3 and 16 (C541 section 2, C554); futon2 23f22dc5", :what-it-is "read both the acting order and the score over the rounds the gate grades -- the primary cohort, `reach/primary?` (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:21), 29 rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4906)."} {:arm :over-the-paired-rounds, :buys "THE SMALLEST DENOMINATOR ON WHICH O4 HOLDS, and it holds on both constructions. At HEAD the fired rule differs on round 7 and the score moves 34 -> 33, so both the acting-order and the score disjunct fire (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4974-4980, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5084-5085). On Arm B the acting order changes at round 7 with the score unmoved at 15 -> 15 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1389, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1394-1398, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1553-1554), so on that construction the verdict rests on the acting-order disjunct ALONE -- which is the disjunct the question is about.", :costs "IT IS TWENTY ROUNDS WIDER THAN THE COHORT THE GATE GRADES and the question does not name it: 20 of its 49 rounds are outside primary (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1219-1220), and C541 section 4 offered primary, transcript-and-primary split, and full play. Choosing it means answering D2 with a denominator no one proposed, which is a defensible answer and not a free one. Its TRUE at HEAD is also the weakest of the three baseline verdicts in one respect that is measured rather than argued: on Arm B its score does not move, so the whole verdict is the acting order at a single round (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1394-1395).", :run-by "F12 slices 3 and 16 (C541 section 2, C554); futon2 23f22dc5", :what-it-is "read both over the rounds the record pairs, `g/paired?` (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:22), 49 rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4979). NOT ONE OF THE THREE OPTIONS C541 SECTION 4 NAMED -- it is a denominator the checker ran, and it is registered because it is the cheapest arm on which O4 is exercised and true."} {:arm :over-the-transcript-rounds, :buys "the widest measured contention and both disjuncts firing on both constructions: at HEAD the fired rule differs on rounds 3, 4 and 7 and the score moves 83 -> 81 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5087-5093, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5303-5304); on Arm B contention at the same rounds 3, 4 and 7 with the score moving 20 -> 19 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1555, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1560-1564, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1878-1879). It is the only denominator on which the score disjunct fires under BOTH constructions, so the verdict does not hang on one disjunct.", :costs "73 OF ITS 102 ROUNDS ARE OUTSIDE THE COHORT THE GATE GRADES -- the round sets nest, primary inside paired inside transcript (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5323-5324), and the transcript arm admits 102 where primary admits 29 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5092, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4906). What it buys in exercise it pays for in rounds no agreement number covers. And its verdict disagrees with the primary arm's on every construction measured, which is not a defect of the arm but is the whole content of the question: the two contending rounds it adds over paired are 3 and 4 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5320, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1218).", :run-by "F12 slices 3 and 16 (C541 section 2 option (i) AS RUN, C554); futon2 23f22dc5", :what-it-is "read both over every round carrying a transcript, `:has-transcript?` (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:23), 102 rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5092). THIS IS NOT C541's OPTION (i) AS WRITTEN, which split the two readings; the split is the fifth arm below, run by slice 19."} {:arm :over-the-full-play, :buys "no round is excluded, so the verdict needs no cohort argument at all -- the one thing none of the other three arms can say. On Arm B O4 holds with contention at rounds 3, 4 and 7 and the score moving 21 -> 20 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:794-804, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1119-1120).", :costs "IT IS MEASURED ON ONE CONSTRUCTION ONLY. The HEAD baseline reports three arms -- primary, paired, transcript -- and carries no full-play key (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4901, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:4974, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5087), so what this arm does at HEAD is unmeasured and the entry does not guess it. It also adds exactly ONE round over the transcript denominator, 103 against 102 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:909, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1668), and on Arm B that round changes nothing: the contending rounds are 3, 4 and 7 under both (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:796, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:1556). So on everything measured it is the transcript arm plus a round, and it is registered separately because C541 named it and because its cohort argument is different, not because a number separates it.", :run-by "F12 slice 16 (C541 section 2 option (iii), C554); futon2 23f22dc5", :what-it-is "state O4 of the whole play and report the denominator with it -- every round in the record, 103 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:909), computed by the arm-B worker rather than as one of the three denominator specs (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:20-23)."} {:arm :split-acting-order-over-transcript-score-over-primary, :buys "NOTHING OVER THE TRANSCRIPT ARM ON EITHER CONSTRUCTION, which is measured rather than predicted. O4 HOLDS ON BOTH and on the same single disjunct: at HEAD :o4-holds? true with :disjuncts-that-hold [:acting-order-changed] and the primary score unmoved at 14 -> 14 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:7021-7023, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:7233-7234); on Arm B the same, with the primary score at 15 -> 15 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6187, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6293, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6536-6537). So its TRUE rests on the acting-order disjunct alone, which is the transcript arm's own disjunct, and the score half of the split contributes nothing to either verdict. WHAT IT DOES BUY IS A STATEMENT AND NOT A NUMBER: the score is read over the 29 rounds the gate grades, so the objection that a score needs a determined oracle label is answered without moving the acting order off the transcript -- which is exactly the point C541 section 4 wrote the option to take.", :costs "IT IS THE TRANSCRIPT ARM'S VERDICT WITH A NARROWER SCORE, AND NO CONSTRUCTION ANYONE HAS BUILT CAN TELL THE TWO APART. Slice 17 stated the separation condition; it is now a recorded field value rather than an argument: :construction-can-separate-them? false with :why-not :acting-order-moves-so-o4-holds-on-that-disjunct-alone on both constructions (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6896-6902 at HEAD, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6160-6169 on Arm B), recomputed against the parent arms at holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:140-171 rather than restated. Separating them needs a construction whose transcript acting order does NOT move, and neither measured construction supplies one (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:7020-7023, holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6182-6188). It also inherits the transcript arm's cost on the half it reads there: 73 of its 102 acting-order rounds lie outside the cohort the gate grades, the round sets nesting primary inside paired inside transcript (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:5323-5324).", :run-by "F12 slice 19 (C541 section 4 option (i) AS WRITTEN, C555); futon2 3c0ad833", :what-it-is "C541 section 4 option (i) AS WRITTEN: read the acting order over the transcript rounds and the score over the primary ones. It is the option that takes the gate's point -- a score is graded against an oracle label and an acting order is not -- at face value. NO ARM ABOVE COULD EXPRESS IT: each builds ONE round set from its keep? and reads both fields off it (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:44-71), so the four are four denominators and not four readings; the split spec takes two predicates, one per field (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:88-138), and with the two equal it is that arm's own row, which the identity control checks rather than assumes (holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:181, holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_d2_denominator_check.clj:388-392). As run: 102 acting-order rounds against 29 score rounds (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/11-d2-denominator.edn:6186-6188)."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861? The declaration is a total function `Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:860 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded O1-O4 instance `does not select one canonical implementation`. Slice 1 established the sorry is INERT: no term in any DarkTower module references `organise`, so discharging it changes no proof obligation. What the arms below differ over is therefore not whether a proof gets easier; it is what the declaration SAYS afterwards.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :organise-sorry], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861? The declaration is a total function `Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:860 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded O1-O4 instance `does not select one canonical implementation`. Slice 1 established the sorry is INERT: no term in any DarkTower module references `organise`, so discharging it changes no proof obligation. What the arms below differ over is therefore not whether a proof gets easier; it is what the declaration SAYS afterwards.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861? The declaration is a total function `Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:860 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded O1-O4 instance `does not select one canonical implementation`. Slice 1 established the sorry is INERT: no term in any DarkTower module references `organise`, so discharging it changes no proof obligation. What the arms below differ over is therefore not whether a proof gets easier; it is what the declaration SAYS afterwards.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/organise-sorry", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:all-arms-run "2026-09-07, F12 slice 14 (C552): the five arms that are this entry's carry measured :buys and :costs; the sixth points at :organise-carrier, where its arms are run. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. mathlib4 git log -1 still reads 61c4825dc3 on Holes.lean and 50fa53469a on holes-contract.json.", :not-claimed "NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED. This entry does not say the sorry should be discharged, amended, sealed or left; it says what each costs. The sorry at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 is untouched by the slice that registered it. It says nothing about D2 (which denominator O4's acting order is read over), about D3, about the third-origin choice registered as :organise-third-origin, about the O3 field question registered as :organise-o3-field -- both existence and both non-uniqueness results are stated separately under each reading precisely so that this entry does not decide it -- or about the carrier question registered as :organise-carrier.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "A RECORDED RUN IN WHICH ORGANISE ADDS A NODE TO THE CASCADE. That is what would let the corpus tell the two conformant discharges apart, and it is what the sole producer cannot emit: futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:412 writes :added-by-organise as an empty set literal, and holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_discharge_check.bb FAILS if that literal ever becomes computed, because the zero above would then be stale. The eight non-empty organise-added sets in the corpus are all in futon3:checks/snatch-cascade.edn and are disjoint from their own cascades' nodes, which slice 11 established means the field there does not denote O1's second origin.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C552-F12-discharge-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/09-discharge-arm.edn; holes/labs/wm-contract/C539-F12-organise-census.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C544-F12-organise-function-conformance.md", :question "WHAT IS DONE WITH THE SORRY at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861? The declaration is a total function `Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P` whose body is `sorry`, and whose docstring at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:860 calls it a DELIBERATE IMPLEMENTATION REFUSAL on the ground that the recorded O1-O4 instance `does not select one canonical implementation`. Slice 1 established the sorry is INERT: no term in any DarkTower module references `organise`, so discharging it changes no proof obligation. What the arms below differ over is therefore not whether a proof gets easier; it is what the declaration SAYS afterwards.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-07", :by "joe", :channel "session, same walkthrough, item 5; Joe verbatim: 'So this sounds good. I like your plan.' -- accepting the staged plan -- plus: 'when we put in a refusal, what we're really doing is alluding to a new design pattern, and we should write that down, probably in our problems library, with the typical if-however-then format.' The pattern is authored: futon3 library/problems/deliberate-refusals-allude-to-unwritten-patterns.flexiarg (futon3 524fa95).", :consequence "With :organise-carrier this frees F12 slice 4. No seat discharges the sorry with a concrete implementation: the non-uniqueness proofs make that an arbitrary selection the record cannot justify, which is the docstring's refusal proved rather than stated.", :decision "DESTINATION :amend-to-an-existence-statement AT THE ARM-6 SIGNATURE: replace the refused def with the arm-6 conformance predicate plus 'exists f, Conformant f', whose content is already proved (existence and non-uniqueness under each O3 reading: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:48, :53, :84, :93). STAGING: the declaration at Holes.lean:861 stays as :leave-it-refused until the slice-4 exemplar validates arm 6; then the retype and the existence amendment land as ONE Holes.lean edit. The interim state is refused-by-design, and the refusal's pattern is written down.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :row :F12, :arms [{:arm :discharge-with-any-inhabitant, :buys "THE SORRY GOES AND NOTHING ELSE HAPPENS. The type is inhabited with no assumptions (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:28), so the sorry was never standing in for an empty type -- which is what makes the other arms' costs the real subject.", :costs "THE RESULTING DECLARATION IS REFUTED BY THE O-LAWS ON THE RECORDED INPUTS, under both readings of O3: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:32 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:40. So this arm converts a declaration that proves nothing into one that is false of the record, which is worse than the sorry and not merely equal to it.", :run-by "F12 slice 14 (C552); mathlib4 26092af4f2 + 38a34f286a", :what-it-is "Replace the sorry with any total term. `organiseEmpty` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:24) returns the empty cascade whatever it is handed."} {:arm :discharge-with-a-conformant-implementation, :buys "A CONFORMANT DISCHARGE EXISTS AND THE EXISTENCE IS PROVED SEPARATELY UNDER EACH O3 READING, so taking this arm does not tacitly decide the choice registered as :organise-o3-field: mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:48 and mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:53.", :costs "IT SELECTS ONE IMPLEMENTATION, WHICH IS THE THING THE DOCSTRING REFUSES -- and the refusal is now a PROVED FACT rather than a stated one. Under the selected reading the laws admit two functions that return different node sets on the recorded zaif inputs (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:84, difference from mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:107); under the node-set reading they admit two more (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:93), which needed a second witness of its own because `organiseUpClosure` is refuted there (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:173). The difference is located rather than merely exhibited: both node-reading witnesses return every recorded selected node (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:111), so they disagree about O1's SECOND origin and nothing else, and each side of the disagreement is inhabited on the record (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:120, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:127, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:133) without the edge relation being total (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:140). AND NO RECORDED RUN COULD SETTLE IT: over the nine cascade records under futon3:checks, 52 O1-shaped cascades carry 8 with a non-empty organise-added set, all 8 in futon3:checks/snatch-cascade.edn, and ZERO in which a node organise added is a node of the cascade -- recomputed into holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/09-discharge-arm.edn, with the constructor's empty literal at futon3:checks/construct_cascade.clj:412 read out so the emptiness is a fact about the producer and not about which runs happened to be recorded.", :run-by "F12 slice 6 (C544) built the witnesses; F12 slice 14 (C552) states the existence and the non-uniqueness; mathlib4 26092af4f2 + 38a34f286a", :what-it-is "Replace the sorry with a term the O-laws accept -- `organiseSelectedOnly` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:59) or `organiseUpClosure` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:77), each a total function at organise's own type."} {:arm :amend-to-an-existence-statement, :buys "ITS WHOLE CONTENT IS ALREADY PROVED and needs no new mathematics: existence under each reading (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:48, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:53) and non-uniqueness under each (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:84, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:93). It removes the sorry while saying exactly what the docstring says, instead of contradicting it.", :costs "TWO, AND ONE OF THEM IS OUTSIDE THIS ROW. It turns `organise` from a term into a proposition, so anything applying `organise` would have to eliminate an existential -- which costs nothing today, since slice 1 found zero term references to it anywhere in DarkTower, and would cost whatever the first consumer costs. And editing Holes.lean moves the contract twice over: the authority is derived as `git log -1 -- Holes.lean` (mathlib4/DarkTower/Contract/Emit.lean:52-62), so the amendment requires the C176 regeneration slice 4 had to perform after slice 2, AND the hole registry in the same file carries `organise` as a refusal (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:8025), which an amendment has to restate rather than leave saying `implementation, not a law` of a declaration that is no longer an implementation. That is why this slice proved the content in a separate module and left Holes.lean untouched.", :run-by "F12 slice 14 (C552) proves the content; the edit to Holes.lean is NOT applied", :what-it-is "Replace the refused `def organise ... := sorry` with the conformance predicate plus `exists f, Conformant f` -- the shape the acceptance's own swappability clause asks for, `implementation conformance, not identity`."} {:arm :seal-it-opaque, :buys "THE SORRY GOES WITH NO IMPLEMENTATION CHOSEN -- which is NOT what the packet expected. The packet claimed `opaque` requires a body, so that this arm would be the previous one in disguise; it does not. `organiseOpaqueNoBody` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:271) elaborates with no body at all, from the inhabitance instance at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:262, and removing that instance is what makes it fail. What separates the two routes is their AXIOM FOOTPRINT and it is machine-readable: `#print axioms` reports NO axioms for the body-carrying `organiseOpaqueZaif` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:256) and `Classical.choice` for the bodiless one.", :costs "NOTHING ABOUT THE VALUE SURVIVES THE SEAL, so no O-law can be witnessed of the declaration at all -- this arm keeps the refusal's content and gives up its evidence, where the conformant-discharge arm gives up the refusal and keeps the evidence. The body-carrying route additionally seals a specific term, and the only term anyone has to seal here is `organiseEmpty`, which mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12DischargeArm.lean:32 refutes.", :run-by "F12 slice 14 (C552), and the dispatch packet's premise about this arm was REFUTED; mathlib4 26092af4f2 + 38a34f286a", :what-it-is "Replace the sorry with an `opaque` declaration, keeping the refusal and removing the sorry token."} {:arm :leave-it-refused, :buys "NOTHING MOVES, and the cost of that is smaller than it looks: the sorry is INERT. Recomputed at slice 14 rather than copied from slice 1, because six F12 modules have been added since it was measured: over all of mathlib4/DarkTower there are still ZERO term references to `organise`. Every occurrence outside the declaration itself is prose in a doc-comment or module header, plus one string literal in the hole registry (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:8025, `mkRefused \"organise\"`; slice 1 recorded that literal at :7899 and the file has grown since). So no proof obligation anywhere depends on it.", :costs "THE MODULE KEEPS REPORTING IT. `lake build DarkTower.WarMachine.F12DischargeArm` emits `declaration uses sorry` for mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861 alongside nine others in the same file, so any sorry census over Holes.lean counts it, and the acceptance's clause stays open indefinitely.", :run-by "F12 slice 1 (C539) measured its cost; unchanged by every slice since", :what-it-is "Do nothing to the declaration."} {:arm :amend-the-type, :buys :see-organise-carrier, :costs :see-organise-carrier, :run-by :not-here, :what-it-is "Change what `organise` returns, so the laws can be stated of it. This is D1, and it is REGISTERED SEPARATELY as :organise-carrier with six arms, all run.", :why-not-run-here "Not this entry's to run and not restated here: duplicating that entry's measured payments under a second key would make one choice look like two. What this entry adds is that the type amendment and the sorry are SEPARABLE -- every other arm above removes the sorry without touching the type, and :organise-carrier's arms are about the type whether or not the sorry moves."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "O1 gives a cascade node three origins and organise's declared type takes no input that determines the third. `organise : Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P := sorry` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861); the third origin `admittedBy` was added by the :LA2 field amendment (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:833-845). The free hand: does the signature gain an attribution input that pins admittedBy, or does the declaration record that the attribution is free? Both arms are RUN, each in a Lean module that touches no existing declaration.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :organise-third-origin], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "O1 gives a cascade node three origins and organise's declared type takes no input that determines the third. `organise : Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P := sorry` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861); the third origin `admittedBy` was added by the :LA2 field amendment (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:833-845). The free hand: does the signature gain an attribution input that pins admittedBy, or does the declaration record that the attribution is free? Both arms are RUN, each in a Lean module that touches no existing declaration.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "O1 gives a cascade node three origins and organise's declared type takes no input that determines the third. `organise : Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P := sorry` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861); the third origin `admittedBy` was added by the :LA2 field amendment (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:833-845). The free hand: does the signature gain an attribution input that pins admittedBy, or does the declaration record that the attribution is free? Both arms are RUN, each in a Lean module that touches no existing declaration.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/organise-third-origin", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:all-arms-run "2026-09-07, F12 slice 10: every arm now carries a measured cost. NO RULING IS TAKEN AND NONE IS IMPLIED -- :status is still :observed-not-decided and there is no :ruling key. What the fourth arm changed is that the free hand C547 section 6 named inside the pay arm is no longer unmeasured.", :not-claimed "This entry says nothing about D1 (which carrier the four O-laws are stated of), D2 (which denominator O4's acting order is read over), D3 (whether an O4 witness may be reached by an encoding written after the law), or the O3 field question (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:1034). O4 is still not stateable at the arm carrier: ArmOneCascade has none of its six fields.", :what-would-change-the-measurement "a recorded run in which two policy-grain rules each admit at least one pattern. The maximum rule-carrying member count on any recorded run is 1 (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/02-o4-reachability.edn), and the gate that would produce such a run does not pass at HEAD -- require-pass! aborts with :rule-does-not-encode-an-authored-then for three of four rules (futon3c:scripts/zaif_cascade_gate.clj:579-582), a table :F12 does not own.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/C547-F12-choice-point.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C548-F12-support-grain-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C543-F12-d1-arms-run.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C544-F12-organise-function-conformance.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C545-F12-admitting-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/C546-F12-attribution-arm.md; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F12-organise/06-attribution-arm.edn", :question "O1 gives a cascade node three origins and organise's declared type takes no input that determines the third. `organise : Cascade Policy -> Set P -> Repository P -> Cascade P := sorry` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:861); the third origin `admittedBy` was added by the :LA2 field amendment (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:833-845). The free hand: does the signature gain an attribution input that pins admittedBy, or does the declaration record that the attribution is free? Both arms are RUN, each in a Lean module that touches no existing declaration.", :registered-by [:claude-wm-edge], :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-07", :by "joe", :channel "session, same walkthrough, item 9; Joe verbatim: 'I agree with your suggestion as far as I can follow it. I would just say that what seems to be a consideration beyond any structural or architectural decision is just a data availability problem... that limitation needs to be addressed in order for any decision here to be meaningful... alongside your structural proposition, we need to start up a new mining loop that actually goes and produces some historical cascades that we can use as a source of data.'", :consequence "DATA-AVAILABILITY RIDER, which Joe places beyond the structural decision: the one-distinct-rule-id corpus bound must be addressed for any grain distinction to be meaningful. Commissioned alongside: (a) the two-rule cascade excursion (:organise-o4-after-the-law-encoding rider 3), and (b) a NEW MINING LOOP producing historical cascades as data -- reconstituting the Cascade Live problem hierarchies as cascades that solved them, each naming the patterns involved (the mission-cloth precedent from the predecessor site), upgrading the library-loop/why-how machinery. Commissioning note: futon2 holes/labs/library-loop/MINING-historical-cascades.md.", :decision "ARM 4, :support-grain-input: the declared signature gains a Set P attribution input and the one equality clause, so admittedBy is determined by a recorded input rather than an implementation's free hand (any two conformant functions agree at every input, F12SupportArm.lean:82). Grounds: the item-6 no-bootstrap ruling made admittedBy load-bearing for O3's meaning -- a free attribution lets the proved mirror empty the field and shrink the set O3 quantifies over toward the refuted selected reading. The rule-grain upgrade stays open and cheap: the two grains are inter-derivable (F12SupportArm.lean:137, :263), so full rule provenance lands by indicator instantiation when the corpus carries more than one rule id. The attribution input joins the Score parameter in the SAME staged single Holes.lean edit (:organise-sorry ruling).", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-07", :measurement-that-separates-them "THE RECORDED DATA CANNOT EXERCISE THE GRAIN THE PAY ARM BUYS ITS DETERMINATION AT. Recomputed 2026-09-07 by re-running holes/labs/wm-contract/f12_attribution_check.bb (PASS, artifact byte-identical to the committed one): over the nine cascade records under futon3:checks, 213 admissions, seven records carrying provenance, two carrying none (construct-cascade.edn, snatch-cascade.edn), and ONE distinct rule id in the whole corpus, :widen-the-cascade-only-on-evidence. So no recorded run distinguishes an emitting-rule attribution from a boolean admitted-or-not flag.", :row :F12, :arms [{:arm :pay-for-the-argument, :buys "the third origin is determined: any two conformant functions agree on admittedBy at every input (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:128), and every conformant function returns the nine recorded admissions (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:138).", :costs "a fourth argument the declaration does not have, and a determination that is a projection of it rather than a property the interface gained: at the ENLARGED argument list, two functions conformant on the four laws still disagree on admission until the clause is added (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:208). It also overturns a proved result -- the slice-7 mirror, conformant at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:98, is refuted at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:119.", :run-by "F12 slice 8 (C547 section 3); mathlib4 0251291563 + 4930505dc1", :what-it-is "one input added to the declared type -- `P -> Option Rule` (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:48-49) -- and one conformance clause `oattr` pinning admittedBy to that input's support (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:63-64)."} {:arm :attribution-is-free, :buys "no argument is paid for, and the O-laws stay statable of the function as slice 6 states them (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:23-37).", :costs "WITH an admittedBy field (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12D1Arms.lean:74-82) the attribution is undetermined: a conformant function files all nine recorded admissions under addedByOrganise, leaves admittedBy empty, and satisfies all four clauses (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AdmittingArm.lean:98). WITHOUT one (Cascade as declared, mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:29-34) it is worse than undetermined -- every recorded admission is FORCED under addedByOrganise (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12Conformance.lean:123), which is the misattribution the :LA2 amendment added the field to prevent.", :run-by "F12 slices 6 and 7 (C547 section 4); mathlib4 0c5745c39e, 0691f74e48, 7d4f6ffca3, acb4e95bcf", :what-it-is "the declared argument list kept, and the declaration amended to say the laws do not fix the attribution. Two sub-arms by carrier."} {:arm :read-it-off-the-temperament, :buys "nothing: REFUTED. The two slice-7 witnesses disagree on admittedBy for EVERY temperament (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:230), and the proof never reads the temperament's fields -- Cascade Policy carries rule ids and nothing mapping a rule to the patterns it admitted.", :costs "n/a -- this arm is closed by the refutation, not by a choice.", :run-by "F12 slice 8 (C547 section 4)", :what-it-is "organise already takes the policy-grain cascade, so reading the attribution off it would cost no argument."} {:arm :support-grain-input, :buys "THE SAME DETERMINATION ON A SMALLER INPUT. Any two conformant functions agree on admittedBy at every input (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:82), and the two arms are inter-derivable: support conformance transfers forward through support erasure (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:137), and rule-grain conformance transfers back through an indicator at ANY named rule (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:263), instantiated at the single rule id the recorded corpus carries (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:277). Handed the support of the recorded provenance map, every conformant function returns the nine recorded admissions (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:240).", :costs "THE SAME FOURTH ARGUMENT -- this arm is cheaper in grain, not in argument count -- and the same price statement holds: at the enlarged argument list without the clause, two functions conformant on the four laws agree on nodes and on an inhabited edge relation and still disagree on admission at vertex 11 (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:114, non-vacuity at mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:227). WHAT THE SMALLER INPUT LOSES IS NOT VISIBLE IN admittedBy: for any conformant rule-grain function, equal supports force equal admittedBy (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:167), and on the recorded run no conformant function distinguishes the recorded provenance from a counterfactual relabelling to the stop rule with the same support (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:186). Stated against overstating it: the rule grain IS readable by a conformant function in another field -- a witness filing the stop-labelled subset under addedByOrganise conforms (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:205), returns the same nodes as the natural witness (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:292), and differs from it only on the counterfactual input, never on the recorded one (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:216).", :run-by "F12 slice 10 (C548); mathlib4 60cab98ab3", :what-it-is "the pay arm with a `Set P` attribution input instead of a rule-keyed map (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:24), and the same one added clause, now equality with that argument (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12SupportArm.lean:38). It is a free hand INSIDE the pay arm: the clause reads only the support, {p | (prov p).isSome} (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:63-64); the determination discharges by rw on that clause alone and never eliminates Rule (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/F12AttributionArm.lean:128); and the field it pins is a Set P for a reason the source states (mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Holes.lean:833-845)."}]}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "Which Obs v declarations does the machine's C range over, family-or-one-C, and where does serendipity value live? Raised by :F10 (worklist.edn), surveyed in C538-F10-outcome-domain-decision-sheet.md sections 1-6: today the machine computes no KL[Q(o|pi) || C] anywhere -- the only real Q ranges over the 7 M-INC state/* events while the risk term's C reads 13 channel ranges, disjoint alphabets -- so declaring Obs is the entire decision.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :outcome-domain], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "Which Obs v declarations does the machine's C range over, family-or-one-C, and where does serendipity value live? Raised by :F10 (worklist.edn), surveyed in C538-F10-outcome-domain-decision-sheet.md sections 1-6: today the machine computes no KL[Q(o|pi) || C] anywhere -- the only real Q ranges over the 7 M-INC state/* events while the risk term's C reads 13 channel ranges, disjoint alphabets -- so declaring Obs is the entire decision.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "Which Obs v declarations does the machine's C range over, family-or-one-C, and where does serendipity value live? Raised by :F10 (worklist.edn), surveyed in C538-F10-outcome-domain-decision-sheet.md sections 1-6: today the machine computes no KL[Q(o|pi) || C] anywhere -- the only real Q ranges over the 7 M-INC state/* events while the risk term's C reads 13 channel ranges, disjoint alphabets -- so declaring Obs is the entire decision.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/outcome-domain", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:correction-2026-09-07 "DATED CORRECTION, owed by the ruling itself (the never-silent rule) and triggered by the C574 census + Joe's trace-or-clear instruction ('Either we can trace it properly. Or we can't. So, I'm not going to guess.'). The :decision text's 'FOURTEEN terminal flight dispositions, the nine never-yet-observed' inherits a miscount: TRACED in C574-F10-disposition-enumeration.md section 10 to a literal-grep artifact -- at the origin note's authorship revision (futon2 453cedfa, 2026-08-27) full_loop_runner.clj held exactly fourteen literal :outcome keywords, missing :grounded-change and :no-selection because they are assigned via variables. The fourteen counts syntax, not a vocabulary. CORRECTED READING: Obs organisations ranges over outcome-kinds (full_loop_cohort.clj:31-33), TWELVE members, the set the machine gates on at :317 and tripwire.clj:189; the five observed dispositions (kl-worked-example.edn) are members; SEVEN carry named zero mass, not nine. Every other clause of the ruling stands unchanged. Support widens later only by a reviewed change to the gate itself. The runner/gate vocabulary seam (emittable-but-ungated names) is recorded in C574 section 10 as a code-consistency finding, outside this correction.", :question "Which Obs v declarations does the machine's C range over, family-or-one-C, and where does serendipity value live? Raised by :F10 (worklist.edn), surveyed in C538-F10-outcome-domain-decision-sheet.md sections 1-6: today the machine computes no KL[Q(o|pi) || C] anywhere -- the only real Q ranges over the 7 M-INC state/* events while the risk term's C reads 13 channel ranges, disjoint alphabets -- so declaring Obs is the entire decision.", :ruling {:at "2026-09-07", :by "joe", :channel "session, claude-1 walking C538 as RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-07.md items 1-3, rulings dictated across the day. D3 (item 1): 'Option 1 is good here' -- C_ser prefers the OCCASION (organisations vertex), not the UPDATE (evidence vertex); plus the preference-registry framing ('what we're doing now is not solving that once and for all, but creating something like a preference registry and seeding it with some content'). D2 (item 3): 'I definitely rule arm two' plus 'we should also lift the exclusion on preferences related to evidence... there's a clear preference there for finding evidence that is epistemologically valid... [otherwise] a different version of the dark room problem, where we have loads of preferences that are effectively internal to the system, and no preference is related to its actual performance.' D1 (item 2, ruled PENDING-EVIDENCE until both commissioned evidence halves landed, then): 'these recommendations all look good... if we're judging behavior based on historical flights, that's not as good as running new information through the system and showing that it has the expected good behavior... it would be nice to complement that with at least one new end-to-end run of the relevant subcomponents, so that we can demonstrate performance and conformance of the system, as well as some kind of historical relevance. Record it.'", :consequence "F10 leaves :needs-joe and its next slices build the seed: the preference-registry seed content and the Lean Obs declarations. LIVE-RUN RIDER, blocking validation: historical flights are usable evidence, but the seed is not treated as validated until AT LEAST ONE NEW END-TO-END RUN of the relevant subcomponents computes the seeded C live and demonstrates performance and conformance (the contract-edits-wait-for-their-exemplar staging, applied to the C seed). The Q-side gap remains named: Q(o|pi) over dispositions must be built, and F1's finding stands -- the blocking piece is B's dependence on u (belief.clj:216-231). The section-2a-prime amendment to P-validated-R5 is owed as a dated follow-up section, never a silent edit.", :decision "ONE C OVER THE TAGGED SUM (C538 section 4 arm 2): the family becomes a support partition of a single PreferenceDistribution (Holes.lean:6778-6780 is the surface the model keeps; the per-vertex C at Holes.lean:151-152 is the one it does not). Obs organisations := the FOURTEEN terminal flight dispositions, the nine never-yet-observed carrying NAMED ZERO MASS (only 5 of 14 occur in the 82-attempt corpus, runs/D1-evidence/kl-worked-example.edn -- a first occurrence is a registry event, not a crash). Obs evidence := certification/update records, valued by EIG, PLUS a named C-region for EPISTEMIC VALIDITY (the D2 extension lifting P-validated-R5 section 2a-prime's blanket exclusion: mass on the validity of what is learned from, never on raw having-learned). NAMED-EMPTY Obs slots at nouns and verbs (four-frames: vertex-local preferences later are registry writes, not type migrations). C_int stays OUTSIDE the sum, declared as channel proprioception at tick grain. C_ser is a NAMED-EMPTY region of organisations support (D3: the occasion -- anomaly-on-the-board -- not the update). The typed-absence vocabulary (preferences.clj:360-408) stays instrument-side, not part of the domain. The document graph (479 docs, real modular structure at z=-3.53, runs/D1-evidence/spectral.edn) is recorded as the registry's PLANNED EVOLUTION -- future support structure for regions -- not a competing domain; treatment of its 112 components and 69 isolates is deferred to that step.", :evidence "C538-F10-outcome-domain-decision-sheet.md (the survey); runs/D1-evidence/kl-worked-example.edn (Q discriminates; C placement flips the policy ranking -- address-sorry last under uniform C, second under grounded-change-weighted C; 68 pairs + 14 no-pi = the NOTE's 82); runs/D1-evidence/spectral.edn + receipt.md (normalized lambda_2 = 0.0410 vs null 0.2235 +/- 0.0518, z = -3.53, 200 rewirings seed 54112026); C537-serendipity-shapes-C.md (the occasion/update distinction D3 declares)", :grounds :ruling}, :status :decided}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "pi-zero-form", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :pi-zero-form], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "pi-zero-form", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/pi-zero-form", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/C20" "wm-ticket/C21" "wm-ticket/C23"], :subjects [], :choice {:statement "eq. 2.7's beta update is driven by (pi - pi_0) . G, so what pi_0 contains decides what the update measures. The sources disagree with themselves: friston2017.txt:684 gives pi_0 = sigma(-gamma . G) with no habit prior, while the authors' own implementation computes pu = spm_softmax(qE + w*Q) -- the habit prior IN pi_0 as well as in pi (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:964, verified in clone 530ec52). Our futon2.aif.policy-precision puts ln E in neither today.", :note-2026-09-09 "Item 19c (E on for RUN4) does NOT select an arm here; the codex-17 implementation discovery surfaces the arms concretely and the choice returns to Joe unless a recorded principle settles it. SUPERSEDED later the same day by the :ruling above.", :evidence "C463-pymdp-spm-crosscheck.md; SPM 530ec52 spm_MDP_VB_X.m:963-964; friston2017.txt:684; policy.clj:82-100 (the ln E seam); C3 (habit prior not applied to selection); runs/2026-09-01-s2/ARMS.txt:146-286 and run7_beta_arms.clj:42-53,95 (the three arms, run); worklist I1 :slice-b2b", :run-result {:pointers "ARMS.txt:146-192 (:none), :193-239 (:pi only), :240-286 (:both); the gamma-last lines are :169, :216 and :263", :reproduction "run7_beta_arms.clj re-run against f625754 by claude-20 while writing this entry; its output is byte-identical to the committed runs/2026-09-01-s2/ARMS.txt (diff empty, all 308 lines). The script carries its OWN bisection rather than calling converge-beta, and its :none arm is checked against src before any arm is read (ARMS.txt:2, delta 0.0), so these are three arms of one measured object and not two implementations agreeing to four decimals.", :field "runs/2026-09-01-s2/wm-trace-s2.edn -- 20 carried ticks, beta_0 = 1.0, 143 aligned candidates on tick 1 and 145 thereafter", :slice "I1 (b2b)", :at "2026-09-01", :beta-at-tick-20 {:habit-prior-in-both 1.029614, :habit-prior-in-pi-only 1.106121, :none 1.034342}, :by "claude-20", :solver-health "20/20 converged AND bracketed in all three arms", :reading "the SPM form nearly cancels, which is what its rationale predicted, and the prediction now has a number on it: :both moves gamma at tick 20 by 0.004440 away from the ln-E-free arm, :pi-only by 0.062738 -- 14.1 times further. With E in pi only the beta update is driven by the habit prior about as much as by F_pi, which is what eq. 2.7 does not ask for.", :gamma-at-tick-20 {:habit-prior-in-both 0.9712374387398894, :habit-prior-in-pi-only 0.9040600731260442, :none 0.9667979197554702}}, :measurement {:control "the :none arm -- what converge-beta computes by default (:log-prior-placement :none, src/futon2/aif/policy_precision.clj) and what the S2 run itself recorded", :parameter "whether ln E, per candidate, is NON-UNIFORM over the aligned field the beta solve reads -- not whether selection applies it", :ships-behind-flag :habit-prior-in-both, :values "SEPARATED on runs/2026-09-01-s2 -- see :run-result. Separated is not adjudicated: the three arms give three different gammas and all three converge and bracket on 20/20 ticks, and nothing measured here says which is better.", :what-would-adjudicate "a difference in what the machine SELECTS under each arm. That is an S3-stage measurement and not an S2 one, because gamma reaches selection only once FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE :variational-beta-gamma is wired (RUN8). Note before it is run: at today's selection boundary tau does not reach the selected action at all -- worklist I1 :slice-b2b gives the two code sites -- so the adjudicating measurement may have to change the boundary, or be a measurement of something other than the argmax.", :why "so that the arm shipped is stated, and is the one with the better rationale, while the entry stays open until an ADJUDICATING number exists. Recording a default is not deciding the choice.", :withdrawal "That parameter was the wrong one, and the claim recorded under it -- the two arms COINCIDE on the live path and no recorded field can separate them -- is FALSE. It is withdrawn here rather than edited away. eq. 2.7's beta update does not consume the selection posterior: it builds its own pi and pi_0 out of G, F_pi and ln E (run7_beta_arms.clj:42-53), taking ln E from each candidate's :habit-prior-bias (run7_beta_arms.clj:95). The arms therefore separate whenever ln E is non-uniform over that field, whether or not selection ever reads it. Both things hold at once on our own S2 records: :habit-prior-applied? false on 20/20 decisions -- the strategic-recommendation branch war_machine.clj:4829-4837 asks for sets it so at policy.clj:306-307, and its chosen entry is the first non-no-op of the G-ordered list at policy.clj:283-285 -- AND ln E present on every aligned candidate, 3 distinct values, spread 3.0445 nats, no zeros, :habit-prior-source :learned-frequency on 143-145 of 145 candidates on every one of the 20 ticks. C3 stands; the inference drawn from C3 did not.", :withdrawn-parameter "whether ln E is applied to selection at all"}, :interim {:grounds :steward-interim, :statement "Adopt the code's form: ln E enters pi and pi_0 alike. With E in both, (pi - pi_0) isolates what F_pi alone does to the posterior, which is exactly what the beta update is meant to measure; with E in pi only, the update would also be driven by the habit prior, which eq. 2.7 does not ask for.", :alternative "friston2017.txt:684 as printed -- pi_0 = sigma(-gamma . G), no E. Recorded, not chosen.", :consequence "I1 slice (b2) implements pi_0 with ln E and states it: (b2a) made all three placements runnable in the solver at 4625524, default :none; (b2b) names :habit-prior-in-both as the arm the live wiring takes, in worklist I1 :slice-b2b. The sentence that stood here -- until ln E is live the two forms coincide on the live path -- is withdrawn; see :measurement :withdrawal.", :at "2026-09-01", :by "claude-20", :grounds-audit "2026-09-01, I1 (b2b). The second limb of :why-not-a-J-row is FALSIFIED: this one cannot be run yet -- it has been run, on our own field, see :run-result. What made it runnable is the thing :measurement :withdrawal names: the beta solve reads ln E from the record whether or not selection applies it. The interim DECISION is unchanged, and is better supported now than when it was taken, because the near-cancellation it was argued from is measured (0.004440 in gamma against 0.062738 for the alternative) rather than reasoned. What is still missing is an ADJUDICATING number -- a difference in what the machine does -- so the entry stays :open-branches and does not become :decided.", :decision :habit-prior-in-both, :why-not-a-J-row "Joe's rule of 2026-09-01: a choice the theory does not determine gets its branches BUILT AND RUN, not an advance ruling. This one cannot be run yet -- the arms coincide while the habit prior is absent from selection (C3) -- so the entry stays :open-branches with the measurement specified, one arm ships behind the flag, and the comparison happens when ln E goes live. Asking Joe to pick now would be asking with nothing to go on, which is the thing the rule forbids."}, :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "model-choices sitting with codex-17; verbatim in SESSION-model-choices-2026-09-09.md (15e80338): 'Yes, habit in both makes sense in this case. Naturally, as time goes by, we could tune the way in which habits are recorded and how they're referred or deferred to, or even how they're changed or forgotten. But that won't work unless we have them present.'", :decision ":habit-prior-in-both — both pi and pi_0 include ln E; their difference measures the additional F_pi effect conditional on the same habit prior. An operator ruling, NOT an empirical superior-selections claim; habit recording/deference/change/forgetting remain refinable with no mechanism selected; no live beta wiring or strategic-prior promotion inferred (fixture E_S stands per Items 21a+22).", :grounds :ruling}, :observed :all-three-placements-in-the-solver-default-none-nothing-live-consumes-them, :u3-placement-comparison {:sharper-than-the-headroom "ON THE PATH THE RUNS ACTUALLY TOOK, beta reaches nothing that selects at all. All 24 records carry :selection-boundary :reason-bearing-strategic-policy, which is not one of select-action's boundaries: the controller decision's :action is REPLACED at war_machine.clj:5241-5244 by the mission the R14 strategic selector returned, and that selector is called (war_machine.clj:5211-5214) with a vector of three mission-id strings and a trace-id -- the strategic candidates in wm-admissible order (war_machine.clj:5203-5209), wm-admissible being the G-ordered ranked list filtered by executability (war_machine.clj:5169). No tau, no posterior, no score crosses that call. Measured from the records to match: the :decision :action equals the argmax of ln E - G/tau on 0 of 24 ticks. This is U1 readiness point 4 carried one call further, to the site that overwrites the action.", :report "C488-u3-pi-zero-placement.md", :detector-has-teeth "The zeros are not a dead detector. Drop ln E from the SELECTION score while leaving F_pi in -- score -G/tau - F_pi -- and the placement starts deciding: 11 of 20 S2 ticks change argmax at beta_0 = 0.5, with lambda_break 1.043728 BELOW rho 1.166361, i.e. the arms move tau further than the choice survives. That expression is NOT REACHABLE: F_pi enters the posterior at the strategic boundary and nowhere else (policy.clj:634-638 throws otherwise) and that site always passes the full log-priors vector (policy.clj:553-556), built as zeros rather than nil (policy.clj:656-657) -- so F_pi without ln E requires an ln E identically zero, and ln E is non-zero on every aligned candidate here (3 distinct values, spread 3.0445224377 nats, 0 zeros, 24/24 ticks). It is reported as the shape of the null from the other side.", :bearing-on-the-ruling "RECOMMEND :habit-prior-in-both, and the entry STAYS :open-branches -- the ruling is Joe's. Three grounds in decreasing order of what the numbers carry. (1) The adjudicating measurement this entry specified has now been run at the seam this entry named and returns a typed no-discrimination result, 0 of 288 with 35x-8400x headroom and a detector shown able to fire. It does NOT say :both selects better; it says nothing the machine does distinguishes the arms, by a stated margin. (2) Under SPEC U2's fallback rule -- if the arms do not discriminate, choose by source fidelity -- the source is the authors' own implementation, which puts ln E in both (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:963-964, verified in clone by C463). That is already the :interim, so this changes nothing; it removes the reason the entry was open. (3) One ground that is measured and is about the arms rather than the field: :both leaves gamma 14 times closer to the ln-E-free arm than :pi-only does (|d gamma| at S2 tick 20 0.004440 against 0.062738), which is the near-cancellation the SPM rationale predicts and the reason (pi - pi_0) isolates F_pi. WHAT WOULD MAKE THE PLACEMENT DECIDABLE BY MEASUREMENT is not a longer replay: a selector that reads the posterior, and a field whose leaders sit within one ln E group of each other.", :why-the-headroom-is-not-luck "ln E's 3.0445224377-nat spread over 3 groups is what holds the argmax down: within one ln E group the ordering is tau-invariant (the shift is monotone in G), so only cross-group pairs can flip and the nearest cross-group crossing sits 13.6x away. RUN8 found the same structure from the other direction -- runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt reports a smallest cross-group adjacent margin of 0.7355590795 with 0 argmax moves.", :script "u3_pi_zero_placement.clj:1-488", :controls "1 SOLVER: the local generalised solver's :none arm against src converge-beta, max |delta| 0.000e+00 on 20 (S2) and 4 (S4) ticks, run before any arm is read. 2 RECORDED BETA: S2's own :beta-posterior reproduced from its own :beta-prior, max |delta| 0.000e+00 on 20 ticks; S4 recorded no :policy-precision-state and is reported NOT APPLICABLE rather than passed. 3 ENACTMENT: 0 of 24 gated, 0 of 24 realized. 4 TAU-INVARIANCE of the :G law, 24 of 24. 5 DETECTOR TEETH, above. The three arms also reproduce RUN7's gamma at S2 tick 20 independently (:none 0.9667979198, :pi-only 0.9040600731, :both 0.9712374387), so :run-result is now derived by two scripts from the same records.", :bounds "24 ticks, one route, one apparatus -- C486 section 7's bound. The lambda_break window is exact for the ARGMAX and says nothing about the rest of the ordering, which does move: 36-45 candidates change rank at beta_0 = 1.0 on the F_pi-bearing expressions. :G+F's unreachability is a reading of the call sites; a caller that passes a zero ln E vector alongside live F_pi would turn that control into a live case. The R14 selector was not chased into its own repo -- what is established is the SHAPE of its input at the futon2 call site and that the decision's action is replaced with its answer. And tau = beta is the only route from the arms to selection, so the whole comparison is conditional on the variational mode being the one that runs; S4 solved no beta of its own (:tau-source :selection-gain-only, tau = 1.0 on all 24 recorded ticks), so its arms use beta series this study solves.", :question-not-reached "THE DISCRIMINATOR SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U3 NAMED -- whether the in-pi-only arm brackets the H1b bound better -- does not exist on any committed field. Of the 24 records, 0 carry :act-gate-verdicts and 0 carry :realized-outcome; and H1b's restated bound has an antecedent occurring in 0 of the 50 records that DO carry gates (worklist :H1b :owner-did). No arm can be scored against it at any beta.", :at "2026-09-02", :question-reached "THE MEASUREMENT :what-would-adjudicate NAMES -- a difference in what the machine SELECTS under each arm -- run at the one seam where the arms could reach a decision. The arms differ only in the eq. 2.7 beta they solve, and beta reaches selection by exactly one route: tau_eff = beta under :tau-mode :variational-beta-gamma (policy.clj:135-137). So the chain is arm -> beta_a(t) carried -> tau_a(t) -> softmax(ln E - G/tau - F_pi) (policy.clj:148) -> argmax, and every step below the solve uses the shipped function. NO DISCRIMINATION, TYPED BY MARGIN: 0 argmax differences out of 288 arm-tick comparisons (3 reachable score expressions x 4 beta_0 in {0.5,1,2,5} x 24 ticks: S2 20, S4 4). At the ONE site in the code where tau decides -- policy.clj:693-696, chosen-idx = argmax(ln E - G/tau) -- the choice survives a 13.599688-fold change in tau (lambda_break, computed in closed form: the score is linear in u = 1/tau, so the argmax is the upper envelope of lines and the window edge is the nearest crossing) while the three arms move tau by a factor of 1.074306 (rho, max over ticks at beta_0 = 1.0). Headroom 169.6x on S2 and 798.1x on S4, and monotone in beta_0: 34.9x at 0.5, 169.6x at 1.0, 901.9x at 2.0, 8343.3x at 5.0. At beta_0 = 1.0 not one candidate of 145 changes rank either, on :G or on ln E - G/tau.", :by "claude-cli", :artifact "U3-PI-ZERO-PLACEMENT.txt", :arithmetic-floor "Under the ln-E-free, F_pi-free score the expression is -G/tau and argmax(-G/tau) = argmin G for EVERY tau > 0, so no beta whatever can move that law's choice. A fact about the expression, not about our field; CONTROL 4 checks it at nine tau from 1e-3 to 1e3 on 24 of 24 ticks rather than asserting it.", :row :U3}, :arms {:habit-prior-in-both "SPM's form: ln E enters pi and pi_0 alike (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:963-964). (pi - pi_0) then isolates what F_pi alone does to the posterior, which is what the beta update is meant to measure.", :habit-prior-in-pi-only "friston2017.txt:684 as printed: pi_0 = sigma(-gamma . G), no E. The beta update is then driven by the habit prior as well as by F_pi."}}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 3, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "policy-depth", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :policy-depth], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "policy-depth", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/policy-depth", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "war_machine.clj:4485-4487, 4516-4520 (3 with anticipation snapshot, else single-step); rollout.clj:166-171, 212-230 (default 2) (C448 5c.4)", :observed :fixed-per-configuration, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "model-choices sitting with codex-17; verbatim in SESSION-model-choices-2026-09-09.md ('Record RUN4 policy-depth ruling: explicit three and three')", :decision "RUN4-SCOPED fixed configuration: anticipation depth 3 AND cascade rollout depth 3, EXPLICITLY configured in the run config (not flipped defaults). Not an optimality claim, not adaptive depth, not a global-default change, not go-live authorization. Implementation obligations from the sitting's source correction: the effective consumer is cascade_lane.clj:381 passing :depth 5 (rollout.clj default 2 is NOT the effective value) — trace effective consumers; both effective horizons observable in the run record; the war_machine.clj:6300/:6345 conditional-3 with fallback-1 explicitly accounted under the new config; early endings (terminal/truncated/empty, rollout.clj:554-581 counts moves) stay truthful, never padded.", :grounds :ruling, :revision-2026-09-09 "SUPERSEDES the 3/3 values above, same sitting minutes later (SESSION-model-choices-2026-09-09.md section 6): RUN4 runs ANTICIPATION 3 / CASCADE ROLLOUT 5. The 5 matches the existing cascade_lane.clj:381 caller but must still arrive through explicit run config. All other obligations unchanged; adaptive depth future-only; 3/3 preserved as history in section 5."}, :statement "T varies by invocation/configuration, never per candidate policy.", :status :decided}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "policy-grain", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :policy-grain], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "policy-grain", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/policy-grain", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/U64"], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "machine_q.clj:150 (:refusal/policy-selection-distribution -- the boundary already refuses the selection grain); runs/F1-machine-q/02-policy-family-census.edn (889/889 stable identities, all selections; 0/889 offer a cascade choice); habit_prior.clj:13-14 (the namespace's own disclaimer)", :observed :selection-counts-inhabited-cascade-grain-uninhabited, :ruling {:at "2026-09-05", :by "joe", :channel "session, claude-1 presenting F1's blocker as a two-option menu; Joe verbatim: 'i don't know why we are still talking about action grain or why this is even a question after weeks -- months -- of saying that G must be evaluated over policies, and developing a theory of how that can work, which is the core of R5. I guess someone didnt get the memo'", :consequence "F7 (cascade construction: two or more distinct cascades constructed and scored for one target) is the only path to inhabiting pi; it was already in the work seat when this entry was written. F1 slice 2 waits on F7, not on Joe -- F1's :blocker is to be rewritten at the next board pause to name F7 as its gate, so the row leaves the needs-joe channel. The census runs/F1-machine-q/02-policy-family-census.edn stays as the measurement of why the cascade grain is uninhabited today: evidence for the build, not grounds to reopen the grain.", :decision "The policy grain is the CASCADE and the question is CLOSED, not defaulted. G is evaluated over policies; policies are cascades (four-grain correspondence, N-strategy-as-computational-object.md addendum, 2026-09-05); the action grain is NOT admissible as pi and is not to be re-presented as an option by any seat. A blocker that reduces to this question cites this entry and proceeds on the cascade grain.", :grounds :ruling}, :statement "This entry exists because the ruling previously lived in EPIC-run-era.md and the strategy note but NOT in this registry, and F1's seat -- correctly consulting this registry under its no-ruling discipline -- found no entry and re-opened a settled question (2026-09-05). A ruling not present in the registry the lanes consult is not a ruling for the lanes.", :status :decided}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 1, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "policy-posterior-node", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :verified, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :policy-posterior-node], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "policy-posterior-node", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/policy-posterior-node", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "policy.clj:300-438 select-action; route tag war_machine.clj:4584 (C448 5c.7)", :observed :R6, :statement "Q(π) is computed in R6's implementation; no other node computes it. No decision needed.", :status :verified}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "One quantity -- what a chosen policy actually produced -- has been written under three key-sets and read under a fourth, and no reader saw any writer. This entry states the ONE schema the machine is now made to write and read, and rules on nothing: Joe has not ruled, and an observation is not a decision.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :realized-outcome-schema], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "One quantity -- what a chosen policy actually produced -- has been written under three key-sets and read under a fourth, and no reader saw any writer. This entry states the ONE schema the machine is now made to write and read, and rules on nothing: Joe has not ruled, and an observation is not a decision.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "One quantity -- what a chosen policy actually produced -- has been written under three key-sets and read under a fourth, and no reader saw any writer. This entry states the ONE schema the machine is now made to write and read, and rules on nothing: Joe has not ruled, and an observation is not a decision.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/realized-outcome-schema", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:measured "THE CENSUS, over the whole live corpus (57 files, 889 records), by holes/labs/wm-contract/u59_outcome_vocabulary.clj: 88 records carry a :realized-outcome and every one of them is written :july-2026-delta-g; 0 are readable by the key test the gain reader used before this row; 0 records of 889 carry a categorical outcome in any of the three places the readers look. Of the 88, 77 carry BOTH legs as numbers and fold -- the other 11 carry a nil leg and correctly do not, which is why the number that becomes readable is 77 and not 88. Folded in order into a fresh gain state they move it from 1.0 to 1.3375092522591208 at mean performance 0.4195488714331731; under the old reader the same 88 folded 0 and the state held at the prior. The producer that writes the v1 spelling exists (src/futon2/aif/fold_realized.clj:96-100) and did not write any of these: its one caller is src/futon2/aif/enact.clj:329, which C509 measured as outside the tick's require closure.", :statement "THE ONE SCHEMA is :wm/realized-outcome-v1, declared at src/futon2/aif/realized_outcome.clj:50 with its accessors at :72-138. A realized-outcome record carries {:schema :policy :tick :expected-score :realized-score :outcome :scale}. THE TWO NUMERIC LEGS AND THE CATEGORICAL OUTCOME ARE DIFFERENT ANSWERS AND NOT TWO SPELLINGS OF ONE: the legs are the calibration pair the gain reader folds (src/futon2/aif/selection_gain.clj:174-224), the categorical is what the non-progress walk and the tripwires branch on (scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:2425-2439, src/futon2/aif/tripwire.clj:190). Carrying both under one key is the unification; picking either one alone would have left the other reader dark. :expected-G / :realized-G is the July 2026 spelling of the two legs and NOTHING ELSE -- it is now READ, marked :july-2026-delta-g (src/futon2/aif/realized_outcome.clj:54-64), and never written: a vocabulary is retired by making it readable, not by rewriting the records that used it.", :free-hands {:a-which-spelling-is-canonical "v1 (:expected-score/:realized-score) rather than the July :expected-G/:realized-G. OBSERVED, not ruled: v1 is what the live producer already writes and what the gain reader already required, so canonicalising it changes no producer, while canonicalising the July spelling would change one and rewrite none of the records either way.", :b-where-the-categorical-outcome-comes-from "The observation pass decides it from the chosen mission's own :open-hole-count on the two records (holes/labs/wm-contract/wm_step_observe.bb), strictly down => :grounded-change, from the closed vocabulary at src/futon2/aif/full_loop_cohort.clj:31. MISSION-SCOPED ON PURPOSE: the step world record is repo-wide (:world/commit-census, :world/files, :world/mana-age) and moves when anyone commits anything, so reading an outcome off it would attribute an operator's commit to the machine's chosen action. The world delta is recorded on the observation as context and is explicitly not its basis.", :c-when-the-outcome-is-observed "One accepted step later, not at decision time. A decision's outcome does not exist when the decision is written, so it cannot be a key on the record (the seam that writes the record and its RE4 rationale together is scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:2284-2306); it is observed at the next accept and joined by :run/id. That join is also what gives :rationale-regret a pair, which one tick per step could never produce."}, :evidence "src/futon2/aif/realized_outcome.clj:50-138; src/futon2/aif/selection_gain.clj:174-224; scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:2410-2439; src/futon2/aif/fold_realized.clj:96-100; src/futon2/aif/full_loop_cohort.clj:31; holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U59-outcome-vocabulary/u59-outcome-vocabulary.edn", :question "One quantity -- what a chosen policy actually produced -- has been written under three key-sets and read under a fourth, and no reader saw any writer. This entry states the ONE schema the machine is now made to write and read, and rules on nothing: Joe has not ruled, and an observation is not a decision.", :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-09.md Item 19b", :decision "Schema drafting DELEGATED to the E-C-realization sitting (codex-12): review/extend the existing :wm/realized-outcome-v1 (realized_outcome.clj:50) against the sitting recording-design work; adoption before the RUN4 start as its own reviewed step.", :grounds :ruling}, :at "2026-09-05", :observed :one-schema-three-vocabularies-repaired, :by [:claude-wm-edge], :not-decided-here {:whether-a-steps-rationale-is-scored-against-the-next-step "The pairing is implemented and its basis is recorded (the observation names the run it observed, because the pin ordered them), but whether that is the RIGHT window for a retrospective is a rule question C511-repair-or-elaborate.md section 3 raised and this entry does not answer.", :whether-the-decay-reads-it "The non-progress walk can now read an observed outcome through scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:2410-2439, and the var holding them defaults to {} with no caller in the repository binding it outside the measurement. Making the input readable is not the same act as letting it move scoring, and the second one is Joe's."}, :row :U59}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "The machine records WHY it chose what it chose, and nothing ever asks whether that reason held up. Joe, 2026-09-03, dictated in session: when the machine refuses to work on a given piece of work, are we logging that rationale and learning whether the rationale holds up -- does it maybe regret that choice -- we need to really focus on that learning loop aspect. Joe states NO strong prior on the right form, so this entry registers a choice-set and rules on nothing. The free hands are three: what a selection-time rationale ASSERTS (so that it can be contradicted), what evidence SCORES it, and where a refuted one goes.", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :selection-retrospective], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action "The machine records WHY it chose what it chose, and nothing ever asks whether that reason held up. Joe, 2026-09-03, dictated in session: when the machine refuses to work on a given piece of work, are we logging that rationale and learning whether the rationale holds up -- does it maybe regret that choice -- we need to really focus on that learning loop aspect. Joe states NO strong prior on the right form, so this entry registers a choice-set and rules on nothing. The free hands are three: what a selection-time rationale ASSERTS (so that it can be contradicted), what evidence SCORES it, and where a refuted one goes.", :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "The machine records WHY it chose what it chose, and nothing ever asks whether that reason held up. Joe, 2026-09-03, dictated in session: when the machine refuses to work on a given piece of work, are we logging that rationale and learning whether the rationale holds up -- does it maybe regret that choice -- we need to really focus on that learning loop aspect. Joe states NO strong prior on the right form, so this entry registers a choice-set and rules on nothing. The free hands are three: what a selection-time rationale ASSERTS (so that it can be contradicted), what evidence SCORES it, and where a refuted one goes.", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/selection-retrospective", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:measured "THE CARRIER DISJOINTNESS, which is what shapes the form. Over the whole trace corpus (56 files, 885 records): 94 records carry [:decision :controller-ranking], 88 carry [:realized-outcome], and ZERO carry both -- the ranking era is 2026-08-30 to 09-02 and the outcome era is 2026-07-02 to 07-06. No record in the corpus reaches any of the three places trace-outcome looks (war_machine.clj:2328-2332), so the non-progress signal can never read that progress happened on the tick path; the :grounded-change it tests for is written by a different producer. Further, all 88 :realized-outcome maps carry :expected-G/:realized-G, while fold-realized-outcome (selection_gain.clj:196-206) admits a sample only on numeric :expected-score AND :realized-score, so 0 of 88 are foldable and :samples is 0 on all 125 records carrying a gain state; the correctly shaped producer exists at fold_realized.clj:96-100 and is not what wrote them. THE PRIMITIVE SIGNAL'S REACH, measured: on 2026-09-01 the machine ran 79 ticks over exactly two missions in strict alternation; of 11455 candidate rows exactly 79 carry a decay -- one per tick, always the immediately previous selection -- the count reaches 2 on no row, and the chosen action's own :non-progress-count is 0 on all 79 ticks. The walk terminates at the first record naming a different target (the :else arm), so one intervening selection forgives the count: measured on 2026-09-02, M-wm-aif-policy-grain-compliance carries count 1 / decay 0.5 at 14:00 and is back to 0 / 1.0 at 14:03.", :statement "Two refusal channels exist and only one of them says why. ADMISSION: policy-support-exclusions carries a typed reason per refused candidate -- 376 refusals over the 94 ranking-bearing records, 4 per tick, every one :mission-absent-from-capability-graph, never scored. SELECTION: everything below the chosen entry in the controller ranking -- 144 to 146 candidates per tick, so about 145 rejections per tick, with NO reason field, though the full per-candidate G decomposition (G-risk, G-ambiguity, G-goal-outcome, augmentation-terms, habit-prior-bias, and the mission factors on the action) is recorded beside it. A primitive regret signal exists: previous-selection-non-progress? war_machine.clj:2312-2326 and recent-non-progress-count war_machine.clj:2339-2356, decaying mission value by non-progress-decay-k war_machine.clj:2290.", :not-claimed "NO RULING, and four things explicitly not done. The verdict rule is :declared-not-ruled with its alternatives named. No retrospective is run over history beyond the one worked pair -- that is worklist :U40, which is :blocked and builds on this shape. The tension record is not implemented -- that is :U41. Nothing is written to the pattern library. Also NOT repaired here, and recorded so it is not mistaken for a finding of this row: the :expected-G / :expected-score key mismatch is an era artifact of a superseded writer, not a defect in the shipped fold, and the non-progress walk's alternation behaviour is described rather than changed.", :learning-feed "VERDICTS ACCUMULATE AS EVIDENCE; NO LIVE WEIGHT MOVES WITHOUT A J-GATE. Four parts: (1) a verdict is appended to a ledger under runs/ and written into no trace record, no registry entry and no store; (2) nothing in the tick may read the ledger -- ranking, temperature, admissibility verdicts and selector must be byte-identical whether it exists or not, the containment mission_gauges.clj already states for its own observables; (3) the three consumers are all offline -- the Z3-style pre-registered A/B, arm C :cascade-catalog-playout of :task-belief-actand-source, and Joe's review; (4) any change that lets a verdict influence a live number (a weight, non-progress-decay-k, a tau feed, an admissibility rule) is a worklist :J row and Joe's call. This row does not mint that J row; it names the boundary the row would have to cross.", :evidence "DESIGN PASS ONLY -- nothing implemented on the live path, no file under src/ or scripts/futon2/ changed. Producer (read-only; no tick, no run lock, no substrate call, no network, nothing written under data/): holes/labs/wm-contract/u39_selection_retrospective.bb, run from the futon2 root with bb. Design doc and both artifacts under holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U39-selection-retrospective/ (README.md, u39-measurements.edn, U39-SELECTION-RETROSPECTIVE.txt), byte-identical on two consecutive runs. Four controls, all pass: a fabricated mission id appears in no record and in no claim; every claim margin reproduces the recorded controller-score difference at max absolute deviation 0.0; the overtake detector does not fire on a record scored against itself; it does fire on the recorded 2026-09-02 pair.", :question "The machine records WHY it chose what it chose, and nothing ever asks whether that reason held up. Joe, 2026-09-03, dictated in session: when the machine refuses to work on a given piece of work, are we logging that rationale and learning whether the rationale holds up -- does it maybe regret that choice -- we need to really focus on that learning loop aspect. Joe states NO strong prior on the right form, so this entry registers a choice-set and rules on nothing. The free hands are three: what a selection-time rationale ASSERTS (so that it can be contradicted), what evidence SCORES it, and where a refuted one goes.", :convergence "R14's selection gain consumes a signed (expected, realized) pair (selection_gain.clj:40-70) and has never had a foldable sample -- :samples 0 on all 125 records carrying the state, 0 of 88 :realized-outcome records carrying the required keys. The upheld/refuted stream IS a claimed-versus-verified stream in that namespace's own vocabulary, at policy grain, and the retrospective ledger is the precedent data arm C wants to consume. RECORDED AS A CONVERGENCE, NOT PROPOSED AS A WIRING: feeding R14 from it would be exactly the live-weight move the J-gate above governs.", :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-09", :by "joe", :channel "RULINGS-walkthrough-2026-09-09.md Item 19e", :decision "The acceptance inspection IS the retrospective for RUN4 (runbook pin-advance inspection of route reasons); a mechanical retrospective checker is later work, not a RUN4 gate.", :grounds :ruling}, :provenance "U39, minted from Joe's 2026-09-03 dictation. Choice-set registration under TN-edge-review-aif-wiring section 1 point 3, NOT a ruling: it records what the War Machine is observed to do and names the form candidates. claude-2 review invited on the arm-C consumer side, per the row's acceptance. Related entries: :focus-clock-reconciliation, whose one-tick clock lag is why :tension/carried-by reads the previous tick's mission in the worked example; :c-grain, which registers which C runs live and so bounds the C_mis leg; :task-belief-actand-source, whose arm C is the offline consumer named in :learning-feed.", :observed :rationale-recorded-never-scored, :verdict-rule-options {:declared-attributed-overtake "CHOSEN AS THE FORM TO PUT FORWARD, and declared rather than ruled. REFUTED iff some candidate the claim rejected later out-ranked the chosen one AND its own recorded movement alone would have closed the asserted margin; an overtake that happens only because the chosen candidate was decayed is UNTESTABLE. Two booleans read off the records, NO tunable scalar. It discriminates on the recorded corpus: of the four top rejected candidates that out-ranked M-zaif-harness-v1 one tick later, exactly one (M-expressions-of-interest, own G-core fall 0.005237161 against the 0.004028678 it was rejected by) survives the attribution; the other three read :chosen-decayed.", :overtake-dominant "Any overtake refutes. REJECTED HERE ON A MEASUREMENT, not on taste: on the recorded 2026-09-02 pair it refutes every claim after one tick, because the chosen mission's mission-value-factor halves by construction (0.59 to 0.295, non-progress-decay 1.0 to 0.5) while every rival's factor is byte-identical. Such a test measures the decay, not the rationale.", :weighted-legs "Combine the four legs with declared weights. REJECTED HERE: three of the four legs are typed absences on this corpus, so the weights would be unmeasurable and would be fiat standing in for measurement."}, :form-candidates {:a-rationale-as-claim "A typed record projected from fields already on the trace record -- chosen, top-k rejected, the per-term margin decomposition, the term carrying most of it, and the counter-channel that favoured a rejected candidate without being consulted (lnE enters the selected score only under :full-score-posterior, policy.clj:582 and :593, recorded as :habit-authority at policy.clj:619-621). NO NEW LOGGING: :claim/derived-from names seven recorded fields and nothing else. The claim also refuses to mint on a record whose own :selection-law contradicts its ranking, which is a measured case and not a hypothetical: run 0a18c4f7 says :chosen-rank 1 / :moved-from-controller-head? false with the chosen action at controller rank 124, the false stamp recorded at S4-identify-ingest.edn:40.", :b-retrospective-evaluator "A verdict keyed to the claim id and a window, over four legs. Measured today: OVERTAKE only. Typed absent: C_mis movement (the U18/U42 readback is keyed to the tick's SELECTED mission, so two ticks selecting different missions have two subjects and no movement; :measured on 1 of 3 recorded 2026-09-02 runs), and RECEIPTS attributable to the hold (:no-mission-to-receipt-carrier; U23 measured flight-discharge as :writer-exists-no-records and clocked-on as recording who clocked on, not what landed). Closed verdict vocabulary :rationale-upheld / :rationale-refuted / :rationale-untestable {:reason}; :rationale-upheld is unreachable on this corpus because it needs an outcome leg.", :c-tension-mint "Only a REFUTED verdict mints, and it mints into U41's record and not a new one: DESIGN-tensions-as-patterns.md section 3 already owns the shape and already names :tension/born-of :refuted-rationale as one of its three sources. This entry adds only the mint edge -- poles derived from the claim's :lost-on term, statement carrying both run-ids, status :carried, resolution-path :none-named-at-mint. The library home is NAMED AND NOT WRITTEN TO: the WM's addressable pattern artifact is a .flexiarg under futon3/library (pattern_registry.clj:48-53, resolved by pattern_registry.clj:158-161), and the birth rule requires two typed receipts and a person."}}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "selection-rule", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :resolved-by-source, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :selection-rule], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "selection-rule", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/selection-rule", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:boundaries "WHICH BOUNDARY CONSULTS WHAT (U10, 2026-09-02). Recorded because 'the rule is argmax' was true of the posterior and false of the choice, and the entry did not say which. THREE SITES, and until U10 the score and the choice were the same expression at none of them. (i) :actuation without a habit prior (policy.clj:809-812): chooses the head of the G-ordered list; the recorded posterior is sigma(-G/tau), consulted by nothing. (ii) :actuation with a habit prior (policy.clj:838): chooses argmax(ln E - G/tau) -- a real argmax of a real score, but F_pi cannot reach this boundary (policy.clj:759-764 throws), so the F_pi term is absent by construction. (iii) :strategic-recommendation, THE ONE THE LIVE PATH TAKES (war_machine.clj:5377-5378): the F_pi-bearing posterior is recorded at policy.clj:668-670 and, under the default law :controller-head, read by nothing -- the choice is the G-ordered head at policy.clj:569,593. U10 adds the second law: under :selection-law :full-score-posterior the chosen action IS the argmax of that same posterior, taken from the same policy/selection-scores vector the posterior normalises (policy.clj:157-213, 563-567, 593), so the score and the choice are one expression rather than two that happen to agree.", :evidence "DETERMINISTIC, AND THE SOFTMAX WEIGHTS ARE NEVER SAMPLED, at every one of the four selection sites: policy.clj:809-812 (:actuation, no habit prior -- the head of the G-ordered list), policy.clj:838 (:actuation with a habit prior -- argmax of ln E - G/tau), policy.clj:593 (:strategic-recommendation -- head under :controller-head, argmax of ln E - G/tau_eff - F_pi under :full-score-posterior) and policy.clj:399-410 (default-mode-select, the try/catch fallback). C5's pointers (policy.clj:247-250, 387-410, 411-438) were re-anchored by U10 on 2026-09-02: 247-250 had drifted onto sorry-pressure-record and 411-438 onto decision-explanation, both of which kept resolving because pointer_check verifies line ranges and not content. No claim of C5's changed; the lines under it did.", :observed :argmax, :realised {:at "2026-09-02", :by "U10 (worklist.edn), SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U10", :default-unchanged "OFF BY DEFAULT. default-selection-law is :controller-head (policy.clj:520-524) and selection-law-of returns it for an unset OR unrecognised FUTON_WM_SELECTION_LAW (war_machine.clj:165-182), which is the same handling tau-mode-of gives. Pinned by selection-score-readiness-test/full-score-law-is-off-by-default-test on a field where the two laws choose differently, so the default is structurally off and not numerically lucky.", :fail-closed "TWO DIFFERENT FAILURES, TWO DIFFERENT ANSWERS. A law asked for when the flag chain can never produce F_pi is a config error and throws at the top of the tick (war_machine/selection-law-preconditions!, war_machine.clj:198-228, called at war_machine.clj:5311-5312 OUTSIDE the default-mode-select try/catch), because every tick would otherwise record a law it never ran. A per-tick coverage decline is NOT that: coverage is complete-or-off by design and 1 of S4's 4 ticks declined, so the selector takes the head it would have taken and records :selection-law :refusal with the envelope's own reason (policy.clj:582-593, 625-637). Throwing there would kill the tick, and -- because select-action is wrapped in a fallback -- kill it silently.", :flip-is-j-gated "NO FLIP IS MADE HERE and no ruling is written. The prediction the flip is to be judged against is stated BEFORE it in SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U10, U1-falsifier style, and the numbers above are the test's own literals, so a field that moves a different rank or a different term fails the suite rather than being read off a run afterwards.", :measured-effect "ON THE THREE COMMITTED TICKS WHERE THE LAW CAN RUN, IT MOVES THE CHOICE ON ALL THREE. Replaying every recorded tick's own components through select-action under both laws (selection-score-readiness-test/chosen-action-attribution-on-the-recorded-fields-test): S4 ticks 0, 2 and 3 choose the rank-130 candidate where :controller-head takes the rank-1 head, with minimal mover set {ln E, F_pi} TOGETHER on each -- the same set the recorded posterior's argmax change attributes to, so posterior and choice now agree about what moved. The other 21 ticks fall back, and the two reasons are kept apart: S2's 20 ticks carry no :f-pi-posterior envelope at all (RUN7 dark carry, :no-f-pi-opts) and S4's remaining tick declines on :incomplete-coverage, 1 uncovered candidate of 145.", :not-reached "THE MODE DOES NOT MAKE THE MACHINE ACT ON THE FULL SCORE, and that is measured, not hedged: on 24 of 24 recorded ticks the action the RECORD carries is not this selector's output at all. war_machine.clj:5438 replaces the controller decision's :action with the mission the R14 strategic selector returned, and that selector is handed three mission-id strings and a trace id (war_machine.clj:5406-5410, the invoke-strategic-selection call) -- no tau, no posterior, no score crosses the call. U3 found this (see :choices :temperature-update :sharper-than-the-headroom); U10 wires the R6 seam and leaves the overwrite untouched, which was outside its acceptance. Pinned by the same test.", :what "policy/selection-laws (policy.clj:503-519) is a closed two-member set; :selection-law reaches select-action as a declared option (policy.clj:749,754) and its two refusals are closed (policy.clj:765-781) and the live path as FUTON_WM_SELECTION_LAW (war_machine.clj:165-196: selection-law-of 165-182, arena-selection-law 184-196). Ties break to the first maximum (policy.clj:525-536) so a tie cannot read as a law change. The decision carries :selection-law {:requested :applied :refusal :controller-head-rank :chosen-rank :moved-from-controller-head?} (policy.clj:625-637), persisted with the decision (trace.clj:167-177) at trace-schema-version 22."}, :source "dacosta2020 eq. 11: u_t = argmax -- the formalism's stated rule is deterministic", :statement "The code conforms to eq. 11. 'Sample' was not a formalism option in the retrieved sources; the earlier 'argmax or sample' wording was the registry author's, not the theory's. WHAT eq. 11 IS AN ARGMAX OF was not recorded until U10: the formalism's argmax is over the policy posterior, and on the boundary the live path takes the code's argmax was over G while the posterior sat beside it unread. :boundaries states which boundary consults what; the second law that closes the gap is off by default.", :status :resolved-by-source}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "survey-mission-epistemic-action", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :survey-mission-epistemic-action], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "survey-mission-epistemic-action", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/survey-mission-epistemic-action", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:measured "Two question kinds, both off carriers that already exist. (a) THE MISSION'S UNANSWERED MAP QUESTIONS: the numbered list under a standalone `MAP must answer:` line, the carrier C492 section 4c named. Measured over the 133 candidates on 2026-09-02: ONE doc carries it (futon0 M-apm-capability-ratchet.md line 260, six questions). Four other primary docs contain `must answer` in constructions that are not a MAP question list; they are recorded as :near-miss-phrasings (survey_mission_value.clj:125-140) with pointers and deliberately NOT matched, and a test feeds each to the parser and fails if it matches (survey_mission_value_test.clj:44-56). No per-question answer carrier exists -- the doc's own `MAP findings` sections number Finding 1..n against no question id -- so every listed question is open with basis :no-per-question-answer-carrier and a doc-line pointer, which is an absence with a pointer rather than an assumption. (b) THE KIN-CATALOG GAP: U23's eleven-carrier cascade record (holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/U23-cascade-catalog/carrier-population.edn), partitioned into five carriers a survey could read and six it could not, each entry carrying U23's own absence reason and corpus count (survey_mission_value.clj:183-233). A carrier the catalog already read is settled and worth 0, so the three missions U23 surveyed score 0 on this half -- including M-zaif-harness-v1, the mission the machine wants, which is the least informative survey target on the catalog half precisely because it has already been surveyed.", :not-ruled "Whether the portfolio proposer is armed by default, and what value survey-eig-weight takes if it is non-zero. Both are worklist :J8. Nothing here changes a recorded number: the row's whole behavioural footprint on the default path is zero.", :dominated-by-information-gain "AN IDENTITY, NOT A MAGNITUDE CLAIM, and the distinction is the entry's point. Because predict-effects ignores :target for this type, all 133 survey candidates on the staged field share ONE :G-core (runs/U24-survey-mission/04-arms.edn: :distinct-G-core 1 against :distinct-survey-eig-nats 7), so every per-target difference between two survey candidates IS the epistemic leg. At the declared 0.02 the leg is 0.152 of a score of 5.302 -- small. Corollary: no weight can reorder two survey candidates; their order is the nats order at every weight, and the weight decides only whether surveying beats advancing. Pinned by survey_mission_value_test.clj:223-242.", :chosen-form "survey-eig(M) = phase-survey-availability(phase(M)) * SUM_q EIG(q), in NATS, and G(survey-mission M) = G-core(survey) - survey-eig-weight * survey-eig(M). The leg is SUBTRACTED because information gain is preference-increasing -- the sign Holes.G := risk - eig gives it -- and it enters the AUGMENTATION layer, not G-core, because :G-core = risk + ambiguity is invariant I3 (efe.clj:93, :757-760, :814-815). Implementation survey_mission_value.clj:288-326 (the term) and :241-276 (the question set). NATS ARE NOT RESCALED, unlike the U22 mission-value term: that term blends with three dimensionless exploit factors so it is normalized into [0,1]; this leg enters G, where G-risk and G-ambiguity are already nats, so the one declared scalar is a pure exchange rate.", :discharge "The row's statement says the discharge of a survey flight is MAP answers as typed observations at mission grain. That shape is written as data at survey_mission_value.clj:392-419, :status :declared-not-implemented, with what blocks it: U23 measured the flight-discharge carrier as :writer-exists-no-records -- the writer is reachable (futon3c flight_record.clj:347) and there are ZERO *.flight.edn files anywhere under ~/code. No flight record is written by U24 and none exists to write against.", :default-off "Twice over, and measured. (i) :survey-mission is not proposable unless portfolio-action-proposer/*portfolio-proposer-active?* is true, which is false by default and is not wired into war_machine.clj at all (portfolio_action_proposer.clj:131-137). (ii) efe/default-survey-eig-weight is 0.0 (efe.clj:93), at which the :survey-eig key is absent from :augmentation-terms altogether and :controller-score is byte-identical: on the staged field 0 of 278 candidates carry the key and the max score delta against unenriched candidates is 0.000e+00 (runs/U24-survey-mission/04-arms.edn :controls :c-default-off). A candidate carrying NO payload is skipped rather than imputed 0.0 nats, so an unmeasured candidate never records a measured-looking zero (efe.clj:757-760; survey_mission_value_test.clj:216-221).", :status :decided, :ruling {:at "2026-09-02", :by "joe", :consequence "Opened zaif-harness S6; half (a) is wm-contract :U23 (the catalog reader, done) and half (b) is :U24 (implemented 2026-09-03). The DEFAULT FLIP -- arming the portfolio proposer, or giving efe/default-survey-eig-weight a non-zero value -- is NOT ruled and is worklist :J8.", :decision "3b: the machine has no ACTION whose value is finding out -- an epistemic action at mission grain, whose G is dominated by information gain over what the mission has not answered. 3c: the catalog of a mission's cascade record is the substrate such an action would read.", :grounds :ruling, :where "futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle-wm-alignment.md, rulings 3b (the epistemic-action hole) and 3c (the catalog design)"}, :declared "Four fiats, three of them U22's REUSED rather than re-declared. (1) An open latent sits at 0.5 and (2) is read perfectly, so it is worth ln 2 nats -- mission_epistemic_value.clj:59-71 fiats (a) and (b), and every question here goes through mission_epistemic_value.clj:207-210 -> epistemic_value.clj:64-90, the canonical kernel with its Bayes-coherence gate. (3) phase-survey-availability, mission_epistemic_value.clj:130-145, unchanged; a test fails if a second copy of that table appears (survey_mission_value_test.clj:127-130). (4) THE ONE NEW FIAT: the partition of U23's eleven carriers into five answerable and six not. It is not a judgement about importance -- it is whether a survey of an uncatalogued mission could return a reading OR a typed zero, which is what makes the latent readable at all -- and the six excluded are excluded and COUNTED rather than paid ln 2 each, the same discipline that kept 266 unresolvable cross-references out of U22's score.", :observed :survey-mission-action-type-with-an-eig-leg-implemented-default-off, :adjacent-finding "A :survey-mission candidate outranks an :advance-mission candidate on DECLARED DETERMINISM, not on information gain, and this row's demonstration is built not to ride on it. All 36 real IDENTIFY-phase candidates on the staged field: the survey option outranks its own recorded advance option with the epistemic leg OFF, 36 of 36. predict-effects :survey declares a variance on :mission-health and none on the other thirteen channels, so those thirteen take the 1e-9 floor (efe.clj:56-59) and its ambiguity term is 7.915207 nats better than :advance-mission's -- exactly one channel's worth of declared variance, and exactly the figure C487 section 5 measured on the :fire-pattern / :advance-mission pair. Under G = risk + ambiguity with lower preferred, an action model that declares it knows what will happen is rewarded for saying so. That is upstream of this row and is the same coverage gap C487 section 6 reached from the C-vector side. Pinned by survey_mission_value_test.clj:302-329; recorded as a finding, not a ruling.", :u4-rerun "The row's acceptance asks for the U4 sweep re-run after the action type exists, as the before/after of whether ambiguity finally discriminates. THE ANSWER IS NO, and the number says how close it came. U4 grain A on the staged field: the EFE-best candidate is unchanged with and without the ambiguity leg on BOTH arms. lambda_break falls from 1.024081 to 1.004631 -- from 2.41 percent of its own size short of flipping the winner to 0.46 percent short -- and the candidate that would overtake changes from :no-op to a survey candidate. C487's C4 positive control (drop RISK instead) fires on both arms, so the zero is a measurement and not a broken detector. The ambiguity term's VALUE SET is unchanged: five distinct values before and after, survey candidates landing at -116.79209997800035, the level :fire-pattern already occupied. The family adds mass at an existing level, not a new level. runs/U24-survey-mission/05-ambiguity-rerun.edn.", :what-existed-before "The action type was declared and empty. predict-effects :survey-mission delegates to :survey (forward_model.clj:180-187), which predicts an EMPTY obs-delta, a variance on one channel, and IGNORES :target; the candidate carried a flat :weight 0.3 (portfolio_action_proposer.clj:72-85); and can-propose? fell through to the :default arm (false), so the machine's only relationship to surveying a mission was a :learn-action-class candidate saying it could not.", :default-ruling {:at "2026-09-03", :by "joe", :channel "J8 walkthrough in session, claude-1 presenting; Joe verbatim: 'j8 stay off (again, for now)'", :decision "Both defaults stay off FOR NOW: the portfolio proposer stays unarmed and default-survey-eig-weight stays 0.0. The accepted grounds: the U4-rerun discipline -- arming the proposer adds ~133 candidates per tick and removes the bootstrap gap candidate, a change that should be introduced as a measured before/after against a baseline corpus of live ticks that does not yet exist. Revisit once the first live-run corpus is on record; the :adjacent-finding (declared-determinism outranking, the C487 coverage gap) should be dispositioned before or with any arming, or the first armed tick will select surveys for the wrong reason.", :grounds :ruling}, :staged-measurement "runs/U24-survey-mission/, produced by u24_survey_mission.clj, byte-identical on two consecutive runs. The field is data/wm-trace/wm-trace-2026-09-02.edn line 2 (run 4abad68c-5481-4402-8f0e-252add62c54b), and two controls establish it IS the recorded field: all 146 recorded candidates reproduce their own :G-risk, :G-ambiguity and :controller-score at max delta 0.000e+00, and policy/select-action reproduces the record's own :decision. Arms: recorded 146 -> :advance-mission M-zaif-harness-v1; survey-dark 278 at weight 0.0 -> the same decision; survey-live 278 at the declared 0.02 -> :survey-mission M-apm-capability-ratchet, the one mission with a listed MAP question set. The break point is SOLVED, not searched: a survey candidate takes rank 1 for any weight above 0.004808."}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 0, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "task-belief-actand-source", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :task-belief-actand-source], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "task-belief-actand-source", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/task-belief-actand-source", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/U52"], :subjects [], :choice {:arms {:A {:grain :arm-session, :note "portfolio pragmatic-value; scalar heuristic over 5 declared channels + mu-sens + adjacent-missions", :site "futon3c/src/futon3c/portfolio/policy.clj:49-74"}, :B {:grain :mission, :note "mission-head pragmatic/epistemic/effort lookups; scalar over 4 declared channels", :site "futon3c/src/futon3c/aif/mission_head.clj:135-176"}, :C {:grain :mission, :note "accreted query over PSR/PUR, discharges, :shown lists, clock lineage; named so the registry records it", :site "S6 cascade-catalog playout (NOT BUILT; futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle-wm-alignment.md:143-189)"}}, :decision-procedure "U11 section 6 replay comparison; DISCRIMINATION headline; baselines named there", :observed :no-actand-source-wired, :provenance "Choice-set registration, NOT a ruling (Joe 2026-09-01 rule). Authored in zaif-harness runs/U11-actand-design-v1.md section 3 (claude-2, joint pass); landed verbatim by claude-1 per the U11 review + wm row U33, 2026-09-03. Mechanical changes only: section-glyph spelled out, indentation. The comparison has since RUN (futon2 runs/U11e-comparison-v1.edn); its numbers enter this entry only with Joe's arm ruling.", :ruling {:at "2026-09-03", :by "joe", :channel "arm-ruling walkthrough in session, claude-1 presenting the comparison (U11e: table 3 distinct values over 114 with provenance; arms A/B 0-produced, every session a typed refusal under honest adapters). Joe verbatim: 'so, case history should win, that's clear... but in the absence of such, a refusal to predict seems slightly overkill. AIF has a notion of anticipating ourselves, and a generative model... let's not throw the baby out with the bathwater here. Firstly, a refusal in our language is a protopattern. The system could push a bit further... try creating a real pattern, cascade, etc... and only if it can't get anywhere then give up'", :consequence "Rung-2 construction is UNBUILT and is the implementation row this ruling opens (zaif lane -- the task-belief machinery is claude-2's; belled 2026-09-03). Rung 3's tension mint rides U41's ledger. The default flip (controller consuming task-belief live) remains separate and J-gated.", :decision "CASE HISTORY WINS: the empirical actand table (the section-5 materialised query over the machine's own recorded sessions) is THE Q_actand source at :arm-session grain. Arms A and B are recorded :too-weak-at-present per the section-6 reversion clause -- 0 values produced over the whole corpus -- and stay in the record with their adapters and refusal counts; arm C remains the named future contender. ZERO-SUPPORT IS A LADDER, NOT A REFUSAL: where a (actand-class, arm) group has no direct precedent (the 9 -inf sessions; any future empty group), the system does NOT flatly refuse. Rung 1: direct case history. Rung 2: CONSTRUCTIVE GENERALIZATION -- anticipate from the generative model: kin actand-classes in the same table, shared patterns, cascade-catalog playout (arm C's machinery when built) -- with the result marked :constructed (never passed off as observed), its derivation recorded, and its provenance pointing at the kin/pattern records it generalized from. Rung 3: only when construction gets nowhere, a TYPED refusal -- and that refusal MINTS A TENSION RECORD through the U41 schema (:tension/born-of :refused-prediction), because a refusal in this house's language is a proto-pattern: the source of the next design iteration, per Joe's 2026-09-02 turn-143 line now operationalized. D8b's finite-number gate stays as the hard floor beneath all three rungs.", :grounds :ruling}, :statement "Three candidate sources for Q_actand; scalar arms A/B are :scalar-awaiting-density (DESIGN-c-vector section 6) until declared as log-density images; no arm is ruled on before the comparison runs.", :status :decided}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 1, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "temperature-update", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :decided, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :temperature-update], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "temperature-update", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/temperature-update", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks ["wm-ticket/C17" "wm-ticket/C18" "wm-ticket/C24" "wm-ticket/C25"], :subjects [], :choice {:evidence "DEFAULT PATH, unchanged: arena-tau-mode war_machine.clj:643-664 returns :selection-gain-only for an unset or unrecognised FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE, its pure parser tau-mode-of at war_machine.clj:627-641; the closed dispatch policy.clj:76-145; selection_gain.clj:173-206 folds realised outcomes, called live at war_machine.clj:4821-4824 (C448 5c.2). VARIATIONAL LAW, realised behind the flag: policy_precision.clj:95-395 (converge-beta, the eq. 2.7 root) and policy_precision.clj:497-561 (carry-beta, the cross-tick beta and its :beta-source); policy.clj:76-145 case :variational-beta-gamma (tau = beta, g and tau_spread both out of the expression); policy.clj:56-74 (temperature-source); war_machine.clj:156-183 (variational-tau-preconditions!, called at war_machine.clj:5035) and war_machine.clj:185-201 (variational-temperature-opts). Persisted: trace.clj:570-581 (:policy-precision-state) and trace.clj:168-178 (the decision, which keeps :tau and :tau-source). Every pointer here re-read at HEAD on 2026-09-01 by C24; the two this field carried before (war_machine.clj:238-248, policy.clj:32-80) had both drifted onto other code and kept resolving, because pointer_check verifies line ranges and not content.", :observed :selection-gain-fold-default-variational-flag-gated, :realised {:at "2026-09-01", :by "I1 slice (b2c), staged and run as RUN8 / stage S3, futon2 5a24194", :default-unchanged "The default is still the selection-gain fold, which is why :observed keeps that name first. arena-tau-mode (war_machine.clj:643-664) returns :selection-gain-only for an unset OR unrecognised FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE, and RUN8's control pre-flight tick -- run8_s3_preflight.clj on the default mode -- recorded tau 1.0, :tau-source :selection-gain-only, and no beta at all (C469-s3-live-tau.md, table at :76-81).", :fallback "A tick whose solve did not both converge and bracket HOLDS the carried beta -- the last solved posterior, or the declared beta_0 on a cold start -- and does NOT cross to the selection-gain law. The hold is upstream in carry-beta (policy_precision.clj:497-561), and policy.clj:76-145 throws rather than reverting to 1/g when no beta reaches it, because a tau series mixing the two laws is uninterpretable. Which law produced each tick's tau is named per tick by temperature-source (policy.clj:56-74) and persisted with the decision (trace.clj:168-178), so a run may not be reported as N ticks of variational tau without the :converged-posterior count beside it. Named in worklist I1 :slice-b2b (2) BEFORE the wiring was written, as RUN8 :acceptance required.", :measured-effect "On the recorded fields the new law moves the recorded numbers and not the choice. Replaying S1, S1b and S2 under both laws (runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt): 0 controller-rank moves, 0 habit-rank moves, 0 habit-argmax moves and 0 softmax-argmax moves, with mean softmax total-variation distance 0.0003573076 on S1. That is structural rather than lucky for the within-group part -- -G/tau is monotone in G for every tau > 0, so within one ln E value the ordering cannot move -- and measured for the rest: the smallest cross-group adjacent margin was +0.7355590795 (ARMS.txt:14-19). The replay control reproduced each record's own selection at its recorded tau at delta 0.0 before any arm was read.", :not-claimed "NOT ADJUDICATED. No number here says the variational law is better than the selection-gain fold; :observed records that both are now in the code, not that the choice is made. The ln E placement the live path takes ships as the interim of :choices :pi-zero-form, which stays :open-branches. And nothing downstream ACTS on tau: RUN8's :consumer-audit found the only readers of the decision's :tau and :softmax-weights either report (full_loop_runner.clj:2570-2577, not reachable from run_tick_once per RUN6) or persist (trace.clj:175-178). That is a fact about today's code, not a guarantee.", :run-evidence "GAMMA MOVES TICK TO TICK ON OUR OWN FIELD, from G and pi -- but say which run measured what, because the two are not the same run. THE 20-TICK SERIES IS DARK: runs/2026-09-01-s2/ (RUN7, FUTON_WM_BETA_DARK=1) carries :policy-precision-state on 20/20 records, all :converged? true, :bracketed? true, :beta-source :converged-posterior, with beta 1.0026460727 -> 1.0343423166 and gamma 0.997360910 -> 0.966797920 from a declared beta_0 = 1.0 (runs/2026-09-01-s2/README.md; the same series reprinted at runs/2026-09-01-s3/ARMS.txt:4,17-36). Nothing consumed it there. LIVE CONSUMPTION WAS MEASURED ON TWO TICKS, not twenty: run8_s3_preflight.clj ran one control tick and one tick under the flag, the latter selecting at tau = beta = 1.0364669814843985 with :tau-source :converged-posterior and gamma 0.9648160702310347. RUN8 deliberately ran no 20-tick S3 stage run and said so (its :reviewer-should-check (6)). So: a 20-tick gamma series exists and a live tau series does not, and no one should read the first as the second.", :what "gamma = 1/beta, with beta the root of friston2017 eq. 2.7 solved on this tick's field, is now REACHABLE ON THE LIVE PATH as FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE=variational-beta-gamma. tau_eff = beta exactly (policy.clj:76-145): the selection gain g and the score-spread calibration tau_spread BOTH leave the expression, so this is a different law and not a third calibration of the same one. This is what the :ruling above said to pursue; what changed is that pursuing it is now a flag rather than a plan."}, :ruling {:at "2026-09-01", :by "joe", :consequence "D4's retirement of R7->R14 stands; no ruling-added edge. Opened H3 (hole: gamma is not the theory's) and I1 (implement beta/gamma dynamics) in worklist.edn.", :decision "The current tau -- from selection gain / score spread -- is a shortcut, and the drawn R7->R14 was a conflation of two precision-like scalars (J1: no). Pursue the theory-aligned policy precision: gamma = 1/beta with beta updated from the policies' expected free energy (friston2017 eq. 2.7, over the gamma prior P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta) of eq. 2.1), so that the machine's decisiveness is the formalism's, not an engineering proxy.", :grounds :ruling, :sources-note "C461 §6 (2026-09-01) corrected two citations claude-1 wrote into the I1 packet: dacosta2020 A.2 supports only gamma's ROLE in selection (sigma(-G) 'can be extended to sigma(-gamma G)', referring to [44] for the update scheme) and is not a source for the beta update; and in eq. 2.7 pi0 = sigma(-gamma . G), the EFE-only distribution (friston2017.txt:684), not the habit prior E. Eq. 2.7's F is the per-policy F_pi (notation table, friston2017.txt:291) -- the same object as parr2022 B.4 -- so the beta update depends on I2's F_pi (J3). Second read (claude-20, 2026-09-01): dropping dacosta2020 A.2 is right, but dropping eq. 2.1 with it over-corrected -- 2.1 is where beta is introduced, as the rate of the gamma prior P(gamma) = Gamma(1, beta) (friston2017.txt:325-336); 2.7 gives the update, 2.1 gives the prior it is over, so both belong. Also note for anyone diffing this file against a generated figure: the :decision string above, stamped :by joe, was AMENDED after Joe ruled -- its citation list was claude-1's summary wording, not Joe's, and the amendment is C13 plus this second read. Joe's ruling itself (J1: no) is unchanged."}, :statement "The mechanism updates tau from realised selection gain (default) or score spread, not by the β/γ precision dynamics. But LIVE: the judge calls fold-realized-outcome every tick (war_machine.clj:4821-4824; the 4332-4361 this line carried until C24 had drifted) and the fold returns the state unchanged unless a well-formed unseen :realized-outcome is present, and that field is absent on today's live path, simulation-only (selection_gain.clj:187-193; C454). So live tau holds at its prior: an update check runs per tick and never fires. 'Fixed-calibrated' described the live behaviour; 'folds realised outcomes' describes the mechanism; both are needed. SINCE 2026-09-01 THAT IS NO LONGER THE WHOLE MECHANISM: a third mode computes tau by the beta/gamma dynamics instead of calibrating a gain, and it is off by default rather than absent. The sentence above still describes what runs when nobody sets the flag.", :status :decided, :theory-alternative "friston2017 eq. 2.7: β = β + (π - π₀)·G, γ = 1/β -- IMPLEMENTED 2026-09-01 and reachable on the live path as FUTON_WM_TAU_MODE=variational-beta-gamma (I1 slice b1 built the solver, futon2 a75f763 + 0fb8b27; I1 (b2c) / RUN8 stage S3 wired it, futon2 5a24194). Still the ALTERNATIVE and not the default, and still not adjudicated against it -- see :realised below.", :u2-retrodiction {:asked "SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U2 named the vehicle for adjudicating the tau arms: score each arm's policy posterior at tick t against the tick's own recorded next observation, across S2/S3/S4, on the ground that the records carry both halves. They do. The vehicle was run. It does not adjudicate, and the reason is measured rather than asserted.", :report "C486-u2-tau-retrodiction.md", :what-would-answer-it "A field in which the channels the action model predicts actually move -- the same precondition as the selection-gain fold's :realized-outcome, which selection_gain.clj:185-193 records as ABSENT today and simulation-only, and the same obstruction RUN4 is blocked on. Length is NOT the missing thing: a 674-tick replay of this apparatus would carry the same 1e-14, and re-running this study longer is explicitly not recommended.", :not-claimed "No ruling. Nothing here says the variational law selects better or worse than the selection-gain fold; it says the vehicle SPEC U2 named cannot answer that on these fields. The recommendation this study carries is only the fallback SPEC U2 itself prescribed for a no-discrimination result: choose by source fidelity.", :script "u2_retrodiction.clj:1-632", :why-the-vehicle-fails "THE COUNTERFACTUAL CONTROL. Re-scoring every arm against the observation the machine had ALREADY SEEN at tick t moves every arm's mean score by 1.701e-04 on S2 -- and the SPREAD of that movement across arms is 1.066e-14, so it changes no arm-against-arm comparison at all. On S4 the movement spread is 3.874e-04, still an order of magnitude larger than the whole :pi-only vs :both separation. THE MECHANISM: F_pi = SUM_ch 1/2 ln(2 pi v_ch) + SUM_ch 1/2 (o_ch - m_ch)^2 / v_ch. The first sum, which depends only on the candidate's declared variances, has a spread across candidates of exactly ln 2 = 0.693147 at every one of the 22 transitions -- 91.9 percent of F_pi's whole 0.754047 spread. The residual sum has spread 0.062500 and mean 0.0032 to 0.0043, and re-computing it against the previous observation moves it by at most 1.107e-03, nearly identically for every candidate. THE REASON: the three channels any candidate's action model predicts (:mission-health, :sorry-count-norm, :ticks-firing-ratio) are constant to 0.000000 across all 20 S2 ticks and all 4 S4 ticks, while the four that move (:loop-health 14 distinct, range 0.0234; :mathematics-pct, :portfolio-pct, :stack-pct 8 distinct each) are predicted by NO candidate and enter every candidate's F_pi at the same 0.01 variance floor. The observation genuinely varies -- 18 of 20 S2 observations are distinct, as C468 reported -- and varies only in coordinates orthogonal to every prediction on the field.", :rule "L_mix(a,t) = ln SUM_i pi_i exp(-F_pi(t+1)_i), the log evidence of the observed next observation under the arm's posterior as mixture weights, reported beside E_F = SUM_i pi_i F_pi(t+1)_i and F_pi(t+1) at the arm's argmax, and bracketed by an ORACLE (all mass on argmin F) and an ANTI-ORACLE (all mass on argmax F) whose gap -- 0.754047 nats on both fields -- is the whole range any score can move in. F_pi is the horizon-one Gaussian observed-data free energy of the tick-t prediction against the tick-(t+1) observation, policy_free_energy.clj:41-151, called live at war_machine.clj:300-305 with :absent-variance :floor.", :fields "S2 (runs/2026-09-01-s2, 20 records, 19 scorable transitions) and S4 (runs/2026-09-01-s4, 4 records, 3 transitions). S3 NOT FOUND and recorded as such: runs/2026-09-01-s3 holds ARMS.txt and README.md only, its README first line saying it is a replay and not a 20-tick stage run, and RUN8's two live ticks are pre-flight ticks that are not a consecutive pair. S3 contributes 0 transitions.", :result-arms "The three arms are not three. :pi-only and :both put ln E in pi identically and differ only through gamma, so they share an argmax on 19 of 19 and 3 of 3 transitions and their L_mix differs by at most 2.083e-04 (S2) and 3.932e-05 (S4) -- 0.03 percent and 0.005 percent of the range. The separation that exists is :none against the other two (max |dL_mix| 2.785e-03, a different argmax on 22 of 22), which is the question of whether ln E enters pi AT ALL -- U3's question, which both sources answer yes -- and not the pi_0 placement question.", :controls "Four, all run before any arm was read. (1) SOLVER: the local :none arm reproduces src converge-beta at delta 0.00e+00 on both fields. (2) ALIGNMENT: 19 of 19 and 3 of 3 transitions have the t+1 record's :previous-trace-timestamp equal to tick t's :timestamp, so no posterior is scored against an outcome that is not its own. (3) BRACKET: 0 arm-tick scores fall outside [anti-oracle, oracle]. (4) REPRODUCTION: recomputing F_pi(t+1) from tick t's :ranked-actions and tick t+1's observation reproduces the RECORDED value at max delta 0.000e+00 over 145 candidates x 19 transitions, so this is a reading of the run's own score and not a second implementation of it.", :at "2026-09-02", :by "claude-cli", :artifact "U2-RETRODICTION.txt", :typed-outcome :no-discrimination-score-is-outcome-independent, :result-tau-law "NOT ADJUDICATED, and this study cannot adjudicate it. The variational arms' posteriors do retrodict better than the default law's -- softmax(-G/tau) at the record's own tau 1.0, :tau-source :selection-gain-only -- at 22 of 22 transitions (mean L_mix 19.185921 to 19.188693 against 19.179171 on S2). But a UNIFORM posterior scores 19.188231, beating two of the three arms and the default law both; and on S4 uniform beats every arm including the best. A law that loses to uniform is not shown better by that comparison, and a ranking that flips between the two fields of the same machine is not a ranking. What does survive as a fact about the machine: the default law's top candidate has a worse-than-field-average F_pi at 22 of 22 transitions (F@top -19.150441 against a field mean -19.1832), and under the decomposition below that is predominantly a statement about that candidate's declared variances.", :row :U2}}, :reviewer nil, :dependency-counts {:ancestors 0, :downstream 5, :incomplete? false, :unfinished-ancestor-ids [], :unfinished-ancestors 0}, :owner "joe", :tetrahedron {:bucket :organization, :status :proposed}, :blocked-by []} {:description "tensions-cashed-reading", :tags [{:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-01", :basis-count 1, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :adopted-by-machine, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:1", :selector [:choices :tensions-cashed-reading], :sha256 "a6d551bb9bfbc4ca451f3071710e3490926c369266ccccfe5bb4e87c80d3c09d"}], :blockage nil, :next-action nil, :lane nil, :acceptance nil, :title "tensions-cashed-reading", :column :done, :id "wm-choice/tensions-cashed-reading", :kind :choice, :decision-owner "joe", :component-context {:component "Assignment needed", :loops ["Unclassified"], :status :unassigned}, :blocks [], :subjects [], :choice {:measured "THE SIX-SCENARIO FOLD TABLE (holes/labs/wm-contract/u56_fold_consequences.bb, computed by applying run_era_ledger.bb:432-451's own fold rule to the ledger's rows with verdicts substituted IN MEMORY; no row was written). This adoption is scenario S1a. WHAT DECIDED IT AGAINST (B): S1b -- (A) read as a typed absence -- reproduces the deposited ledger EXACTLY, and (B) is the one reading under which re5's deposited row would have been green, so (B) is the reading inconsistent with deposits already made. WHAT THE ADOPTION COSTS, stated because it is a cost: under S1a re5 moves :incomplete -> :red and s5's existing :red gains a second cause, so the reading that best matches the check's name is the one that makes the fold worse. NO READING GREENS ANY RUN (only S5 does, and that takes all four standing absences), so settling this unblocks nothing -- which is why it could be settled on the evidence rather than escalated. WHY (B) IS NOT MERELY LOOSE BUT WRONG-DIRECTED, measured under :U60/:U63: the ladder's producer now mints :tension/provenance {:records [run-id]}, and on the curated ledger the u60 tension declares run 2026-09-05-u60 structurally -- so (B) greens that run for a tension that is uncashed and SAYS it is about that run, which is the case (A) exists to catch. The disagreement set between the two readings is 3 runs on the curated ledger and 5 on the planted one, named in full by negative control 8t.", :statement "THREE READINGS OF ONE CHECK-ID, all implementable, enumerated at C511-repair-or-elaborate.md:426-446. (A) the run's tensions are all cashed -- what the check-id says. (B) the ledger can attribute a tension to this run -- what the code tested until this adoption: the run id or one of its tick ids appearing anywhere in the ledger TEXT, so a run was green for being MENTIONED. (C) the run minted no tension, vacuously satisfied. (A) is adopted, and adopted STRICT: not-all-cashed is a :red rather than the :typed-absence C511 folded as its alternative, because the ledger can see the uncashed tension -- the absence would be a claim that cashing is unobservable, and it is observable, it just has never happened.", :evidence "holes/labs/wm-contract/u41_tension_ledger.bb (:verdict-deposited, and run-attribution's :reading/:uncashed/:status-fold); C511-repair-or-elaborate.md:418-497; holes/labs/wm-contract/u56_fold_consequences.bb:111-167; holes/labs/wm-contract/tension-ledger.edn; p4ng/empirics-futon/negative_controls.sh (8t, 8z)", :reversal "re-record the choice: replace this entry's :adoption with the reading adopted instead, and move u41_tension_ledger.bb's :verdict-deposited back onto the condition that reading names. Nothing else depends on it -- no deposited row was rewritten, no schema field was added, and the run-era fold of the three deposited runs is byte-identical before and after.", :controls "p4ng/empirics-futon/negative_controls.sh 8t (the shipped verdict per run, the named (A)-strict/(B) disagreement set on two ledgers, and the deposited rows unmoved) and 8z (the discrimination: two plants differing by ONE schema-conforming :cashed event, :red without it and :green with it, both validating with 0 defects so neither verdict is a broken tree). In u41 itself, :positive/a-planted-cashing-makes-the-attributed-set-all-cashed and :negative/without-the-cashing-the-same-attribution-stays-uncashed pin the input the verdict reads; the verdict is NOT recomputed inside `controls`, because `deposit-receipt` reds on any failing control and a verdict computed there would be either circular or a second copy of the rule it guards.", :adoption {:at "2026-09-05", :by :claude-wm-edge, :consequence "u41_tension_ledger.bb's :verdict-deposited reads :run-provenance :run-attribution :naming-this-run and its :cashed? field instead of the two substring conditions. On the current ledger 2026-09-01-s5, 2026-09-04-re5 and 2026-09-05-u60 replay :red where reading (B) as coded gave :green; 2026-09-04-010-accepted, 2026-09-05-u5