ior imports tau, which gamma would define. That is a within-tick fixed point, and friston2017 says so explicitly: 'usually one would iterate the equalities in equation 2.7 until convergence' (friston2017.txt:683-685). Two ways to build it, and they compute different things. (i) ITERATE WITHIN THE TICK, as the paper states: solve pi and gamma together to convergence each tick. Faithful; costs a loop inside the tick and needs a convergence rule and a bound the WM does not have today. (ii) CARRY BETA ACROSS TICKS, the way :selection-gain is already read from the previous trace record and written back (war_machine.clj:4332-4361, 4773-4776) -- codex-21's recommendation in C461 section 3. No fixed point, no iteration, one tick of lag: the tick's decisiveness is set by the previous tick's evidence rather than this one's. Cheap, already-proven persistence shape, and a declared departure from the paper's stated solution. This is a ruling because it changes what the machine computes, not how it is coded. ", :tags [{:basis {:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:1", :selector [:items :J4 :class], :sha256 "f0f6aedbde868fe2edaafd6a26441b0c86452f05303bbd3be0f169c05e71386d"}, :relation :work-class, :value "J"} {:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-08", :basis-count 2, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :done, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:1", :selector [:items :J4], :sha256 "f0f6aedbde868fe2edaafd6a26441b0c86452f05303bbd3be0f169c05e71386d"} {:as-of "2026-09-08", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/variable-situation-accounting.edn", :point