reading exactly 0), refuses the rest :no-declared-threshold, and with a threshold declared scores 14/14 and reads 0.75 as unmet or met depending on where the threshold is put. (3) :typed-binary-only -- refuse on spec/observable mismatch, == for genuinely binary observables; scores 0/14 because no criterion declares an observable kind, and 4/14 once one does. Under all three, nil is a typed absence rather than a satisfied criterion, which is C130 discipline and not one of the branches. Arms 2 and 3 are indistinguishable at the composition on this corpus and part company only where a declaration exists. THE QUESTION: should a criterion whose observable carries no declaration be SCORED on the type fix alone, or REFUSED until someone writes the declaration down? Scoring gives the mission-grain C numbers on every tick at the price of calling most readings satisfied; refusing gives it a typed absence on nearly every tick until the mission documents are amended, which is work on nine criteria across two missions and everything written later. NOT PART OF THIS QUESTION, because U16 measured them settled: clause (b) is unchanged by every arm (risk_mis is one number copied to every mission action, so an outcome reading cannot make it vary -- U13's forward model is what would), and the clause (c) zero is unreachable under every arm because 4.5399e-5 is the T=0.1 temperature floor. ", :tags [{:basis {:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-stale? false, :emitted-at nil, :path "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn", :pointer "futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/worklist.edn:1", :selector [:items :J6 :class], :sha256 "f0f6aedbde868fe2edaafd6a26441b0c86452f05303bbd3be0f169c05e71386d"}, :relation :work-class, :value "J"} {:relation :unmapped, :value "R-node-unmapped"}], :freshness {:as-of "2026-09-08", :basis-count 2, :oldest-basis-as-of "2026-09-01", :state :dated-not-revalidated, :unknown-source-dates? false}, :source-status :done, :conflicts [], :basis [{:as-of "2026-09-01", :authority-s